{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_72","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'class Game|advance\\\\(dt|headless =|advance\\\\(seconds|class Humanoid|class Audio' 'Wee Bit of Zen-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221356/engine/my-3d2dge.js' | head -30; sed -n '300,345p' PLAN.md; sed -n '80,150p' TASK.md; sed -n '1,100p' 'Wee Bit of Zen-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221356/src/style.css'; sed -n '195,295p' 'Wee Bit of Zen-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221356/vendor/session.js'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_72","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'class Game|advance\\\\(dt|headless =|advance\\\\(seconds|class Humanoid|class Audio' 'Wee Bit of Zen-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221356/engine/my-3d2dge.js' | head -30; sed -n '300,345p' PLAN.md; sed -n '80,150p' TASK.md; sed -n '1,100p' 'Wee Bit of Zen-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221356/src/style.css'; sed -n '195,295p' 'Wee Bit of Zen-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221356/vendor/session.js'\"","aggregated_output":"2308:class Game {\n2338:    this.headless = !!o.headless || typeof document === 'undefined';\n2842:  advance(seconds = this.o.step, o = {}) {\n4052:class Humanoid {\n\n---\n\n## 9. Animation recipes (all ✔)\n\nRigs are `E.Humanoid` (`weapon: null`). Player and Regulars `chibi`; instructors `build: 'heroic', limbW: 1.5, torsoW: 2.5, hair: 'bald'` (Alder `'ponytail'`) with every colour key in wood tones. Their ball joints: after `rig.draw`, in the same `r.actor`, for `kneeL kneeR elbowL elbowR shL shR`: `const w = rig.worldOffset(rig.J[k]), p = (rig.lastView || r.view).p(w[0], w[1], w[2]);` then `px.disc` radius 3 and radius 2 in two wood tones at `(ox + p[0], oy + p[1])`.\n\n**Real motion capture, including actual yoga, plays on these rigs.** Cut the small set in section 15. Then:\n\n```js\nconst lib = Mocap.load(window.MOCAP.FITCLIPS);\nfunction makeRig(opts) {\n  const rig = new E.Humanoid(Object.assign({ weapon: null }, opts));\n  Mocap.drive(rig, lib);              // first\n  const base = rig.solvePose;         // then our layer: a hand-posed body, then the wobble\n  rig.wob = [0, 0]; rig.body = null;\n  rig.solvePose = function () {\n    base.call(this);\n    if (this.body) setBody(this, this.body(this));\n    const [ax, ay] = this.wob; if (!ax && !ay) return;\n    const J = this.J, a = ax * .45, b = ay * .3, ca = Math.cos(a), sa = Math.sin(a), cb = Math.cos(b), sb = Math.sin(b);\n    for (const k in J) { if (k === 'bladeDir' || !J[k]) continue; const p = J[k];   // turn every joint about the feet\n      const r2 = p[1] * ca + p[2] * sa, z2 = -p[1] * sa + p[2] * ca, f2 = p[0] * cb + z2 * sb, z3 = -p[0] * sb + z2 * cb;\n      p[0] = f2; p[1] = r2; p[2] = Math.max(z3, 0); }\n  };\n  return rig;\n}\n// each step. A clip turns the rig by its own heading, so aim with tgt minus that turn:\nrig.wob = [p.x, p.y];  rig.mocap = lib.sample(clip, t);   // rig.mocap = null to stop\nrig.update(dt, { x, y, z: 0, vx: 0, vy: 0, facing: tgt - (rig.spin || 0) });\n```\n\nFacing: π/2 looks at the camera; 0 is profile. **To hold a pose,** sample inside its window and drift slowly: `t = a + (b - a) * .3 * (.5 + .5 * Math.sin(time * .7))`. Clip motion keeps it alive.\n\n**Pose table** (windows ✔ seen on contact sheets; stork, triangle and dog ✔ seen in the studio):\n\n| Pose | Clip | Window (s) | `tgt` |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Stork (one leg, arms wide) | `111_39_part1` | 3.6 to 7.0 | 1.57 |\n| Knee Lift | `111_39_part2` | .5 to 2.4 | 1.57 |\n| Triangle | `111_39_part3` | 2.2 to 5.2 | 1.2 |\n| Warrior (wide stance, arms wide) | `111_39_part3` | 6.6 to 7.6 | 1.57 |\n| Low Lunge | `111_38_part1` | 2.9 to 5.0 | .25 |\n| Down Dog | `111_38_part2` | 2.8 to 5.2 | .25 |\n| Forward Fold | `111_38_part2` | 8.0 to 8.8 | .25 |\n| Low Plank | `111_41_part3` | 3.4 to 6.4 | .25 |\nNarrative tone: Use a writing style similar to the source’s.\n\n## UI & UX: 10-Foot Controller-First Philosophy\nDesign the game around a PS5 DualSense (or any pad the browser reports in its standard mapping) played on a TV at 10 feet. With keyboard and mouse it's the same game on the same screens, not a separate desktop layout, but they should feel native, not like stand-ins for controller buttons. The keyboard uses the keys PC players expect for the genre. The mouse aims, looks, and clicks menu items and things in the world (hover moves the focus) wherever the genre uses it. On-screen prompts follow the input used last: PlayStation glyphs for the controller (with a Settings option to show Xbox glyphs, A B X Y, instead), keys and mouse buttons for keyboard and mouse.\n\nDo not use overly dense, web-style data screens.\n\nTouch-only devices: no touch controls; show \"Controller or keyboard required\" and the settings button. Let the attract mode run.\n\n## Done\nNo TODOs, placeholders, or stubbed features. The demo is complete.\n\n## Source Information\nCRITICAL: Put Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback in your chat reply and an in-game About/Credits screen. Write \"unknown\" for anything you can't confirm.\n- Date: 2026-11-04 22:13:56\n- Source: the work it's based on\n- Plan: the file name of the plan you were given to build from, or none\n- Genre and Perspective: genre and camera perspective used\n- Tech: stack, libraries/engines, with versions if applicable\n- Art Direction: style used\n- Animation: system used\n- Audio: music, sound effects and voice used\n- Online: network features used, or none\n- Testing: testing parameters allowed\n- Research: research done, or none\n- Environment: Codex CLI (headless); Linux\n- Model: OpenAI, gpt-6.1-terra, reasoning effort max\n- Usage: write \"added on import\". You can't see your own cost, so don't estimate it: the runner records the real cost, tokens and time, and the agent that imports the game into AI Hub puts them on your About/Credits screen.\n\nExit interview: before you finish, also save these answers as exit-interview.json in this folder's root, beside the game's .html: one JSON object in exactly the shape below, every value filled in (\"unknown\" for anything you can't confirm). Tools read it (the game's run record and the AI Hub catalogue), so write plain text, and check that the file parses as JSON.\n{\n  \"sourceInformation\": {\"date\": \"\", \"source\": \"\", \"plan\": \"\", \"genre\": \"\", \"perspective\": \"\", \"tech\": \"\", \"artDirection\": \"\", \"animation\": \"\", \"audio\": \"\", \"online\": \"\", \"testing\": \"\", \"research\": \"\", \"environment\": \"\", \"model\": \"\", \"usage\": \"added on import\"},\n  \"testingFeedback\": [\"your answer to each Testing Feedback question, in order\"],\n  \"engineFeedback\": [\"your answer to each Engine Feedback question, in order\"],\n  \"promptFeedback\": [\"your answer to each Prompt Feedback question, in order\"],\n  \"aiHub\": {\n    \"name\": \"the game's title, as on its title screen\",\n    \"tagline\": \"a few words to go under the title\",\n    \"description\": \"one or two sentences for the catalogue\",\n    \"type\": \"Game, Tech demo or Tool\",\n    \"genre\": \"one of Action, Adventure, Fighting, Flight, Horror, Kids & Learning, Life Sim, Platformer, Puzzle, Racing, RPG, Shooter, Simulation, Sports, Stealth, Strategy\",\n    \"source\": \"the work it's based on, e.g. Moby-Dick\",\n    \"series\": \"its franchise, e.g. Star Fox, or empty\",\n    \"players\": \"how many can play: 1, 1–2 or 1–4\",\n    \"controls\": \"the controls, in one line\",\n    \"tags\": [\"3 to 6 lowercase tags, e.g. 2d, 3d, arcade, story, co-op, versus, first-person, third-person, top-down, side-scrolling, pixel art, low-poly, retro, sci-fi, fantasy, comedy, vehicles, boss fights, exploration\"]\n  }\n}\nThe catalogue's model, effort, CLI, date and usage come from the run's record after you finish, so they aren't asked here.\n\nTesting Feedback\n\n- How many issues did testing catch?\n- How many would be considered critical issues / game breaking?\n- What was the most helpful test you ran?\n- What was the least helpful test you ran?\n\nEngine Feedback\n\n- What did you like most about the engine?\n- Did you get stuck or guess wrong?\n- What was the most important thing you had to build yourself?\n- What was the hardest part about using the engine?\n- What did you change in the engine, and why? (none if nothing)\n- If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be?\n\nPrompt Feedback\n\n- What did you like most about this prompt?\n- What was confusing?\n- What was the hardest thing to do?\n:root{color-scheme:light;--ink:#263d42;--muted:#708485;--teal:#248e8b;--line:#d9e9e2;--paper:#fffefa;--sun:#f8cc76;--shadow:0 18px 50px rgba(41,78,72,.12)}\n*{box-sizing:border-box}html,body{width:100%;height:100%;margin:0;overflow:hidden}body{font-family:ui-rounded,\"Avenir Next\",Avenir,\"Trebuchet MS\",sans-serif;background:#e9f4ed;color:var(--ink);-webkit-font-smoothing:antialiased}button,input,select{font:inherit}button{color:inherit;cursor:pointer}button:focus-visible,input:focus-visible,select:focus-visible{outline:4px solid #f3bb5d;outline-offset:3px}#world{position:fixed;inset:0;width:100%;height:100%;display:block}#app{position:fixed;inset:0;overflow:auto;scrollbar-width:thin}#app:empty{pointer-events:none}.page{min-height:100%;padding:clamp(20px,4vw,64px);display:flex;flex-direction:column;position:relative}.topbar{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:15px;z-index:2}.brand{font-weight:900;letter-spacing:.15em;text-transform:uppercase;font-size:clamp(10px,.9vw,13px);display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px}.brand-mark{display:grid;place-items:center;background:var(--teal);color:white;border-radius:50%;width:30px;height:30px;font-size:17px;letter-spacing:0}.top-actions{display:flex;gap:8px}.icon-btn,.small-btn{border:1px solid rgba(72,116,105,.18);background:rgba(255,255,250,.83);border-radius:999px;box-shadow:0 4px 12px rgba(42,72,64,.05);font-weight:800;padding:11px 17px}.icon-btn:hover,.small-btn:hover{background:#fff;transform:translateY(-2px)}.hero{flex:1;display:flex;align-items:center;min-height:0}.hero-copy{width:min(50%,620px);padding:28px 0 54px}.eyebrow{font-size:12px;font-weight:900;letter-spacing:.19em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#5b9186}.eyebrow:before{content:'';display:inline-block;width:25px;height:2px;background:#8fb9a5;vertical-align:middle;margin-right:10px}.logo{font-size:clamp(50px,7.5vw,108px);letter-spacing:-.075em;line-height:.88;margin:20px 0 22px;font-weight:900;color:#244944}.logo span{color:#49a99d}.lede{font-size:clamp(17px,1.6vw,23px);line-height:1.45;max-width:470px;color:#58716e;margin:0 0 28px}.menu-stack{display:grid;gap:10px;width:min(100%,370px)}.action{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;text-align:left;border:1px solid rgba(61,119,103,.11);background:rgba(255,255,250,.92);border-radius:18px;padding:16px 19px;box-shadow:0 6px 20px rgba(50,95,80,.06);font-weight:850;font-size:17px;transition:transform .15s,box-shadow .15s,background .15s}.action:hover,.action.is-focused{transform:translateX(6px);box-shadow:0 8px 24px rgba(46,112,98,.15);background:#fff}.action.primary{background:#2b9991;color:white;border-color:#2b9991}.action .arrow{font-size:19px;opacity:.75}.footer{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:15px;align-items:center;font-size:11px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.11em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#76918a;z-index:2}.footer strong{color:#44655e}.footer .hint{letter-spacing:.02em;text-transform:none}.main-wrap{flex:1;width:100%;max-width:1160px;margin:0 auto;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;padding:28px 0}.card{width:min(100%,760px);background:rgba(255,255,251,.96);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.9);box-shadow:var(--shadow);border-radius:30px;padding:clamp(24px,4vw,50px);position:relative}.card.wide{width:min(100%,1060px)}.card.narrow{width:min(100%,560px)}.card h1,.card h2{letter-spacing:-.045em;line-height:1.05;margin:10px 0 12px}.card h1{font-size:clamp(32px,4.3vw,53px)}.card h2{font-size:clamp(25px,3vw,36px)}.card p{line-height:1.5;color:#667c79;font-size:17px}.card .action{background:#f4f8f4;box-shadow:none}.card .action.primary{background:#2b9991;color:white}.card .action:hover,.card .action.is-focused{background:#e7f3ed}.card .action.primary:hover,.card .action.primary.is-focused{background:#218b83}.card-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:12px}.activity-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:12px}.activity{border:1px solid #e4eee7;background:#f8fbf7;border-radius:19px;padding:15px;text-align:left;min-height:114px;position:relative}.activity:hover,.activity.is-focused{background:#edf8f1;border-color:#8ec9b3;transform:translateY(-2px)}.activity:disabled{opacity:.5;cursor:not-allowed}.activity-icon{display:grid;place-items:center;float:left;width:42px;height:42px;border-radius:13px;background:var(--tint,#e2f2e9);font-size:23px;margin-right:12px}.activity strong{display:block;font-size:16px}.activity small{display:block;color:#83948e;margin-top:5px}.activity .stars{color:#e4ad4f;font-size:13px;margin-top:8px}.chip{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:7px;border-radius:99px;background:#edf6ef;color:#56836f;font-size:11px;font-weight:900;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.12em;padding:9px 12px}.chip.orange{background:#fff1d5;color:#ae7e31}.chip.pink{background:#fce9df;color:#b77e6e}.split{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:25px;align-items:center}.row{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:16px}.divider{height:1px;background:#e7efe9;margin:19px 0}.field{display:grid;gap:8px;margin:16px 0;color:#748c83;font-weight:800;font-size:12px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.12em}.field input,.field select{width:100%;border:2px solid #e3eee6;border-radius:14px;padding:13px 15px;color:var(--ink);background:#fbfdf9;font-size:17px;letter-spacing:0;text-transform:none}.options{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px}.option{border:2px solid #e6eee6;border-radius:13px;padding:10px 14px;background:#f8fbf8;font-weight:800}.option.selected{border-color:#63b2a0;background:#e7f7ec}.dialogue{background:#eef8f2;border-radius:20px;padding:18px 20px;color:#42665c;font-size:18px;line-height:1.45}.dialogue strong{color:#278f82}.actions{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:10px;margin-top:22px}.actions .action{min-width:160px}.play-hud{position:absolute;inset:0;pointer-events:none;padding:clamp(18px,3vw,40px);display:flex;flex-direction:column;justify-content:space-between}.play-hud button{pointer-events:auto}.hud-top,.hud-bottom{display:flex;align-items:flex-start;justify-content:space-between;gap:12px}.hud-box{background:rgba(255,255,250,.92);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.8);border-radius:20px;padding:14px 20px;box-shadow:0 9px 28px rgba(44,83,75,.09)}.hud-box strong{font-size:20px;letter-spacing:-.03em}.hud-box small{display:block;font-size:11px;color:#79938a;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.12em;font-weight:900;margin-bottom:3px}.meter{height:9px;width:180px;border-radius:20px;background:#e5efe6;overflow:hidden;margin-top:8px}.meter>i{display:block;height:100%;background:#efba68;border-radius:20px}.play-instruction{text-align:center;align-self:center;background:rgba(255,255,250,.91);border-radius:999px;padding:12px 20px;font-weight:800;color:#57776c;box-shadow:var(--shadow)}.progress-dots{display:flex;gap:6px}.progress-dots i{width:9px;height:9px;border-radius:50%;background:#dcebe2}.progress-dots i.on{background:#4cae9c}.score-big{font-size:clamp(48px,7vw,76px);font-weight:900;letter-spacing:-.07em;color:#2b9991;line-height:1}.stars-big{font-size:30px;color:#efb956;letter-spacing:5px}.note{font-size:13px!important;color:#91a39b!important}.scroll{max-height:min(57vh,570px);overflow:auto;padding-right:8px}.about-group{border-top:1px solid #e7efe9;padding:12px 0}.about-group h3{font-size:18px}.about-group p{font-size:14px;margin:5px 0;overflow-wrap:anywhere}.touch-notice{position:fixed;inset:0;z-index:20;display:grid;place-items:center;padding:20px;background:rgba(230,244,236,.92);text-align:center}.touch-notice .card{width:min(100%,460px)}.hidden{display:none!important}.toast{position:fixed;bottom:25px;left:50%;transform:translateX(-50%);background:#284e49;color:#fff;border-radius:99px;padding:12px 22px;z-index:10;font-weight:800}.class-players{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:10px}.player-tile{padding:18px;background:#f2f8f1;border-radius:18px;text-align:center}.player-tile .face{font-size:35px}.slider{width:100%;accent-color:#38a597}.island-message{position:absolute;top:12%;left:50%;transform:translateX(-50%);text-align:center;white-space:nowrap;pointer-events:none}.island-message h1{font-size:clamp(24px,3.2vw,40px);margin:6px;letter-spacing:-.04em}.island-message p{margin:0;color:#708e82;font-weight:700}.map-actions{position:absolute;bottom:clamp(20px,4vh,45px);left:50%;transform:translateX(-50%);width:min(92%,760px);display:flex;justify-content:center;gap:10px}.map-actions .action{min-width:180px}.map-actions button{pointer-events:auto}.center-copy{text-align:center}.center-copy p{max-width:580px;margin-left:auto;margin-right:auto}\n@media(max-width:850px){.hero-copy{width:58%}.logo{font-size:clamp(48px,8vw,72px)}.activity-grid{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr))}.footer .weather{display:none}.card{padding:26px}.main-wrap{align-items:flex-start;padding:25px 0}.page{min-height:100%;padding:22px}.play-hud{padding:16px}.island-message{top:12%}}\n@media(max-width:540px){.page{padding:18px}.hero{align-items:flex-end}.hero-copy{width:100%;padding:30px 0 20px}.logo{font-size:58px;max-width:320px;margin:12px 0}.lede{font-size:16px;max-width:315px;margin-bottom:18px}.menu-stack{width:100%;max-width:340px}.action{padding:13px 16px;font-size:15px;border-radius:15px}.brand{font-size:10px}.footer{font-size:9px}.card-grid,.split{grid-template-columns:1fr}.activity-grid{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:7px}.activity{padding:10px;min-height:92px}.activity-icon{width:34px;height:34px;font-size:18px}.activity strong{font-size:13px}.activity small{font-size:11px}.card h1{font-size:34px}.card p{font-size:15px}.hud-box{padding:10px 12px}.hud-box strong{font-size:16px}.meter{width:110px}.play-instruction{font-size:12px;max-width:90%;padding:10px 14px}.class-players{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr)}.map-actions .action{min-width:0;flex:1}.map-actions{width:90%}.scroll{max-height:55vh}}\n    } catch (e) {\n      return undefined;\n    }\n  }\n\n  function post(type, fields) {\n    var msg = { aihub: 1, type: type };\n    for (var key in fields) if (own(fields, key)) msg[key] = fields[key];\n    try {\n      root.parent.postMessage(msg, origin);\n    } catch (e) {\n      warn('could not reach the hub: ' + e.message);\n    }\n  }\n\n  function emit(type, args) {\n    var list = handlers[type];\n    if (!list || !list.length || pending[type]) {\n      (pending[type] = pending[type] || []).push(args);\n      return;\n    }\n    for (var i = 0; i < list.length; i++) {\n      try {\n        list[i].apply(null, args);\n      } catch (e) {\n        setTimeout(function () {\n          throw e;\n        });\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  function onMessage(event) {\n    if (event.source !== root.parent) return;\n    var m = event.data;\n    if (!m || m.aihub !== 1 || typeof m.type !== 'string') return;\n    if (m.type === 'welcome') {\n      if (welcomed) return;\n      welcomed = true;\n      origin = event.origin && event.origin !== 'null' ? event.origin : '*';\n      // Every field the hub sends is kept, so a newer hub can add one without a newer client.\n      for (var key in m) {\n        if (!own(m, key) || KEEP[key] || typeof hub[key] === 'function') continue;\n        hub[key] = m[key];\n      }\n      hub.players = (m.players || []).slice();\n      hub.seed = m.seed >>> 0;\n      hub.isHost = m.me === m.host;\n      hub.splash = m.splash === true;\n      if (m.limits) {\n        for (var l in limits) if (own(limits, l) && Number(m.limits[l]) > 0) limits[l] = Number(m.limits[l]);\n        tokens = limits.burst;\n      }\n      if (connecting) connecting.resolve(info());\n      return;\n    }\n    if (m.type === 'fullscreen') {\n      fullscreenOn = m.on === true;\n      try {\n        root.document.dispatchEvent(new root.Event('fullscreenchange'));\n      } catch (e) {}\n      return;\n    }\n    if (!welcomed || ended) return;\n    if (m.type === 'start') {\n      goAt = now() + Number(m.in || 0);\n      emit('start', [{ in: Number(m.in || 0) }]);\n    } else if (m.type === 'message') {\n      emit('message', [m.data, m.from]);\n    } else if (m.type === 'leave') {\n      hub.players = hub.players.filter(function (p) {\n        return p.id !== m.id;\n      });\n      emit('leave', [{ id: m.id, reason: m.reason }]);\n    } else if (m.type === 'time-up') {\n      emit('time-up', [{ graceMs: m.graceMs }]);\n    } else if (m.type === 'end') {\n      ended = true;\n      if (progressTimer) clearTimeout(progressTimer);\n      emit('end', [{ reason: m.reason, standings: m.standings || null }]);\n    } else {\n      // An event this client has never heard of: hand it on as it came.\n      var detail = {};\n      for (var k in m) if (own(m, k) && k !== 'aihub' && k !== 'type') detail[k] = m[k];\n      emit(m.type, [detail]);\n    }\n  }\n\n  function info() {\n    var out = {};\n    for (var key in hub) if (own(hub, key) && typeof hub[key] !== 'function' && !KEEP[key]) out[key] = hub[key];\n    out.players = hub.players.slice();\n    return out;\n  }\n\n  /** Join the session. Resolves with the round's info, or null when there is no hub: play normally. */\n  hub.connect = function (opts) {\n    if (connecting) return connecting.promise;\n    var done;\n    var promise = new Promise(function (resolve) {\n      done = resolve;\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
