{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_114","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"D='Wee Bit of Zen-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221356'; rg -n '\"'^(const|let|function|if '\"\\\\(state\\\\.hub|window\\\\.__ZEN|  window\\\\.AIHub)' \\\"\"'$D/src/game.js\"; rg -n '\"'schema|sourceInformation|testingFeedback|engineFeedback|promptFeedback|aiHub|exit.interview' TASK.md; ls \\\"\"'$D/engine\"/*.js; head -c 800 \"$D/vendor/fitclips.js\"; printf '\"'\\\\n--- session instructions from plan ---\\\\n'; rg -n 'Hub|hub|session|mocap|Animation|scripted|Festival|body check' PLAN.md | head -50\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_114","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"D='Wee Bit of Zen-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221356'; rg -n '\"'^(const|let|function|if '\"\\\\(state\\\\.hub|window\\\\.__ZEN|  window\\\\.AIHub)' \\\"\"'$D/src/game.js\"; rg -n '\"'schema|sourceInformation|testingFeedback|engineFeedback|promptFeedback|aiHub|exit.interview' TASK.md; ls \\\"\"'$D/engine\"/*.js; head -c 800 \"$D/vendor/fitclips.js\"; printf '\"'\\\\n--- session instructions from plan ---\\\\n'; rg -n 'Hub|hub|session|mocap|Animation|scripted|Festival|body check' PLAN.md | head -50\"","aggregated_output":"3:const app = document.getElementById('app');\n4:const STORAGE = 'wee-bit-of-zen-v1';\n5:const DEFAULT_SETTINGS = { music: 10, sound: 10, voice: true, gentle: false, breathToggle: false, tips: true, glyphs: 'PlayStation' };\n6:let stored;\n8:const state = {\n15:const keys = new Set();\n16:let mouseLean = null, lastFrame = 0, lastHud = 0, audioContext = null, nextMusic = 0, gamepadPrevious = [];\n17:let toggledBreath = false, pausedFrom = null;\n19:function save() {\n24:function notify(text) {\n30:function tone(frequency, duration = .14, volume = .5, type = 'sine') {\n37:function unlockAudio() {\n40:function music() {\n49:function hint() { return state.input === 'gamepad' ? (state.settings.glyphs === 'Xbox' ? 'A SELECT  ·  B BACK' : '✕ SELECT  ·  ○ BACK') : '↑ ↓ CHOOSE  ·  ENTER SELECT  ·  ESC BACK'; }\n50:function button(label, action, primary = false, id = '', detail = '') {\n53:function shell(content, label = '', footer = true) {\n56:function screen(name) { state.screen = name; state.idle = 0; render(); }\n57:function person() { return state.member || { name: 'Guest', day: 1, sessions: 0, minutes: 0, stars: {}, instructor: 'Birch', color: 1, outfit: 1, finished: false }; }\n58:function labelDay() { const member = person(); return member.finished ? 'FREE PRACTICE' : `DAY ${member.day} OF 5`; }\n59:function tile(activity, locked = false) {\n63:function settingRow(label, value, action, id = '') { return `<div class=\"row\"><span>${label}</span><button class=\"chip setting-button\" data-action=\"${action}\" data-id=\"${id}\">${value}</button></div>`; }\n64:function aboutContent() {\n68:function render() {\n146:function currentButtons() { return [...app.querySelectorAll('button:not([disabled])')].filter(node => node.offsetParent !== null && !node.closest('.touch-notice')); }\n147:function focusMove(direction) {\n151:function memberDefault() { return { name: 'Guest', day: 1, sessions: 0, minutes: 0, stars: {}, instructor: 'Birch', color: 1, outfit: 1, finished: false }; }\n152:function beginCheck() { state.check = { phase: 'still', elapsed: 0, directions: new Set(), spine: 25 + Math.floor(Math.random() * 25) }; state.activity = null; screen('check'); }\n153:function startActivity(activity, options = {}) {\n159:function completeActivity() {\n169:function attemptInput(key) {\n182:const tuningDefaults = { spring: 11, damping: 6, instability: 1.3, noise: .19 };\n183:const tuning = { ...tuningDefaults };\n184:function updateActivity(dt) {\n225:function updateHUD() {\n242:function updateCheckHUD() {\n250:function update(dt) {\n256:function action(name, id) {\n317:function pollGamepad() {\n337:const simulation = new My3D2dge.Game({ headless: true, step: 1 / 120 });\n339:function frame(now) {\n345:window.__ZEN = {\n352:if (state.hub.active) {\n354:  window.AIHub.on('start', () => { state.hub.started = true; state.hub.startedAt = window.AIHub.time(); startActivity(ACTIVITIES.find(activity => activity.id === 'stork'), { seconds: 60 }); });\n355:  window.AIHub.on('message', (data, from) => { state.hub.ghosts[from] = data; });\n356:  window.AIHub.on('time-up', () => { if (!state.hub.finished) { state.hub.finished = true; if (state.activity && state.screen === 'play') state.hub.score += state.activity.score / Math.max(1, state.activity.samples) * 1000; window.AIHub.result({ score: Math.round(state.hub.score) }); screen('hub'); } });\n357:  window.AIHub.on('end', () => { state.hub.finished = true; screen('hub'); });\n358:  window.AIHub.connect({ mode: 'ghost', seats: [1, 4], card: true }).then(() => window.AIHub.ready()).catch(() => notify('Unable to connect to the Hub.'));\n109:Exit interview: before you finish, also save these answers as exit-interview.json in this folder's root, beside the game's .html: one JSON object in exactly the shape below, every value filled in (\"unknown\" for anything you can't confirm). Tools read it (the game's run record and the AI Hub catalogue), so write plain text, and check that the file parses as JSON.\n111:  \"sourceInformation\": {\"date\": \"\", \"source\": \"\", \"plan\": \"\", \"genre\": \"\", \"perspective\": \"\", \"tech\": \"\", \"artDirection\": \"\", \"animation\": \"\", \"audio\": \"\", \"online\": \"\", \"testing\": \"\", \"research\": \"\", \"environment\": \"\", \"model\": \"\", \"usage\": \"added on import\"},\n112:  \"testingFeedback\": [\"your answer to each Testing Feedback question, in order\"],\n113:  \"engineFeedback\": [\"your answer to each Engine Feedback question, in order\"],\n114:  \"promptFeedback\": [\"your answer to each Prompt Feedback question, in order\"],\n115:  \"aiHub\": {\nWee Bit of Zen-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221356/engine/my-3d2dge-agent.js\nWee Bit of Zen-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221356/engine/my-3d2dge.js\n/* FITCLIPS: an animation set in my-3D2dge's readable format (written by the tools in tools/; clips may be edited by hand).\n * Mesh2Motion (CC0), Quaternius (CC0), CMU Graphics Lab Motion Capture Database (free for all uses)\n * 23 clips, 560 key poses. Played by src/mocap/mocap.js with src/mocap/readable.js. \"sources\" holds the proportions\n * each library was measured with; \"fit\" each clip's average and worst body-point error against its capture (mm).\n * my-3D2dge readable clip. Times in seconds; every other number is a whole number. Rig frame: forward, right, up.\n * L and R are the figure's own sides. Directions are percentages and need not add up: [100, 0, 0] and [50, 0, 0] agree.\n * hips   [forward, right, up]   the pelvis, in percent of standing hip height (100 = standing, 55 = sitting\n--- session instructions from plan ---\n8:- **✔ means tested.** It was run on this computer against engine v0.88.0 and hub client 1.4.0 while this plan was written. Trust those recipes. Numbers marked \"start\" are tuning defaults: change them with the dev sliders.\n39:4. **The daily ritual.** Weigh-in, sessions, recap, bed. Tiny numbers feel huge.\n54:In an AI Hub session: straight to the round, no title or menus (section 14).\n57:**A session (every activity, every time):** Card (one sentence on what you can and can't do here, device-correct controls, star targets, your best) → instructor demonstrates for 3 s with one line → \"Breathe in\" 3-2-1 → play for 45 to 90 s → stars stamp down, minutes drop into Gerald, Tare comments → Again / Done. Again is free: a session ends only on Done, your best run counts, and every run pays minutes. Target: 2 to 3 minutes door to door. A story run takes 40 to 50 minutes and shows everything.\n66:// one fixed step (dt = 1/120). nx, ny: smooth noise. fx, fy: scripted pushes (a gull, a gust, a thought)\n110:✔ The input map must keep the engine's menu actions. **A custom map replaces the whole preset**: without `confirm` and `start`, menus and the hub card's Enter silently stop working.\n173:**Minutes and Gerald.** Gerald is a ceramic hippo with a coin slot who swallows your minutes. Earned: session minutes × (1 + .25 × stars), × 1.5 on Tare's Suggestion for the day. Coins fly up and clink in. Cumulative, never spent.\n188:| 1 Orientation | Arrival card, pick instructor, first Body Check | Stork, Squat, Step, Tray | Forced guided Stork Stand counts as session 1 |\n195:3 sessions a day. You may go to bed early (Tare says something). Tare's Suggestion marks one mat with a floating star.\n203:**Members.** Three save slots shown as big Member Cards (rig portrait, nickname, Spine Age, Day). No text entry: avatar by pills (hair `short spiky long ponytail bald`, 6 skins, 8 tops, 4 bottoms) and a nickname from a list with Reroll (\"Gentle Doug\", \"Sir Slouch\", \"Ms. Almost\", \"The Other Pat\", ...). Use `game.saves` (`write`, `read`, `save(slot)`, `list()`, `latest()`). Autosave at dawn and after each session. Saves go through `saves.write`, so a test can reload them.\n207:## 6. The island (hub)\n209:The Institute for Gentle Improvement, on Lumbar Island. Motto on every sign: *Gently, Or Not At All.* A small `TileMap` in `threequarter`, about 44 × 26 cells. Crossing it takes 5 s. No enemies, no timer. Time passes only by doing sessions: morning light, noon, then dusk.\n230:- **HUD:** top left Day and 3 session pips; top right Spine Age and Gerald's count, clear of `game.cornerArea()`. Nothing else.\n293:**Lights:** morning ambient about .92, noon lights off, dusk about .62 with warm lamps (`game.lights`). Keep bright scenes bright; a dark look is wrong here. Canvas lighting only: no `enableGPU`, and no WebGPU requirement for the hub.\n303:## 9. Animation recipes (all ✔)\n328:rig.wob = [p.x, p.y];  rig.mocap = lib.sample(clip, t);   // rig.mocap = null to stop\n347:Other clips in the set: `Meditate` (Candle), `Pushup`, `22_14`, `Jumping Jacks`, `Run_Loop`, `Walk_Loop`, `Hop_One_Foot_Loop` (regaining balance), `Dizzy` (stumble), `Get_Up_From_Back` (falls), `Victory`, `Cheering_Two_Hands` (3★), `Stretch_Yawn` (morning), `Sleeping` (Lou, bed), `Greeting` (instructor's bow), `Wave_Hello`, `Waiting_Loop`, `Idle_Subtle` (Regulars). Crossfade with `lib.blend(a, b, k)`, or fade a clip over the rig with `rig.mocapW`.\n448:**Tools:** jump to any scene/activity/tier/day; finish now with N stars; unlock all; +10 minutes; set Spine Age; reset this member; no stumbles; bot plays (poor/average/good/expert); show Plate trace and numbers; frame step; force attract; **Pose Viewer** (pick any clip, scrub, print a pose row for `game/data/poses.js`); log `game.debug.snapshot()` to the console. Hidden in a hub session.\n456:**AI Hub session (`ghost` mode, 1 to 4).** Follow the protocol README (`https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/README.md`); it is short, read it. Outside a session the game is unaffected and `connect()` answers `null`. ✔ This exact shape passed the harness at 1, 2, 3 and 4 players, on the bad network, and with the host leaving.\n458:**The round: \"Morning Class\".** Everyone plays the same 3 events on their own copy, in lockstep, seeing others as translucent seat-coloured ghosts on neighbouring mats (or in the world for Slalom and Jog). About 150 s: each event is 5 s intro + 40 s play + 5 s scores. Deal with `AIHub.rng('deal')`: one from Stork/Candle/Squat/Push-Up, one from Step/Hoop, one from Slalom/Jog.\n461:const inSession = !!(window.AIHub && AIHub.active);\n467:  const info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'ghost', seats: [1, 4], card: true });\n469:  AIHub.on('card', c => { card = c; });\n470:  AIHub.on('start', () => {});\n471:  AIHub.on('message', (d, from) => { /* ghost state */ });\n472:  AIHub.on('leave', ({ id }) => { /* remove that ghost */ });\n473:  AIHub.on('time-up', () => report());                  // result() at once if not reported\n474:  AIHub.on('end', () => { over = true; game.audio.stopMusic(); game.audio.mute(true); game.input.clear(); });\n475:  await game.booted; AIHub.ready();                     // no key press\n479:- **Card (yours, `card: true`):** the studio with the players lined up on mats, Tare hopping, the title, each player's name and colour with a ready tick, how to win, this player's controls, seconds left. While `AIHub.time() === -Infinity`: `confirm` or `start` → `AIHub.answer('ready')`, `more` (△) → `AIHub.answer('more')`, clicks on Ready/More too. No menus or choices on the card. Show \"More time\" state from the `card` event (`asked`, `paused`).\n480:- **Clock:** all event timing comes from `AIHub.time()`, not `game.time`. A frame over 50 ms gives up its time, so a slow machine's game clock lags and would desync. Countdown while negative. Play at ≥ 0. If `info.limitMs` is shorter than the round, shrink the events.\n481:- **Randomness:** every activity takes its disturbances from `AIHub.rng('e' + eventIndex)` (and a seeded `E.rng` offline). `Math.random` is only for cosmetics like particles and blinks, because copies draw it at different rates.\n482:- **Ghost data:** `AIHub.send({ t: 'g', a: eventIndex, l: [x, y], p: phase, w: [wx, wy], s: score }, { reliable: false })` about 10 times a second. Draw only if `a` matches your current event. `r.actor(..., { alpha: .5 })`, name tag in seat colour. Names come from `info.players`, drawn with `E.font` only (never HTML). Limit: 20 messages/s.\n483:- **Reporting:** `AIHub.progress({ score: total, label: total + ' pts' })` about once a second; at the end `AIHub.result({ score: total, stats: { Steadiness: '84%' }, awards: [{ title: 'Most Still', detail: '...' }] })` once.\n484:- **In a session:** no title, attract, dev, quit, restart or saved progress. Options opens the settings over the running round (`live`). No chat, emotes or custom names. No other network. Engine already ignores Options while Create is held ✔.\n490:<script>/* vendor/session.js, unmodified, first script in head */</script>\n495:<meta name=\"hub:type\" content=\"Game\"><meta name=\"hub:players\" content=\"1–4\"><meta name=\"hub:source\" content=\"Wii Fit\">\n496:<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\"><meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"1-4\"><meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"ghost\">\n497:<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"3\">\n498:<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Stay steadiest over 3 exercises; most points wins\">\n499:<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Lean: left stick, WASD or mouse. Breathe: R2, Space or click\">\n506:**Stack:** the my-3D2dge full engine (2D views), its `mode7`, `road`, `physics`, `rhythm` modules (all inside `my-3d2dge.js`), `Mocap` and a cut clip set, the hub client. No World3D, no other libraries. **Start from no single kit:** this game mixes genres, so use the full engine with your own page, and read `engine/kits/road.js`, `kart.js`, `rhythm.js`, `pinball.js` (physics) and `sports.js` (joining players) when you build those parts.\n511:git clone --depth 1 --filter=blob:none --sparse https://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge.git _src\n516:mkdir -p vendor/clipsrc/tools vendor/clipsrc/src/mocap tests/hub\n517:B=https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge/main\n518:H=https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub\n520:curl -fsSLo vendor/clipsrc/tools/mocap-lib.mjs $B/tools/mocap-lib.mjs\n521:curl -fsSLo vendor/clipsrc/src/mocap/readable.js $B/src/mocap/readable.js    # the tool needs it exactly here\n522:curl -fsSLo vendor/readable.js $B/src/mocap/readable.js\n523:curl -fsSLo vendor/mocap.js $B/src/mocap/mocap.js\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
