{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_137","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,180p' TASK.md; printf '\\\\n--- HUB & HANDOFF SPEC ---\\\\n'; sed -n '490,655p' PLAN.md; printf '\\\\n--- ACTIVE UPDATE ---\\\\n'; D='Wee Bit of Zen-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221356'; sed -n '190,225p' \\\"\"'$D/src/game.js\" | fold -sw 200; printf '\"'\\\\n--- KEY SCREENS ---\\\\n'; sed -n '55,108p' \\\"\"'$D/src/game.js\" | fold -sw 200'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_137","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,180p' TASK.md; printf '\\\\n--- HUB & HANDOFF SPEC ---\\\\n'; sed -n '490,655p' PLAN.md; printf '\\\\n--- ACTIVE UPDATE ---\\\\n'; D='Wee Bit of Zen-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221356'; sed -n '190,225p' \\\"\"'$D/src/game.js\" | fold -sw 200; printf '\"'\\\\n--- KEY SCREENS ---\\\\n'; sed -n '55,108p' \\\"\"'$D/src/game.js\" | fold -sw 200'","aggregated_output":"SOURCE: Wii Fit\n\nGenre: Pick the game genre(s) that best fit the source and would make the best game.\n\nPerspective: Pick the camera perspective(s) that best fit the genre and source and would make the best game.\n\nGame Title: A playful riff on SOURCE's name. Silently brainstorm 50 titles, then pick one with a real random number generator (e.g., run code).\n\nResearch: Whether and how much to research is your choice.\n\nPackage: For ease of deployment and sharing provide a single html file [GameTitle-SOURCE-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221356].html. Dependencies that can be downloaded do not have to be included in the html file if that is easier.\n\nTech Stack: Build on https://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge/tree/main/dist/handoff. You may change anything in it, the engine included, and add whatever systems, art assets and animations the game needs. The rest of the tech stack is your choice.\n\nArt Direction: Use the engine’s native style as the base. Make new art assets for whatever makes the game feel like the source; the engine’s asset library is fine for generic props.\n\nAnimation: Use the engine’s native animation system as the base. Make new animations for whatever makes the game feel like the source.\n\nAudio: All music, sound effects and voices are written in code, with no audio files. Voices are Animalese/Simlish-style gibberish. Music is to be set to 10% volume by default.\n\nOnline: https://github.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/tree/main/lib/hub\n\nWorking Environment and deliverable:\nCreate a subfolder called [GameTitle-SOURCE-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221356] to keep all your dev files in. You can develop separate modules, then bundle into a single file [GameTitle-SOURCE-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221356].html in root when you’re done. You may use external CDN dependencies. Do not read files outside what you need: other agents work in the folders beside this one. They share this machine’s ports and processes too. Prefer file:// and the engine’s headless tools. If you need a server (the AI Hub harness does), bind 127.0.0.1 on a port the OS picks (`python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1` prints it) and confirm the page is your game before trusting a result. Stop only processes you started, by their PID: never pkill, killall, fuser -k, or kill whatever holds a port.\n\nPerformance: Treat the performance budget as unlimited. Add as much detail, enemies, effects, lights, and shadows as the scene needs. Out of scope (handled later): FPS targets, optimization.\n\nTesting: Test as much as you like with headless tools: scripts that play the game and check its state, including a scripted playthrough of the whole game. Keep them behind one command that prints only failures and a one-line count, and rerun it only after changing the code it covers. Use screenshots only for what a script can’t check. Don’t use subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit.\n\nEffort: Spend effort however you see fit.\n\n## This computer\nChecked 2026-11-04 20:05 (America/Vancouver) by node check-environment.mjs.\n\n- **Computer:** Worki9: 13th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i9-13900K, 32 cores, 20 GB RAM, 8 GB swap. Ubuntu 26.04.1 LTS on WSL2 (Linux 6.18.33.1-microsoft-standard-WSL2).\n- **Space:** 850 GB free in the home folder. /tmp: 9.8 GB, in memory (tmpfs), 8.2 GB free when checked.\n- **Display:** none for runs (they run with DISPLAY unset), so a headed browser needs xvfb-run.\n- **Browsers:** Playwright 1.63.0 for Python (from playwright.sync_api import sync_playwright), with Chromium 153.0 (WebGL 2, software-rendered; WebGPU, software-rendered, when started with --enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader), Firefox 155.0 (WebGL 2, software-rendered), WebKit 26.6 (WebGL 2) already downloaded. Phone and tablet device profiles are built in.\n  WebGPU only works on a secure page: file:// or http://127.0.0.1. A WebGPU canvas can come out blank in a headless screenshot, so check the game's state instead.\n  For Node, `npm install playwright@1.63.0` in your folder uses the browsers already downloaded; another version downloads its own.\n  Playwright runs here with PLAYWRIGHT_HOST_PLATFORM_OVERRIDE=ubuntu24.04-x64 (already set for runs): this OS isn't one it supports by name.\n- **Tools:** node 24.22.1, npm 11.19.1, python3 3.14.8, pip3 26.2.1, git 2.56.0, gh 2.46.0, curl 8.22.0, wget 1.25.0, jq 1.8.1, ffmpeg 9.0.2, ffprobe 9.0.2, sqlite3 3.53.4, zip 3.0, unzip 6.00, rustc 1.99.0, cargo 1.99.0, go 1.27.1, java 27, lighthouse 13.5.0, shot-scraper 1.12, xvfb-run, magick 7.1.2, esbuild 0.28.2, uv 0.12.23, tsc 7.0.2, wasm-bindgen 0.2.129.\n- **Rust:** rustup's toolchains 1.96.0, 1.98.1, stable; the wasm32-unknown-unknown target on 1.98.1.\n- **Not installed:** sox, bun, deno.\n- **Network:** internet works (github.com, registry.npmjs.org).\n- **Memory:** earlyoom is on: when memory runs out it ends the biggest browser, so \"Target closed\", \"page crashed\" or \"browser has been closed\" means memory ran out, not a bug in your game. Run fewer browsers at once rather than retrying.\n\n### What this computer doesn't have\n\nNo script can check these, so they're written by hand. Test with the stand-ins; anything that needs the real thing is checked as far as it can be here, never required.\n\n- **No physical controller.** Emulate one: replace navigator.getGamepads with a stub that returns a pad in the standard mapping (Playwright's add_init_script / addInitScript).\n- **No touch device.** Use Playwright's phone and tablet profiles, which have touch, and tap with page.touchscreen.\n- **Nobody to listen.** Check sound by what Web Audio produces: render it with an OfflineAudioContext, or read levels from an AnalyserNode.\n- **No second player.** Play multiplayer with two browser pages (or contexts) on this computer.\n- **No real iPhone or iPad.** WebKit with an iPhone profile is the closest; it isn't iOS Safari.\n- **No TV.** Judge the 10-foot view from screenshots at 1920×1080.\n\n### Sharing this computer\n\n- Other agents run here at the same time. Keep one or two browsers open at once, and close them when you're done.\n- Keep every file you make inside your own folder, not /tmp or a parent folder: /tmp is shared.\n- The browsers are already downloaded: don't run `playwright install` or `playwright install-deps`.\n- The system Python has Playwright and nothing else. For one (Pillow, numpy …), use uv: `uv run --with pillow python script.py`, adding `--with playwright==1.63.0` when the script drives a browser too (a newer Playwright can't find the browsers here).\n\n## Goal\n\nBuild an original game inspired by the source.\n\nScope\n\nCreate a feature-complete demo. Capture what makes the source distinctive (its world, characters, themes and tone) and turn it into the mechanics, pacing and UX of a great game. The demo must be long enough to show ALL features and gameplay mechanics so a player can clearly understand how the game plays and feels, and what they can and cannot do. Treat the demo as a complete, polished vertical slice. It should contain all the infrastructure, systems, and polish needed so the remainder of the game could later be built out with normal designer tools.\n\nInclude a dev mode, reachable from the pause menu, with the standard tools for testing the game quickly. Balance is key, so expose the most important gameplay variables as live sliders, with a reset to defaults.\n\nAttract Mode: After 10 seconds without input on the title/menu screen, start a looping AI-played demo or scripted replay (arcade/kiosk style); any input exits it. The AI (or replay) can be simple and may cheat freely (infinite health, ammo, abilities, no clip, etc). Its only job is to show as much of the demo as possible, the attract mode is not meant to balance the game.\n\nMultiplayer: Follow https://github.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/tree/main/lib/hub for multiplayer integration into ai-hub as well as for the game on its own.\n\nNarrative tone: Use a writing style similar to the source’s.\n\n## UI & UX: 10-Foot Controller-First Philosophy\nDesign the game around a PS5 DualSense (or any pad the browser reports in its standard mapping) played on a TV at 10 feet. With keyboard and mouse it's the same game on the same screens, not a separate desktop layout, but they should feel native, not like stand-ins for controller buttons. The keyboard uses the keys PC players expect for the genre. The mouse aims, looks, and clicks menu items and things in the world (hover moves the focus) wherever the genre uses it. On-screen prompts follow the input used last: PlayStation glyphs for the controller (with a Settings option to show Xbox glyphs, A B X Y, instead), keys and mouse buttons for keyboard and mouse.\n\nDo not use overly dense, web-style data screens.\n\nTouch-only devices: no touch controls; show \"Controller or keyboard required\" and the settings button. Let the attract mode run.\n\n## Done\nNo TODOs, placeholders, or stubbed features. The demo is complete.\n\n## Source Information\nCRITICAL: Put Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback in your chat reply and an in-game About/Credits screen. Write \"unknown\" for anything you can't confirm.\n- Date: 2026-11-04 22:13:56\n- Source: the work it's based on\n- Plan: the file name of the plan you were given to build from, or none\n- Genre and Perspective: genre and camera perspective used\n- Tech: stack, libraries/engines, with versions if applicable\n- Art Direction: style used\n- Animation: system used\n- Audio: music, sound effects and voice used\n- Online: network features used, or none\n- Testing: testing parameters allowed\n- Research: research done, or none\n- Environment: Codex CLI (headless); Linux\n- Model: OpenAI, gpt-6.1-terra, reasoning effort max\n- Usage: write \"added on import\". You can't see your own cost, so don't estimate it: the runner records the real cost, tokens and time, and the agent that imports the game into AI Hub puts them on your About/Credits screen.\n\nExit interview: before you finish, also save these answers as exit-interview.json in this folder's root, beside the game's .html: one JSON object in exactly the shape below, every value filled in (\"unknown\" for anything you can't confirm). Tools read it (the game's run record and the AI Hub catalogue), so write plain text, and check that the file parses as JSON.\n{\n  \"sourceInformation\": {\"date\": \"\", \"source\": \"\", \"plan\": \"\", \"genre\": \"\", \"perspective\": \"\", \"tech\": \"\", \"artDirection\": \"\", \"animation\": \"\", \"audio\": \"\", \"online\": \"\", \"testing\": \"\", \"research\": \"\", \"environment\": \"\", \"model\": \"\", \"usage\": \"added on import\"},\n  \"testingFeedback\": [\"your answer to each Testing Feedback question, in order\"],\n  \"engineFeedback\": [\"your answer to each Engine Feedback question, in order\"],\n  \"promptFeedback\": [\"your answer to each Prompt Feedback question, in order\"],\n  \"aiHub\": {\n    \"name\": \"the game's title, as on its title screen\",\n    \"tagline\": \"a few words to go under the title\",\n    \"description\": \"one or two sentences for the catalogue\",\n    \"type\": \"Game, Tech demo or Tool\",\n    \"genre\": \"one of Action, Adventure, Fighting, Flight, Horror, Kids & Learning, Life Sim, Platformer, Puzzle, Racing, RPG, Shooter, Simulation, Sports, Stealth, Strategy\",\n    \"source\": \"the work it's based on, e.g. Moby-Dick\",\n    \"series\": \"its franchise, e.g. Star Fox, or empty\",\n    \"players\": \"how many can play: 1, 1–2 or 1–4\",\n    \"controls\": \"the controls, in one line\",\n    \"tags\": [\"3 to 6 lowercase tags, e.g. 2d, 3d, arcade, story, co-op, versus, first-person, third-person, top-down, side-scrolling, pixel art, low-poly, retro, sci-fi, fantasy, comedy, vehicles, boss fights, exploration\"]\n  }\n}\nThe catalogue's model, effort, CLI, date and usage come from the run's record after you finish, so they aren't asked here.\n\nTesting Feedback\n\n- How many issues did testing catch?\n- How many would be considered critical issues / game breaking?\n- What was the most helpful test you ran?\n- What was the least helpful test you ran?\n\nEngine Feedback\n\n- What did you like most about the engine?\n- Did you get stuck or guess wrong?\n- What was the most important thing you had to build yourself?\n- What was the hardest part about using the engine?\n- What did you change in the engine, and why? (none if nothing)\n- If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be?\n\nPrompt Feedback\n\n- What did you like most about this prompt?\n- What was confusing?\n- What was the hardest thing to do?\n- What would you change in this prompt?\n\n--- HUB & HANDOFF SPEC ---\n<script>/* vendor/session.js, unmodified, first script in head */</script>\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover\">\n<title>THE TITLE — a tagline</title>\n<meta name=\"description\" content=\"one or two sentences\">\n<meta name=\"theme-color\" content=\"#2cc6e6\">\n<meta name=\"hub:type\" content=\"Game\"><meta name=\"hub:players\" content=\"1–4\"><meta name=\"hub:source\" content=\"Wii Fit\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\"><meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"1-4\"><meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"ghost\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"3\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Stay steadiest over 3 exercises; most points wins\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Lean: left stick, WASD or mouse. Breathe: R2, Space or click\">\n```\n\n---\n\n## 15. Tech and setup\n\n**Stack:** the my-3D2dge full engine (2D views), its `mode7`, `road`, `physics`, `rhythm` modules (all inside `my-3d2dge.js`), `Mocap` and a cut clip set, the hub client. No World3D, no other libraries. **Start from no single kit:** this game mixes genres, so use the full engine with your own page, and read `engine/kits/road.js`, `kart.js`, `rhythm.js`, `pinball.js` (physics) and `sports.js` (joining players) when you build those parts.\n\n**Fetch (✔ every command run from a clean folder; run from the dev folder):**\n\n```sh\ngit clone --depth 1 --filter=blob:none --sparse https://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge.git _src\ngit -C _src sparse-checkout set dist/handoff\ncp -r _src/dist/handoff engine        # then remove _src\nnpm install playwright@1.63.0         # uses the browsers already here. Never `playwright install`, whatever the engine's README says\n\nmkdir -p vendor/clipsrc/tools vendor/clipsrc/src/mocap tests/hub\nB=https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge/main\nH=https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub\ncurl -fsSLo vendor/clipsrc/tools/anim-set.mjs $B/tools/anim-set.mjs\ncurl -fsSLo vendor/clipsrc/tools/mocap-lib.mjs $B/tools/mocap-lib.mjs\ncurl -fsSLo vendor/clipsrc/src/mocap/readable.js $B/src/mocap/readable.js    # the tool needs it exactly here\ncurl -fsSLo vendor/readable.js $B/src/mocap/readable.js\ncurl -fsSLo vendor/mocap.js $B/src/mocap/mocap.js\nfor f in src/mocap/sets/mesh2motion.js src/mocap/sets/cmu.js examples/cmu-lib/CMU_111.js examples/cmu-lib/CMU_22.js; do curl -fsSLo vendor/clipsrc/$(basename $f) $B/$f; done\ncurl -fsSLo vendor/session.js $H/session.js\nfor f in harness.html bridge.js round.js; do curl -fsSLo tests/hub/$f $H/$f; done\nnode vendor/clipsrc/tools/anim-set.mjs vendor/clipsrc/mesh2motion.js vendor/clipsrc/cmu.js vendor/clipsrc/CMU_111.js vendor/clipsrc/CMU_22.js \\\n  --clips \"Pushup,Meditate,Jumping Jacks,Sleeping,Victory,Cheering_Two_Hands,Dizzy,Idle_Subtle,Greeting,CMU:Run_Loop,CMU:Walk_Loop,Stretch_Yawn,Get_Up_From_Back,Waiting_Loop,Hop_One_Foot_Loop,Wave_Hello,111_38_part1,111_38_part2,111_39_part1,111_39_part2,111_39_part3,111_41_part3,22_14\" \\\n  --name FITCLIPS --out vendor/fitclips.js --credit \"Mesh2Motion (CC0), Quaternius (CC0), CMU Graphics Lab Motion Capture Database (free for all uses)\"\n# prints 23 clips, about 173 KB. vendor/clipsrc can then go; it is not bundled\n```\n\nMore clips, if you want them: search `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge/main/src/mocap/catalogs/cmu-takes.tsv` (take `NN_xx` lives in `examples/cmu-lib/CMU_NN.js`) and `.../catalogs/mesh2motion.json`.\n\n**Layout:**\n\n```\nengine/        the handoff copy (my-3d2dge.js is the engine; API.md, API-INDEX.md, AI_GUIDE.md, tools/, kits/, docs/)\nvendor/        readable.js, mocap.js, fitclips.js, session.js\ngame/\n  index.html   dev page: canvas (#screen with CSS width and height 100%, or it draws at 300×150 ✔) and the scripts in order\n  core.js      G namespace, game, INPUT, DEV defaults, state, saves, deep links (#hub, #act/stork/1, #day/3, #ending)\n  balance.js   Balance model, intent sources (devices, bots), Plate\n  rigs.js      makeRig, setBody and moves, Tare, Gerald, joints, cast\n  ui.js        Pills, prompt, Card, Results, DevPanel\n  audio.js     songs, sfx, babble\n  data/        lines.js, poses.js, activities.js, charts.js, courses.js, trays.js, days.js, unlocks.js\n  activities/  hold.js, candle.js, rep.js, step.js, hoop.js, jog.js, slalom.js, tray.js, laundry.js\n  scenes/      title, attract, member, arrival, island, bodycheck, session, evening, games, ending, about, class, round\ntests/run.mjs  the one test command; tests/hub/ the harness\nbuild.mjs      the one build command\n```\n\nPlain scripts on one global `G`, no ES modules (the page must work from `file://`). **Build out by data:** a designer adds a tier, pose, chart, gate course, tray, line or day by editing `game/data/`, with no code change. Add a short `game/data/README.md` saying how.\n\n**Activity registry:**\n\n```js\nG.activity({ id: 'stork', family: 'hold', discipline: 'Stillness', name: 'Stork Stand', view: 'brawler', camera: { zoom: false },\n  class: true, hub: true, tiers: [ {/* numbers */}, {/* numbers */} ], stars: [.35, .65, .90], lines: {/* ... */},\n  setup(ctx) {}, update(dt, ctx) {}, draw(r, ctx) {}, hud(r, ctx) {},\n  result(ctx) { return { pct, detail }; },\n  bot(ctx, skill) { return intent; },\n  ghost(ctx) { return state; }, drawGhost(r, ctx, id, state) {} });\n```\n`ctx`: `{ tier, rng (seeded), contestants: [{ intent, bal, rig, name, color, score, local }], time, done, cheat }`. Every activity becomes its own pausable scene, generated from the entry. Set `game.debug = { snapshot() { return { scene, activity, tier, day, session, pct, stars, minutes, spineAge, lean, source }; } }`: tests and engine tools read it.\n\n**`build.mjs`:** concatenates engine, `vendor/readable.js`, `vendor/mocap.js`, `vendor/fitclips.js`, game files; replaces every `</script` with `<\\/script` in everything it inlines ✔; writes head tags, CSS, the boot markup at the start of `<body>` (copy the `e3-boot` div from `engine/game/index.html`); injects the exit-interview JSON as `G.ABOUT`; writes the single file to the place your brief names (pass it as an argument) and copies it to `tests/hub/game.html`. External CDN is allowed but not needed: inline everything. About 1.5 MB.\n\n**Engine changes:** only the small Dialog shadow patch (section 11) is required. Everything else works through the public API and the wrappers above. Note whatever you change, and why, for your Engine Feedback.\n\n**Traps already found (so you don't lose time on them):**\n1. A custom `input` map replaces the preset (section 3).\n2. `brawler`: +y is toward the camera (section 8).\n3. Mouse movement doesn't change `lastDevice` from `'keyboard'` (section 3).\n4. Default `music` is .5 and `glyphs` 'auto': set both (section 11).\n5. Music at 10% hides the beat: click on the sfx bus (section 4).\n6. HTML menus lack hover focus; the touch notice is 88% opaque (section 11).\n7. `E.Dialog` hard-codes a dark text shadow (section 11). The standard Settings list is long at 10 feet: rely on its scrolling focus and the zoom CSS.\n8. In tests, `game.fadeTime = 0`; `game.go` otherwise delays the new scene .22 s.\n9. A frame past 50 ms gives up its time: browser tests here are software-rendered and slow, so wait on game state, never on the clock.\n10. In Python Playwright use `page.wait_for_timeout`, not `time.sleep` (it freezes the event loop and frames never appear).\n11. `E.store` is shared by id; set `id` on the game, and `E.store.clear()` between test games in one process.\n12. Fixed-camera scenes need `camera: { zoom: false }`, or the wheel zooms instead of stepping.\n\n---\n\n## 16. Testing\n\n**One command: `node tests/run.mjs [rules|browser|hub|all]`.** It prints only failures and one final line (`213 passed, 0 failed`). Rerun only the group whose code you changed. Use scripted checks first and screenshots only for what a script can't judge. Do not use subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit.\n\n**`rules` (Node, no browser, seconds).** Load engine, vendor and game files in a `vm` context with `window`, `addEventListener` and `location` stand-ins (✔ `Mocap` and clips load this way; see `engine/kits/test.mjs`). Drive with `game.advance` and `input.tap/hold`; read `game.debug.snapshot()`.\n- Lean model: each row of the section 3 table lands in its band (±10 points) with the bots, on 12 seeds.\n- Every activity, every tier: passive under 1★; average at least 1★; good at least 2★; finishes in its time; `game.errors` stays empty.\n- **Full scripted playthrough:** New Member through every scene to the Ending using real input taps and bots, all 12 activities played, Spine Age falls, Day 3 plateau holds, unlocks arrive, Free Play opens. Also a passive run (the worst player still reaches the end).\n- Saves: reload gives the same state; 3 members stay separate; a damaged save doesn't crash.\n- Same seed and same input give the same hash twice.\n- Attract: fires at 10 s idle (and not at 9.9), visits every playlist item, any input returns to title, no save or unlock changed.\n- Dev: every slider changes its live value; reset restores all; every jump target loads.\n- Class: 4 inputs, scores, podium. Hub logic with a fake `AIHub` object: same seed, same deal; time-up reports once; end stops input.\n- Data lint: every line, pose, clip name, activity and unlock referenced exists; no `TODO` or placeholder strings in `game/`.\n\n**`browser` (Playwright, one browser at a time, on the built file via `file://`, which needs no server):**\n- `node engine/tools/check.mjs <built file>` passes with no errors (and act on its look notes), at 1280×720.\n- **Controller stand-in ✔:** `add_init_script` replaces `navigator.getGamepads` with a `'DualSense Wireless Controller (STANDARD GAMEPAD)'` pad in `mapping: 'standard'`. Check axes lean, `buttons[7].value` reads through `input.value`, ✕ confirms, prompts show ✕, Settings to Xbox shows A.\n- Keyboard and mouse: WASD nudges; pointer leans; hover moves focus in `Pills` and in the HTML menus; click activates; prompts change with the device.\n- Touch-only: a phone profile shows the notice and Settings button, no touch controls, and attract starts at 10 s behind it. iPhone profile on WebKit as a smoke test; also load in Firefox.\n- Sound: after a gesture, an `AnalyserNode` on the music bus is non-silent and `game.settings.music === .1` on fresh storage; the voice bus sounds during dialog; `OfflineAudioContext` renders `babble` non-silent; no audio files and no network requests at all (`page.on('request')`).\n- 1920×1080 screenshots for the 10-foot judgement of title, Plate, Card, results and island: look at them once per milestone.\n\n**`hub`:** copy the bundle to `tests/hub/game.html`, serve `tests/hub` with `python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1`, read the port it prints, confirm the page is yours, then open `harness.html?game=game.html&` + each of: `players=1&auto=1`; `players=2&auto=1`; `players=3&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`; `players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`; `players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&scenario=host-leave`. Wait for `document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'`, require `window.__hubCheck.pass`, and print failing `checks`. Then open the game on its own and see it reach the title. Stop only your server, by its PID, never with `pkill`, `killall` or `fuser -k`.\n\n**Sharing this computer:** keep one or two browsers open, keep every file in your own folder, don't read the folders beside it (other agents work there), never kill anything you did not start. \"Target closed\" or \"page crashed\" means memory ran out: run fewer browsers rather than retrying.\n\n---\n\n## 17. Build order\n\nEach milestone ends with a playable game and green tests. Keep the build and the tests working from M0 onward.\n\n| # | Build | Done when |\n|---|---|---|\n| M0 | Fetch; `build.mjs`; `tests/run.mjs`; `INPUT`, Shell theme, settings; empty title and round scenes with the session wrapper | Harness passes on the empty game; music .1; `tests/run.mjs` prints its line |\n| M1 | Lean, intent, devices, bots, Plate; `makeRig`; Tare and voice; studio scene; **Stork Stand** with Card and Results | Feels good on stick, keys and mouse. Bands hold. **Stop and tune here: it is the whole game** |\n| M2 | Title, Pills, Member Card, Arrival, island, mats, Body Check, Day loop, evening, saves, Gerald, Spine Age; attract skeleton; Dev panel with Lean sliders | A day can be lived start to end |\n| M3 | Sun Flow, Quiet Candle, all three Rail exercises | Bots pass; poses read at 1080p |\n| M4 | Step Class, Hoop Hips, Coastal Jog | Bots pass; beat audible at default volume |\n| M5 | Slalom, Tray Service, Laundry Line | Bots pass |\n| M6 | Five-day script, Tare's Day, Gentle Games, duel, Ending, Credits, Free Play, wardrobe, full line bank, all music and sfx | Full playthrough test passes |\n| M7 | Class mode; the hub round with ghosts and card | Harness at all five settings; two-page play shows ghosts |\n| M8 | Full attract, full Dev Mode with Pose Viewer, About screen, tier 2s, Comfort, polish pass (particles, stamps, rumble, transitions: `game.go` with `fade: 'iris'`) | All groups green |\n| M9 | Final bundle, exit interview parses, About matches it, brief checklist below | Done |\n\n**If you truly run out of room, cut in this order and remove every trace (no stubs):** tier 2s except Eyes Closed → Tare's Day scene → Laundry Line → Coastal Jog → wardrobe items beyond three. Never cut: the Lean, Stork, Rail, Step, Candle, Slalom, Tray, the day loop, the ending, attract, dev mode, Class, the hub round, About.\n\n---\n\n## 18. Finish line: your brief, line by line\n\n- [ ] Title chosen by the brief's method and shown on the title screen; single HTML file with the brief's name in the brief's place; dev files in the brief's dev folder\n- [ ] Original game: no copied names, characters, art, music or levels\n- [ ] Genre and perspective as section 1; built on the handoff engine (changes noted)\n- [ ] Art and animation: engine-native base, new assets and motion (sections 8, 9)\n- [ ] All audio from code; gibberish voices; music 10% by default (section 10)\n- [ ] Hub session passes the harness; the game also runs on its own, with local Class (section 14)\n- [ ] Demo shows every feature; all infrastructure is real; designer data in `game/data/` (section 15)\n- [ ] Dev Mode from the pause menu: tools, live sliders, reset (section 13)\n- [ ] Attract at 10 s idle, loops, any input exits, runs on touch-only (section 12)\n- [ ] Writing in the source-inspired tone throughout (section 7)\n- [ ] 10-foot, controller-first; native keyboard and mouse; hover moves focus; prompts follow last device; PlayStation glyphs with Xbox setting; no dense screens (section 11)\n- [ ] Touch-only: no touch controls, \"Controller or keyboard required\", Settings button (section 11)\n- [ ] One test command, failures and a count only; scripted playthrough of the whole game (section 16)\n- [ ] No TODOs, placeholders or stubs anywhere\n- [ ] Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback, Prompt Feedback in the chat reply **and** the About screen, \"unknown\" for what you can't confirm, Usage as \"added on import\". Plan field: this plan's file name. Research field: what you actually did (further research is optional; this plan's recipes are already tested)\n- [ ] Exit-interview JSON beside the HTML, in the brief's exact shape, parses. Suggested `aiHub`: type `Game`, genre `Sports`, source `Wii Fit`, series empty, players `1–4`, controls in one line, tags from: `pixel art`, `comedy`, `versus`, `arcade`, `story`, `2d`\n\n--- ACTIVE UPDATE ---\n  if (activity.stun <= 0) {\n    if (mouseLean) { activity.ux = mouseLean.x; activity.uy = mouseLean.y; }\n    else if (axisX || axisY) { activity.ux = axisX; activity.uy = axisY; }\n    else { activity.ux = clamp(activity.ux + dx * 2.2 * dt, -1, 1); activity.uy = clamp(activity.uy + dy * 2.2 * dt, -1, 1); if (!dx) activity.ux *= Math.max(0, 1 - .5 * dt); if (!dy) activity.uy *= \nMath.max(0, 1 - .5 * dt); }\n  } else activity.stun -= dt;\n  const gentle = state.settings.gentle ? .7 : 1, time = activity.elapsed, disturbance = tuning.noise * gentle;\n  const ax = tuning.spring * (activity.ux - activity.px) - tuning.damping * activity.vx + tuning.instability * gentle * activity.px + disturbance * (Math.sin(time * 1.7) + .5 * Math.sin(time * 3.23));\n  const ay = tuning.spring * (activity.uy - activity.py) - tuning.damping * activity.vy + tuning.instability * gentle * activity.py + disturbance * (Math.sin(time * 1.19 + 1) + .5 * Math.sin(time * \n2.71));\n  activity.vx += ax * dt; activity.vy += ay * dt; activity.px += activity.vx * dt; activity.py += activity.vy * dt;\n  if (Math.hypot(activity.px, activity.py) >= 1 && activity.stun <= 0) { activity.stumbles++; activity.stun = 1; activity.px *= .5; activity.py *= .5; activity.vx *= -.2; activity.vy *= -.2; \ntone(196, .18); }\n  const phase = Math.floor(time / 12), rng = seeded(phase * 667 + 43);\n  activity.ringX = activity.id === 'stork' ? (rng() - .5) * .65 : activity.kind === 'slalom' ? Math.sin(time * .55) * .46 : 0;\n  activity.ringY = activity.id === 'stork' ? (rng() - .5) * .35 : 0;\n  const distance = Math.hypot(activity.px - activity.ringX, activity.py - activity.ringY), ringSize = state.settings.gentle ? .48 : .38;\n  const steadiness = clamp(1 - distance * 1.4, 0, 1);\n  let quality = steadiness;\n  const held = state.settings.breathToggle ? toggledBreath : keys.has(' ') || !!pad?.buttons[7]?.pressed;\n  activity.effort = clamp(activity.effort + (held ? 1 : -1) * dt / 4, 0, 1);\n  if (activity.kind === 'rep') { const goal = (Math.sin(time * Math.PI / 2 - Math.PI / 2) + 1) / 2; quality = clamp(1 - Math.abs(activity.effort - goal), 0, 1) * steadiness; activity.reps = \nMath.floor(time / 4); }\n  if (activity.kind === 'breath') { const inhale = Math.sin(time * Math.PI / 4) > 0; quality = steadiness * (held === inhale ? 1 : .5); }\n  if (activity.kind === 'step') quality = clamp(activity.beatHits / Math.max(1, time * 100 / 60) * 1.5, 0, 1);\n  if (activity.kind === 'hoop') { activity.motions += (Math.abs(activity.vx) + Math.abs(activity.vy)) * dt; quality = clamp(activity.motions / Math.max(1, time) * 3 + activity.hoopHits / Math.max(1, \ntime / 10), 0, 1); }\n  if (activity.kind === 'jog') quality = clamp(activity.jogHits / Math.max(1, time * 2) * 1.5, 0, 1) * steadiness;\n  if (activity.kind === 'slalom') quality = clamp(1 - Math.abs(activity.px - activity.ringX) * 1.5, 0, 1);\n  if (activity.kind === 'tray') { activity.tray += (activity.px - activity.tray) * dt * 1.5; quality = clamp(1 - Math.abs(activity.tray) * 2, 0, 1); }\n  if (activity.kind === 'rope') quality = clamp(1 - Math.abs(activity.px) * 2, 0, 1) * (activity.uy < -.1 ? 1 : .65);\n  if (activity.kind === 'candle') { activity.flame = clamp(activity.flame + (distance < ringSize ? .13 : -.3) * dt, 0, 1); quality = activity.flame; }\n  activity.score += quality; activity.samples++;\n  if (state.hub.active) {\n    const now = window.AIHub.time();\n    if (now - state.hub.lastSend >= 100) { state.hub.lastSend = now; window.AIHub.send({ x: activity.px, y: activity.py, exercise: activity.id }); }\n    if (now - state.hub.lastProgress >= 1000) { state.hub.lastProgress = now; window.AIHub.progress({ score: Math.round(state.hub.score + activity.score / Math.max(1, activity.samples) * 1000), \nlabel: activity.name }); }\n  }\n  if (activity.elapsed >= activity.seconds) completeActivity();\n}\nfunction updateHUD() {\n\n--- KEY SCREENS ---\n}\nfunction screen(name) { state.screen = name; state.idle = 0; render(); }\nfunction person() { return state.member || { name: 'Guest', day: 1, sessions: 0, minutes: 0, stars: {}, instructor: 'Birch', color: 1, outfit: 1, finished: false }; }\nfunction labelDay() { const member = person(); return member.finished ? 'FREE PRACTICE' : `DAY ${member.day} OF 5`; }\nfunction tile(activity, locked = false) {\n  const group = GROUPS[activity.group], stars = person().stars?.[activity.id] || 0;\n  return `<button class=\"activity ${locked ? 'locked' : ''}\" data-action=\"${locked ? 'locked' : 'select-activity'}\" data-id=\"${activity.id}\" \nstyle=\"--group:${group.color};--group-light:${group.light}\"><span class=\"activity-icon\">${activity.icon}</span><span class=\"activity-copy\"><span \nclass=\"activity-group\">${group.name}</span><strong>${activity.name}</strong><small>${locked ? `Opens day ${activity.day}` : activity.tagline}</small></span><span class=\"activity-end\">${locked ? '⌁' : \n(stars ? '★'.repeat(stars) : '↗')}</span></button>`;\n}\nfunction settingRow(label, value, action, id = '') { return `<div class=\"row\"><span>${label}</span><button class=\"chip setting-button\" data-action=\"${action}\" \ndata-id=\"${id}\">${value}</button></div>`; }\nfunction aboutContent() {\n  const info = window.BUILD_INFO || {}, sections = [ ['Source Information', info.sourceInformation], ['Testing Feedback', info.testingFeedback], ['Engine Feedback', info.engineFeedback], ['Prompt \nFeedback', info.promptFeedback] ];\n  return sections.map(([title, value]) => `<div class=\"about-group\"><h3>${title}</h3>${Array.isArray(value) ? value.map((item, index) => `<p><b>${index + 1}.</b> ${escapeHTML(item)}</p>`).join('') : \nObject.entries(value || {}).map(([key, item]) => `<p><b>${escapeHTML(key)}:</b> ${escapeHTML(item)}</p>`).join('')}</div>`).join('');\n}\nfunction render() {\n  const member = person();\n  let content = '', heading = '';\n  if (state.screen === 'title' || state.screen === 'attract') {\n    content = `<main class=\"hero\"><section class=\"hero-copy\"><div class=\"eyebrow\"><span class=\"sun-dot\">✳</span> A LITTLE ISLAND FOR YOURSELF</div><h1 class=\"logo\">wee bit<br><em>of zen</em><span \nclass=\"logo-dot\">.</span></h1><p class=\"lede\">A pleasantly imperfect retreat for<br>your body, mind, and general wobble.</p><div class=\"menu-stack\">${button('Begin your stay', 'slots', true, '', 'A \nlittle time just for you')}${button('Local Class', 'class', false, '', 'Practice together, up to four')}${button('About & credits', 'about')}</div></section><div class=\"island-message\"><span>✦ &nbsp; \nTAKE IT AT YOUR OWN PACE</span><strong>Good things happen<br>one wobble at a time.</strong></div></main>`;\n    if (state.screen === 'attract') content += '<div class=\"center-copy\">DEMONSTRATION &nbsp; · &nbsp; PRESS ANY KEY</div>';\n  } else if (state.screen === 'slots') {\n    heading = 'YOUR STAY';\n    content = `<main class=\"main-wrap\"><div class=\"section-head\"><div><div class=\"eyebrow\">✳ &nbsp; THE GUEST BOOK</div><h1>Make yourself at home.</h1><p>Choose a room for your island \nstay.</p></div></div><div class=\"card-grid\">${state.slots.map((slot, index) => `<button class=\"card slot-card\" data-action=\"slot\" data-id=\"${index}\"><span class=\"slot-num\">0${index + 1}</span><span \nclass=\"slot-avatar\">${slot ? '☺' : '+'}</span><strong>${slot ? escapeHTML(slot.name) : 'New member'}</strong><small>${slot ? `${slot.finished ? 'Free practice' : `Day ${slot.day}`} · \n${Math.floor(slot.minutes || 0)} fit minutes` : 'A fresh start awaits'}</small><span class=\"arrow\">↗</span></button>`).join('')}</div><div class=\"actions\">${button('Back', 'home')}</div></main>`;\n  } else if (state.screen === 'setup') {\n    heading = 'NEW MEMBER';\n    content = `<main class=\"main-wrap narrow\"><div class=\"section-head\"><div><div class=\"eyebrow\">✳ &nbsp; NICE TO MEET YOU</div><h1>A little about you.</h1><p>There is no wrong way to \narrive.</p></div></div><div class=\"card setup-card\"><label class=\"field\">WHAT SHOULD WE CALL YOU?<input id=\"nickname\" maxlength=\"16\" value=\"${escapeHTML(member.name === 'Guest' ? '' : member.name)}\" \nplaceholder=\"Your name\" autocomplete=\"off\"></label><p class=\"field-label\">CHOOSE YOUR COLOUR</p><div class=\"options\">${OUTFITS.map((color, index) => `<button class=\"option swatch ${member.outfit === \nindex ? 'selected' : ''}\" data-action=\"outfit\" data-id=\"${index}\" style=\"--swatch:${color}\" aria-label=\"Outfit ${index + 1}\">${member.outfit === index ? '✓' : ''}</button>`).join('')}</div><p \nclass=\"field-label\">YOUR INSTRUCTOR</p><div class=\"options\">${['Birch', 'Alder'].map(name => `<button class=\"option ${member.instructor === name ? 'selected' : ''}\" data-action=\"instructor\" \ndata-id=\"${name}\">${name === 'Birch' ? '✳' : '✦'} &nbsp; ${name}</button>`).join('')}</div><div class=\"actions\">${button('Back', 'slots')}${button('Arrive on the island', 'create-member', \ntrue)}</div></div></main>`;\n  } else if (state.screen === 'intro') {\n    heading = labelDay();\n    content = `<main class=\"main-wrap narrow\"><div class=\"dialogue card\"><div class=\"eyebrow\">✳ &nbsp; A NOTE FROM TARE</div><div class=\"speaker\">☺</div><h1>Welcome${member.day === 1 ? ', ' + \nescapeHTML(member.name) : ' back'}.</h1><p>“${DAY_INTROS[Math.min(4, member.day - 1)]}”</p><p class=\"note\">Your stay starts with a gentle body check. No weights, no judgement, and absolutely no pop \nquizzes. Well, one tiny quiz.</p><div class=\"actions\">${button('Begin body check', 'check', true)}</div></div></main>`;\n  } else if (state.screen === 'check') {\n    heading = 'BODY CHECK';\n    content = `<main class=\"play-hud\"><div class=\"hud-top\"><div class=\"hud-box\"><div class=\"eyebrow\">✳ &nbsp; BODY CHECK</div><h2>Just checking in.</h2><p id=\"check-text\">Find a comfortable \ncenter.</p></div><div class=\"hud-box timer\" id=\"check-timer\">05</div></div><div class=\"hud-bottom\"><div class=\"play-instruction\">${state.check?.phase === 'lean' ? 'Lean in each direction: ← ↑ → ↓' : \n'Stay steady. Small wobbles are welcome.'}</div><div class=\"meter\"><span id=\"check-progress\"></span></div></div></main>`;\n  } else if (state.screen === 'question') {\n    heading = 'BODY CHECK';\n    content = `<main class=\"main-wrap narrow\"><div class=\"card dialogue\"><div class=\"eyebrow\">✳ &nbsp; ONE VERY SCIENTIFIC QUESTION</div><h1>How are you arriving today?</h1><p>Your answer helps us \ncalibrate the island's extremely sophisticated vibes.</p><div class=\"menu-stack\">${button('Bright-eyed and bushy-tailed', 'question-answer', true, 'bright')}${button('A little wobbly, honestly', \n'question-answer', false, 'wobbly')}${button('Mostly thinking about snacks', 'question-answer', false, 'snacks')}</div></div></main>`;\n  } else if (state.screen === 'check-result') {\n    heading = 'BODY CHECK COMPLETE';\n    content = `<main class=\"main-wrap narrow\"><div class=\"card dialogue\"><div class=\"eyebrow\">✳ &nbsp; ACCORDING TO TARE</div><div class=\"score-big\">${state.check.spine}</div><h1>Your Spine \nAge</h1><p>“A completely imaginary number. Your actual spine remains splendid.”</p><p class=\"note\">Today is a fine day to practice being here.</p><div class=\"actions\">${button('Explore the island', \n'island', true)}</div></div></main>`;\n  } else if (state.screen === 'island') {\n    heading = labelDay();\n    const dialogue = CAST[(member.day + member.sessions) % CAST.length];\n    content = `<main class=\"main-wrap island-main\"><div class=\"section-head\"><div><div class=\"eyebrow\">✳ &nbsp; ${labelDay()} &nbsp; / &nbsp; ${Math.floor(member.minutes || 0)} FIT \nMINUTES</div><h1>Find your kind of movement.</h1><p>${member.finished ? 'The island is yours. Stay as long as you like.' : `Hello, ${escapeHTML(member.name)}. Choose a mat and settle \nin.`}</p></div><div class=\"day-badge\"><strong>${member.sessions || 0}<small>/ 3</small></strong><span>TODAY'S<br>SESSIONS</span></div></div><div class=\"activity-grid\">${ACTIVITIES.map(activity => \ntile(activity, !member.finished && activity.day > member.day)).join('')}</div><div class=\"island-bar\"><p><b>${dialogue[0]} says:</b> “${dialogue[1]}”</p><div class=\"map-actions\">${button('Local \nClass', 'class')}${button(member.finished ? 'Your story' : member.day === 5 ? 'Gentle Games' : 'End the day', member.finished ? 'ending' : 'sleep', true)}</div></div></main>`;\n  } else if (state.screen === 'activity') {\n    const activity = state.selection, group = GROUPS[activity.group]; heading = group.name.toUpperCase();\n    content = `<main class=\"main-wrap narrow\"><div class=\"card activity-detail\" style=\"--group:${group.color};--group-light:${group.light}\"><div class=\"activity-large-icon\">${activity.icon}</div><div \nclass=\"eyebrow\">${group.icon} &nbsp; ${group.name.toUpperCase()} &nbsp; / &nbsp; ${activity.seconds} SECONDS</div><h1>${activity.name}</h1><p>${activity.tagline}</p><div class=\"divider\"></div><h3>How \nto play</h3><p>${activity.instruction}</p><p class=\"note\">Lean with WASD, arrow keys, left stick or mouse. ${state.settings.gentle ? 'Gentle mode is on.' : 'Make small, comfortable \nmovements.'}</p><div class=\"actions\">${button('Back to island', state.classMode ? 'class' : 'island')}${button('Begin practice', 'start-activity', true)}</div></div></main>`;\n  } else if (state.screen === 'play') {\n    const activity = state.activity, group = GROUPS[activity.group]; heading = group.name.toUpperCase();\n    content = `<main class=\"play-hud\"><div class=\"hud-top\"><div class=\"hud-box\"><div class=\"eyebrow\">${group.icon} &nbsp; ${group.name.toUpperCase()}</div><h2>${activity.name}</h2><p \nid=\"play-status\">Find your center.</p></div><div class=\"hud-box timer\"><span id=\"play-timer\">${Math.ceil(activity.seconds)}</span><small>SEC</small></div></div><div class=\"balance-plate\" \naria-label=\"Balance indicator\"><span class=\"plate-ring\" id=\"plate-ring\"></span><span class=\"plate-dot\" id=\"plate-dot\"></span></div><div class=\"hud-bottom\"><div class=\"play-instruction\" \nid=\"play-instruction\">${activity.instruction}</div><div class=\"meter\"><span id=\"play-progress\"></span></div><div class=\"hud-caption\"><span id=\"play-score\">A GENTLE START</span><span>ESC / OPTIONS \n&nbsp; PAUSE</span></div></div></main>`;\n  } else if (state.screen === 'result') {\n    const result = state.result;\n    heading = 'SESSION COMPLETE';\n    content = `<main class=\"main-wrap narrow\"><div class=\"card dialogue result-card\"><div class=\"eyebrow\">✳ &nbsp; PRACTICE COMPLETE</div><div \nclass=\"stars-big\">${'★'.repeat(result.stars)}<span>${'☆'.repeat(3 - result.stars)}</span></div><h1>Lovely work${state.classMode ? ', everyone' : ''}.</h1><p>“${result.message}”</p><div \nclass=\"result-stats\"><div><strong>${result.percent}%</strong><small>STEADINESS</small></div><div><strong>+${result.minutes}</strong><small>FIT \nMINUTES</small></div><div><strong>${result.stumbles}</strong><small>WOBBLES</small></div></div><div class=\"actions\">${button('Practice again', 'retry')}${button(state.festival ? 'Continue the Games' \n: state.classMode ? 'Class results' : 'Back to island', 'result-continue', true)}</div></div></main>`;\n  } else if (state.screen === 'recap') {\n    heading = 'DAY COMPLETE';\n    content = `<main class=\"main-wrap narrow\"><div class=\"card dialogue\"><div class=\"eyebrow\">✳ &nbsp; ANOTHER DAY WELL SPENT</div><h1>Rest is part of it.</h1><p>“${member.sessions} sessions today. \nGerald the ceramic hippo has made a careful note.”</p><div class=\"result-stats\"><div><strong>${Math.floor(member.minutes)}</strong><small>FIT \nMINUTES</small></div><div><strong>${Object.keys(member.stars || {}).length}</strong><small>MATS VISITED</small></div></div><div class=\"actions\">${button('Wake up to day ' + (member.day + 1), \n'next-day', true)}</div></div></main>`;\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_138","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n '14\\\\.|AIHub|AI Hub|Hub' PLAN.md | tail -40; sed -n '1,240p' 'Wee Bit of Zen-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221356/src/game.js'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_138","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n '14\\\\.|AIHub|AI Hub|Hub' PLAN.md | tail -40; sed -n '1,240p' 'Wee Bit of Zen-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221356/src/game.js'\"","aggregated_output":"54:In an AI Hub session: straight to the round, no title or menus (section 14).\n277:**Candle thoughts:** \"Did you lock the door?\" / \"What is a lumbar?\" / \"Is that my knee?\" / \"Dennis.\" / \"You left the stove on in 2014.\" / \"Who sent that card?\" / \"Am I breathing right now?\" / \"Now I'm breathing on purpose.\" / \"Olive?\"\n452:## 14. Multiplayer\n456:**AI Hub session (`ghost` mode, 1 to 4).** Follow the protocol README (`https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/README.md`); it is short, read it. Outside a session the game is unaffected and `connect()` answers `null`. ✔ This exact shape passed the harness at 1, 2, 3 and 4 players, on the bad network, and with the host leaving.\n458:**The round: \"Morning Class\".** Everyone plays the same 3 events on their own copy, in lockstep, seeing others as translucent seat-coloured ghosts on neighbouring mats (or in the world for Slalom and Jog). About 150 s: each event is 5 s intro + 40 s play + 5 s scores. Deal with `AIHub.rng('deal')`: one from Stork/Candle/Squat/Push-Up, one from Step/Hoop, one from Slalom/Jog.\n461:const inSession = !!(window.AIHub && AIHub.active);\n467:  const info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'ghost', seats: [1, 4], card: true });\n469:  AIHub.on('card', c => { card = c; });\n470:  AIHub.on('start', () => {});\n471:  AIHub.on('message', (d, from) => { /* ghost state */ });\n472:  AIHub.on('leave', ({ id }) => { /* remove that ghost */ });\n473:  AIHub.on('time-up', () => report());                  // result() at once if not reported\n474:  AIHub.on('end', () => { over = true; game.audio.stopMusic(); game.audio.mute(true); game.input.clear(); });\n475:  await game.booted; AIHub.ready();                     // no key press\n479:- **Card (yours, `card: true`):** the studio with the players lined up on mats, Tare hopping, the title, each player's name and colour with a ready tick, how to win, this player's controls, seconds left. While `AIHub.time() === -Infinity`: `confirm` or `start` → `AIHub.answer('ready')`, `more` (△) → `AIHub.answer('more')`, clicks on Ready/More too. No menus or choices on the card. Show \"More time\" state from the `card` event (`asked`, `paused`).\n480:- **Clock:** all event timing comes from `AIHub.time()`, not `game.time`. A frame over 50 ms gives up its time, so a slow machine's game clock lags and would desync. Countdown while negative. Play at ≥ 0. If `info.limitMs` is shorter than the round, shrink the events.\n481:- **Randomness:** every activity takes its disturbances from `AIHub.rng('e' + eventIndex)` (and a seeded `E.rng` offline). `Math.random` is only for cosmetics like particles and blinks, because copies draw it at different rates.\n482:- **Ghost data:** `AIHub.send({ t: 'g', a: eventIndex, l: [x, y], p: phase, w: [wx, wy], s: score }, { reliable: false })` about 10 times a second. Draw only if `a` matches your current event. `r.actor(..., { alpha: .5 })`, name tag in seat colour. Names come from `info.players`, drawn with `E.font` only (never HTML). Limit: 20 messages/s.\n483:- **Reporting:** `AIHub.progress({ score: total, label: total + ' pts' })` about once a second; at the end `AIHub.result({ score: total, stats: { Steadiness: '84%' }, awards: [{ title: 'Most Still', detail: '...' }] })` once.\n600:- Class: 4 inputs, scores, podium. Hub logic with a fake `AIHub` object: same seed, same deal; time-up reports once; end stops input.\n645:- [ ] Hub session passes the harness; the game also runs on its own, with local Class (section 14)\n655:- [ ] Exit-interview JSON beside the HTML, in the brief's exact shape, parses. Suggested `aiHub`: type `Game`, genre `Sports`, source `Wii Fit`, series empty, players `1–4`, controls in one line, tags from: `pixel art`, `comedy`, `versus`, `arcade`, `story`, `2d`\n'use strict';\n\nconst app = document.getElementById('app');\nconst STORAGE = 'wee-bit-of-zen-v1';\nconst DEFAULT_SETTINGS = { music: 10, sound: 10, voice: true, gentle: false, breathToggle: false, tips: true, glyphs: 'PlayStation' };\nlet stored;\ntry { stored = JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem(STORAGE) || '{}'); } catch (_) { stored = {}; }\nconst state = {\n  screen: 'title', clock: 0, idle: 0, input: 'keyboard', settings: { ...DEFAULT_SETTINGS, ...(stored.settings || {}) },\n  slots: Array.isArray(stored.slots) ? stored.slots : [null, null, null], slot: 0, member: null,\n  selection: null, activity: null, returnScreen: 'title', check: null, toast: '', classPlayers: [],\n  festival: false, festivalIndex: 0, hub: { active: !!window.AIHub?.active, started: false, finished: false, score: 0, lastSend: 0, lastProgress: 0, ghosts: {} }\n};\nwhile (state.slots.length < 3) state.slots.push(null);\nconst keys = new Set();\nlet mouseLean = null, lastFrame = 0, lastHud = 0, audioContext = null, nextMusic = 0, gamepadPrevious = [];\nlet toggledBreath = false, pausedFrom = null;\n\nfunction save() {\n  if (state.hub.active) return;\n  if (state.member) state.slots[state.slot] = state.member;\n  try { localStorage.setItem(STORAGE, JSON.stringify({ settings: state.settings, slots: state.slots })); } catch (_) { notify('Saving is unavailable in this browser.'); }\n}\nfunction notify(text) {\n  state.toast = text;\n  const node = document.getElementById('toast');\n  if (node) { node.textContent = text; node.hidden = false; }\n  setTimeout(() => { if (state.toast === text) { state.toast = ''; const toast = document.getElementById('toast'); if (toast) toast.hidden = true; } }, 3000);\n}\nfunction tone(frequency, duration = .14, volume = .5, type = 'sine') {\n  if (!audioContext || audioContext.state !== 'running' || !state.settings.sound) return;\n  const oscillator = audioContext.createOscillator(), gain = audioContext.createGain(), now = audioContext.currentTime;\n  oscillator.type = type; oscillator.frequency.setValueAtTime(frequency, now);\n  gain.gain.setValueAtTime(.0001, now); gain.gain.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(Math.max(.00011, state.settings.sound / 100 * volume * .18), now + .015); gain.gain.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(.0001, now + duration);\n  oscillator.connect(gain); gain.connect(audioContext.destination); oscillator.start(now); oscillator.stop(now + duration + .01);\n}\nfunction unlockAudio() {\n  try { if (!audioContext) audioContext = new (window.AudioContext || window.webkitAudioContext)(); if (audioContext.state === 'suspended') audioContext.resume(); } catch (_) {}\n}\nfunction music() {\n  if (!audioContext || audioContext.state !== 'running' || !state.settings.music || state.clock < nextMusic) return;\n  nextMusic = state.clock + 1.25;\n  const notes = [261.63, 329.63, 392, 493.88, 392, 329.63, 293.66, 349.23];\n  const oscillator = audioContext.createOscillator(), gain = audioContext.createGain(), now = audioContext.currentTime;\n  oscillator.type = 'sine'; oscillator.frequency.value = notes[Math.floor(state.clock / 1.25) % notes.length];\n  gain.gain.setValueAtTime(.0001, now); gain.gain.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(Math.max(.00011, state.settings.music / 100 * .035), now + .08); gain.gain.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(.0001, now + 1.1);\n  oscillator.connect(gain); gain.connect(audioContext.destination); oscillator.start(now); oscillator.stop(now + 1.15);\n}\nfunction hint() { return state.input === 'gamepad' ? (state.settings.glyphs === 'Xbox' ? 'A SELECT  ·  B BACK' : '✕ SELECT  ·  ○ BACK') : '↑ ↓ CHOOSE  ·  ENTER SELECT  ·  ESC BACK'; }\nfunction button(label, action, primary = false, id = '', detail = '') {\n  return `<button class=\"action${primary ? ' primary' : ''}\" data-action=\"${action}\" data-id=\"${escapeHTML(id)}\"><span>${label}${detail ? `<small>${detail}</small>` : ''}</span><span class=\"arrow\">↗</span></button>`;\n}\nfunction shell(content, label = '', footer = true) {\n  return `<div class=\"page\"><header class=\"topbar\"><button class=\"brand\" data-action=\"home\" aria-label=\"Return to title\"><span class=\"brand-mark\">✳</span><span>WEE BIT <b>OF ZEN</b></span></button><span class=\"top-label\">${label}</span><button class=\"settings-link\" data-action=\"settings\" aria-label=\"Settings\">⚙ <span>SETTINGS</span></button></header>${content}${footer ? `<footer class=\"footer\"><span>${hint()}</span><span>THE INSTITUTE FOR GENTLE IMPROVEMENT&nbsp; ✳ &nbsp; LUMBAR ISLAND</span></footer>` : ''}</div><div class=\"toast\" id=\"toast\" hidden></div>`;\n}\nfunction screen(name) { state.screen = name; state.idle = 0; render(); }\nfunction person() { return state.member || { name: 'Guest', day: 1, sessions: 0, minutes: 0, stars: {}, instructor: 'Birch', color: 1, outfit: 1, finished: false }; }\nfunction labelDay() { const member = person(); return member.finished ? 'FREE PRACTICE' : `DAY ${member.day} OF 5`; }\nfunction tile(activity, locked = false) {\n  const group = GROUPS[activity.group], stars = person().stars?.[activity.id] || 0;\n  return `<button class=\"activity ${locked ? 'locked' : ''}\" data-action=\"${locked ? 'locked' : 'select-activity'}\" data-id=\"${activity.id}\" style=\"--group:${group.color};--group-light:${group.light}\"><span class=\"activity-icon\">${activity.icon}</span><span class=\"activity-copy\"><span class=\"activity-group\">${group.name}</span><strong>${activity.name}</strong><small>${locked ? `Opens day ${activity.day}` : activity.tagline}</small></span><span class=\"activity-end\">${locked ? '⌁' : (stars ? '★'.repeat(stars) : '↗')}</span></button>`;\n}\nfunction settingRow(label, value, action, id = '') { return `<div class=\"row\"><span>${label}</span><button class=\"chip setting-button\" data-action=\"${action}\" data-id=\"${id}\">${value}</button></div>`; }\nfunction aboutContent() {\n  const info = window.BUILD_INFO || {}, sections = [ ['Source Information', info.sourceInformation], ['Testing Feedback', info.testingFeedback], ['Engine Feedback', info.engineFeedback], ['Prompt Feedback', info.promptFeedback] ];\n  return sections.map(([title, value]) => `<div class=\"about-group\"><h3>${title}</h3>${Array.isArray(value) ? value.map((item, index) => `<p><b>${index + 1}.</b> ${escapeHTML(item)}</p>`).join('') : Object.entries(value || {}).map(([key, item]) => `<p><b>${escapeHTML(key)}:</b> ${escapeHTML(item)}</p>`).join('')}</div>`).join('');\n}\nfunction render() {\n  const member = person();\n  let content = '', heading = '';\n  if (state.screen === 'title' || state.screen === 'attract') {\n    content = `<main class=\"hero\"><section class=\"hero-copy\"><div class=\"eyebrow\"><span class=\"sun-dot\">✳</span> A LITTLE ISLAND FOR YOURSELF</div><h1 class=\"logo\">wee bit<br><em>of zen</em><span class=\"logo-dot\">.</span></h1><p class=\"lede\">A pleasantly imperfect retreat for<br>your body, mind, and general wobble.</p><div class=\"menu-stack\">${button('Begin your stay', 'slots', true, '', 'A little time just for you')}${button('Local Class', 'class', false, '', 'Practice together, up to four')}${button('About & credits', 'about')}</div></section><div class=\"island-message\"><span>✦ &nbsp; TAKE IT AT YOUR OWN PACE</span><strong>Good things happen<br>one wobble at a time.</strong></div></main>`;\n    if (state.screen === 'attract') content += '<div class=\"center-copy\">DEMONSTRATION &nbsp; · &nbsp; PRESS ANY KEY</div>';\n  } else if (state.screen === 'slots') {\n    heading = 'YOUR STAY';\n    content = `<main class=\"main-wrap\"><div class=\"section-head\"><div><div class=\"eyebrow\">✳ &nbsp; THE GUEST BOOK</div><h1>Make yourself at home.</h1><p>Choose a room for your island stay.</p></div></div><div class=\"card-grid\">${state.slots.map((slot, index) => `<button class=\"card slot-card\" data-action=\"slot\" data-id=\"${index}\"><span class=\"slot-num\">0${index + 1}</span><span class=\"slot-avatar\">${slot ? '☺' : '+'}</span><strong>${slot ? escapeHTML(slot.name) : 'New member'}</strong><small>${slot ? `${slot.finished ? 'Free practice' : `Day ${slot.day}`} · ${Math.floor(slot.minutes || 0)} fit minutes` : 'A fresh start awaits'}</small><span class=\"arrow\">↗</span></button>`).join('')}</div><div class=\"actions\">${button('Back', 'home')}</div></main>`;\n  } else if (state.screen === 'setup') {\n    heading = 'NEW MEMBER';\n    content = `<main class=\"main-wrap narrow\"><div class=\"section-head\"><div><div class=\"eyebrow\">✳ &nbsp; NICE TO MEET YOU</div><h1>A little about you.</h1><p>There is no wrong way to arrive.</p></div></div><div class=\"card setup-card\"><label class=\"field\">WHAT SHOULD WE CALL YOU?<input id=\"nickname\" maxlength=\"16\" value=\"${escapeHTML(member.name === 'Guest' ? '' : member.name)}\" placeholder=\"Your name\" autocomplete=\"off\"></label><p class=\"field-label\">CHOOSE YOUR COLOUR</p><div class=\"options\">${OUTFITS.map((color, index) => `<button class=\"option swatch ${member.outfit === index ? 'selected' : ''}\" data-action=\"outfit\" data-id=\"${index}\" style=\"--swatch:${color}\" aria-label=\"Outfit ${index + 1}\">${member.outfit === index ? '✓' : ''}</button>`).join('')}</div><p class=\"field-label\">YOUR INSTRUCTOR</p><div class=\"options\">${['Birch', 'Alder'].map(name => `<button class=\"option ${member.instructor === name ? 'selected' : ''}\" data-action=\"instructor\" data-id=\"${name}\">${name === 'Birch' ? '✳' : '✦'} &nbsp; ${name}</button>`).join('')}</div><div class=\"actions\">${button('Back', 'slots')}${button('Arrive on the island', 'create-member', true)}</div></div></main>`;\n  } else if (state.screen === 'intro') {\n    heading = labelDay();\n    content = `<main class=\"main-wrap narrow\"><div class=\"dialogue card\"><div class=\"eyebrow\">✳ &nbsp; A NOTE FROM TARE</div><div class=\"speaker\">☺</div><h1>Welcome${member.day === 1 ? ', ' + escapeHTML(member.name) : ' back'}.</h1><p>“${DAY_INTROS[Math.min(4, member.day - 1)]}”</p><p class=\"note\">Your stay starts with a gentle body check. No weights, no judgement, and absolutely no pop quizzes. Well, one tiny quiz.</p><div class=\"actions\">${button('Begin body check', 'check', true)}</div></div></main>`;\n  } else if (state.screen === 'check') {\n    heading = 'BODY CHECK';\n    content = `<main class=\"play-hud\"><div class=\"hud-top\"><div class=\"hud-box\"><div class=\"eyebrow\">✳ &nbsp; BODY CHECK</div><h2>Just checking in.</h2><p id=\"check-text\">Find a comfortable center.</p></div><div class=\"hud-box timer\" id=\"check-timer\">05</div></div><div class=\"hud-bottom\"><div class=\"play-instruction\">${state.check?.phase === 'lean' ? 'Lean in each direction: ← ↑ → ↓' : 'Stay steady. Small wobbles are welcome.'}</div><div class=\"meter\"><span id=\"check-progress\"></span></div></div></main>`;\n  } else if (state.screen === 'question') {\n    heading = 'BODY CHECK';\n    content = `<main class=\"main-wrap narrow\"><div class=\"card dialogue\"><div class=\"eyebrow\">✳ &nbsp; ONE VERY SCIENTIFIC QUESTION</div><h1>How are you arriving today?</h1><p>Your answer helps us calibrate the island's extremely sophisticated vibes.</p><div class=\"menu-stack\">${button('Bright-eyed and bushy-tailed', 'question-answer', true, 'bright')}${button('A little wobbly, honestly', 'question-answer', false, 'wobbly')}${button('Mostly thinking about snacks', 'question-answer', false, 'snacks')}</div></div></main>`;\n  } else if (state.screen === 'check-result') {\n    heading = 'BODY CHECK COMPLETE';\n    content = `<main class=\"main-wrap narrow\"><div class=\"card dialogue\"><div class=\"eyebrow\">✳ &nbsp; ACCORDING TO TARE</div><div class=\"score-big\">${state.check.spine}</div><h1>Your Spine Age</h1><p>“A completely imaginary number. Your actual spine remains splendid.”</p><p class=\"note\">Today is a fine day to practice being here.</p><div class=\"actions\">${button('Explore the island', 'island', true)}</div></div></main>`;\n  } else if (state.screen === 'island') {\n    heading = labelDay();\n    const dialogue = CAST[(member.day + member.sessions) % CAST.length];\n    content = `<main class=\"main-wrap island-main\"><div class=\"section-head\"><div><div class=\"eyebrow\">✳ &nbsp; ${labelDay()} &nbsp; / &nbsp; ${Math.floor(member.minutes || 0)} FIT MINUTES</div><h1>Find your kind of movement.</h1><p>${member.finished ? 'The island is yours. Stay as long as you like.' : `Hello, ${escapeHTML(member.name)}. Choose a mat and settle in.`}</p></div><div class=\"day-badge\"><strong>${member.sessions || 0}<small>/ 3</small></strong><span>TODAY'S<br>SESSIONS</span></div></div><div class=\"activity-grid\">${ACTIVITIES.map(activity => tile(activity, !member.finished && activity.day > member.day)).join('')}</div><div class=\"island-bar\"><p><b>${dialogue[0]} says:</b> “${dialogue[1]}”</p><div class=\"map-actions\">${button('Local Class', 'class')}${button(member.finished ? 'Your story' : member.day === 5 ? 'Gentle Games' : 'End the day', member.finished ? 'ending' : 'sleep', true)}</div></div></main>`;\n  } else if (state.screen === 'activity') {\n    const activity = state.selection, group = GROUPS[activity.group]; heading = group.name.toUpperCase();\n    content = `<main class=\"main-wrap narrow\"><div class=\"card activity-detail\" style=\"--group:${group.color};--group-light:${group.light}\"><div class=\"activity-large-icon\">${activity.icon}</div><div class=\"eyebrow\">${group.icon} &nbsp; ${group.name.toUpperCase()} &nbsp; / &nbsp; ${activity.seconds} SECONDS</div><h1>${activity.name}</h1><p>${activity.tagline}</p><div class=\"divider\"></div><h3>How to play</h3><p>${activity.instruction}</p><p class=\"note\">Lean with WASD, arrow keys, left stick or mouse. ${state.settings.gentle ? 'Gentle mode is on.' : 'Make small, comfortable movements.'}</p><div class=\"actions\">${button('Back to island', state.classMode ? 'class' : 'island')}${button('Begin practice', 'start-activity', true)}</div></div></main>`;\n  } else if (state.screen === 'play') {\n    const activity = state.activity, group = GROUPS[activity.group]; heading = group.name.toUpperCase();\n    content = `<main class=\"play-hud\"><div class=\"hud-top\"><div class=\"hud-box\"><div class=\"eyebrow\">${group.icon} &nbsp; ${group.name.toUpperCase()}</div><h2>${activity.name}</h2><p id=\"play-status\">Find your center.</p></div><div class=\"hud-box timer\"><span id=\"play-timer\">${Math.ceil(activity.seconds)}</span><small>SEC</small></div></div><div class=\"balance-plate\" aria-label=\"Balance indicator\"><span class=\"plate-ring\" id=\"plate-ring\"></span><span class=\"plate-dot\" id=\"plate-dot\"></span></div><div class=\"hud-bottom\"><div class=\"play-instruction\" id=\"play-instruction\">${activity.instruction}</div><div class=\"meter\"><span id=\"play-progress\"></span></div><div class=\"hud-caption\"><span id=\"play-score\">A GENTLE START</span><span>ESC / OPTIONS &nbsp; PAUSE</span></div></div></main>`;\n  } else if (state.screen === 'result') {\n    const result = state.result;\n    heading = 'SESSION COMPLETE';\n    content = `<main class=\"main-wrap narrow\"><div class=\"card dialogue result-card\"><div class=\"eyebrow\">✳ &nbsp; PRACTICE COMPLETE</div><div class=\"stars-big\">${'★'.repeat(result.stars)}<span>${'☆'.repeat(3 - result.stars)}</span></div><h1>Lovely work${state.classMode ? ', everyone' : ''}.</h1><p>“${result.message}”</p><div class=\"result-stats\"><div><strong>${result.percent}%</strong><small>STEADINESS</small></div><div><strong>+${result.minutes}</strong><small>FIT MINUTES</small></div><div><strong>${result.stumbles}</strong><small>WOBBLES</small></div></div><div class=\"actions\">${button('Practice again', 'retry')}${button(state.festival ? 'Continue the Games' : state.classMode ? 'Class results' : 'Back to island', 'result-continue', true)}</div></div></main>`;\n  } else if (state.screen === 'recap') {\n    heading = 'DAY COMPLETE';\n    content = `<main class=\"main-wrap narrow\"><div class=\"card dialogue\"><div class=\"eyebrow\">✳ &nbsp; ANOTHER DAY WELL SPENT</div><h1>Rest is part of it.</h1><p>“${member.sessions} sessions today. Gerald the ceramic hippo has made a careful note.”</p><div class=\"result-stats\"><div><strong>${Math.floor(member.minutes)}</strong><small>FIT MINUTES</small></div><div><strong>${Object.keys(member.stars || {}).length}</strong><small>MATS VISITED</small></div></div><div class=\"actions\">${button('Wake up to day ' + (member.day + 1), 'next-day', true)}</div></div></main>`;\n  } else if (state.screen === 'festival') {\n    heading = 'DAY 5 &nbsp; / &nbsp; GENTLE GAMES';\n    content = `<main class=\"main-wrap narrow\"><div class=\"card dialogue\"><div class=\"eyebrow\">✳ &nbsp; THE GENTLE GAMES</div><h1>Ready, steady,<br><em>be yourself.</em></h1><p>Three friendly challenges, ending in the Grand Stillness with Gertrude. The prize is a very nice feeling.</p><p class=\"note\">Challenge ${state.festivalIndex + 1} of 3 &nbsp; · &nbsp; ${['Stork Stand', 'Slalom', 'Quiet Candle'][state.festivalIndex]}</p><div class=\"actions\">${button('Begin challenge', 'festival-start', true)}</div></div></main>`;\n  } else if (state.screen === 'ending') {\n    heading = 'THANK YOU FOR STAYING';\n    content = `<main class=\"main-wrap narrow\"><div class=\"card dialogue\"><div class=\"eyebrow\">✳ &nbsp; YOUR ISLAND IS ALWAYS HERE</div><div class=\"stars-big\">✳</div><h1>A little steadier.<br><em>A lot more you.</em></h1><p>Gertrude awards you the Golden Composure. Dennis is emotional. Tare insists the award is calibrated.</p><p class=\"note\">Thank you for five days of moving, breathing, and making room. The mats are yours whenever you wish.</p><div class=\"actions\">${button('Explore freely', 'free-play', true)}${button('About & credits', 'about')}</div></div></main>`;\n  } else if (state.screen === 'class') {\n    heading = 'LOCAL CLASS';\n    const players = state.classPlayers;\n    content = `<main class=\"main-wrap\"><div class=\"section-head\"><div><div class=\"eyebrow\">✳ &nbsp; BETTER TOGETHER</div><h1>Make room for friends.</h1><p>Up to four share the same screen. One keyboard player; connect controllers for more.</p></div></div><div class=\"class-players\">${[0, 1, 2, 3].map((index) => `<div class=\"card player-tile\"><span class=\"slot-avatar\">${players[index] ? '☺' : '+'}</span><strong>${players[index] ? escapeHTML(players[index].name) : 'Open spot'}</strong><small>${players[index] ? escapeHTML(players[index].type) : 'Join or add a bot'}</small><button class=\"chip\" data-action=\"class-toggle\" data-id=\"${index}\">${players[index] ? 'REMOVE' : 'ADD BOT'}</button></div>`).join('')}</div><div class=\"card class-select\"><p>CHOOSE A CLASS</p><div class=\"options\">${['stork','candle','step','slalom','tray'].map(id => `<button class=\"option ${state.selection?.id === id ? 'selected' : ''}\" data-action=\"class-activity\" data-id=\"${id}\">${ACTIVITIES.find(a => a.id === id).name}</button>`).join('')}</div></div><div class=\"actions\">${button('Back', member.name === 'Guest' ? 'home' : 'island')}${button('Start class', 'start-class', true)}</div></main>`;\n  } else if (state.screen === 'class-result') {\n    heading = 'LOCAL CLASS';\n    content = `<main class=\"main-wrap narrow\"><div class=\"card dialogue\"><div class=\"eyebrow\">✳ &nbsp; EVERYONE SHOWED UP</div><h1>A class act.</h1><p>Everyone gets their own kind of gold star.</p>${state.classPlayers.map((player, index) => `<div class=\"row\"><span>${escapeHTML(player.name)} ${player.type === 'Bot' ? '· BOT' : ''}</span><b>${Math.max(30, state.result.percent - index * 5)} points &nbsp; ★</b></div>`).join('')}<div class=\"actions\">${button('Back to class', 'class', true)}</div></div></main>`;\n  } else if (state.screen === 'settings') {\n    heading = 'SETTINGS';\n    content = `<main class=\"main-wrap narrow\"><div class=\"section-head\"><div><div class=\"eyebrow\">✳ &nbsp; MAKE YOURSELF COMFORTABLE</div><h1>Your settings.</h1></div></div><div class=\"card settings-card\">${settingRow('Music', state.settings.music + '%', 'volume', 'music')}${settingRow('Sound effects', state.settings.sound + '%', 'volume', 'sound')}${settingRow('Voice sounds', state.settings.voice ? 'ON' : 'OFF', 'toggle', 'voice')}${settingRow('Gentle mode', state.settings.gentle ? 'ON' : 'OFF', 'toggle', 'gentle')}${settingRow('Breathing', state.settings.breathToggle ? 'TOGGLE' : 'HOLD', 'toggle', 'breathToggle')}${settingRow('Tips', state.settings.tips ? 'ON' : 'OFF', 'toggle', 'tips')}${settingRow('Controller symbols', state.settings.glyphs.toUpperCase(), 'glyphs')}<p class=\"note\">Select a volume to cycle from 0% to 100%. Gentle mode makes balancing more forgiving.</p><div class=\"actions\">${button('Done', 'settings-back', true)}</div></div></main>`;\n  } else if (state.screen === 'pause') {\n    heading = 'PAUSED';\n    content = `<main class=\"main-wrap narrow\"><div class=\"card dialogue\"><div class=\"eyebrow\">✳ &nbsp; TAKE YOUR TIME</div><h1>Pause is a practice, too.</h1><div class=\"menu-stack\">${button('Resume', 'resume', true)}${button('Restart session', 'restart')}${button('Settings', 'settings')}${state.hub.active ? '' : button('Developer mode', 'dev')}${state.hub.active ? '' : button('Leave session', 'leave-play')}</div></div></main>`;\n  } else if (state.screen === 'dev') {\n    heading = 'DEVELOPER MODE';\n    content = `<main class=\"main-wrap narrow\"><div class=\"card settings-card\"><div class=\"eyebrow\">✳ &nbsp; LIVE TUNING</div><h1>Behind the wobble.</h1>${[['spring','Spring',4,20,.5],['damping','Damping',1,12,.5],['instability','Instability',0,4,.1],['noise','Disturbance',0,.8,.05]].map(([key, name, min, max, step]) => `<label class=\"slider\">${name} <output id=\"out-${key}\">${tuning[key]}</output><input type=\"range\" data-tuning=\"${key}\" min=\"${min}\" max=\"${max}\" step=\"${step}\" value=\"${tuning[key]}\"></label>`).join('')}<div class=\"actions\">${button('Reset tuning', 'reset-tuning')}${button('Back to pause', 'pause', true)}</div></div></main>`;\n  } else if (state.screen === 'about') {\n    heading = 'ABOUT & CREDITS';\n    content = `<main class=\"main-wrap narrow\"><div class=\"card scroll\"><div class=\"eyebrow\">✳ &nbsp; A LITTLE NOTE FROM THE MAKERS</div><h1>About & credits.</h1><p>Made with care for everyone who has ever wobbled.</p>${aboutContent()}<div class=\"actions\">${button('Back', 'about-back', true)}</div></div></main>`;\n  } else if (state.screen === 'hub') {\n    heading = 'AI HUB &nbsp; / &nbsp; GHOST CLASS';\n    content = `<main class=\"main-wrap narrow\"><div class=\"card dialogue\"><div class=\"eyebrow\">✳ &nbsp; THREE MINUTES TOGETHER</div><h1>${state.hub.finished ? 'Class complete.' : 'A little steadiness, shared.'}</h1><p>${state.hub.finished ? 'Your result has been sent to the Hub.' : 'Stork Stand, Step Class, and Quiet Candle. The steadiest practice wins; everyone gets a moment to breathe.'}</p><div class=\"result-stats\"><div><strong>${Math.round(state.hub.score)}</strong><small>POINTS</small></div></div><p class=\"note\">${state.hub.started ? 'The class is underway.' : 'Waiting for the other guests…'}</p></div></main>`;\n  }\n  app.innerHTML = shell(content, heading, state.screen !== 'play' && state.screen !== 'check');\n  if (state.screen === 'play') updateHUD();\n  if (state.screen === 'check') updateCheckHUD();\n  const touchOnly = matchMedia('(pointer: coarse)').matches && !Array.from(navigator.getGamepads?.() || []).some(Boolean);\n  if (touchOnly && !['settings','about'].includes(state.screen)) {\n    const notice = document.createElement('div'); notice.className = 'touch-notice'; notice.innerHTML = '<div><span>✳</span><h2>Controller or keyboard required</h2><p>Connect a controller or keyboard to enjoy the island.</p><button class=\"action primary\" data-action=\"settings\">Settings <span class=\"arrow\">↗</span></button></div>'; app.appendChild(notice);\n  }\n}\nfunction currentButtons() { return [...app.querySelectorAll('button:not([disabled])')].filter(node => node.offsetParent !== null && !node.closest('.touch-notice')); }\nfunction focusMove(direction) {\n  const buttons = currentButtons(); if (!buttons.length) return;\n  const index = buttons.indexOf(document.activeElement); buttons[(index + direction + buttons.length) % buttons.length].focus();\n}\nfunction memberDefault() { return { name: 'Guest', day: 1, sessions: 0, minutes: 0, stars: {}, instructor: 'Birch', color: 1, outfit: 1, finished: false }; }\nfunction beginCheck() { state.check = { phase: 'still', elapsed: 0, directions: new Set(), spine: 25 + Math.floor(Math.random() * 25) }; state.activity = null; screen('check'); }\nfunction startActivity(activity, options = {}) {\n  const selected = { ...activity }, duration = options.seconds || selected.seconds;\n  state.selection = selected;\n  state.activity = { ...selected, seconds: duration, elapsed: 0, px: 0, py: 0, vx: 0, vy: 0, ux: 0, uy: 0, ringX: 0, ringY: 0, flame: .6, score: 0, samples: 0, stumbles: 0, stun: 0, effort: 0, reps: 0, beatHits: 0, lastBeat: -1, lastJog: '', jogHits: 0, hoopHits: 0, good: 0, tray: 0, lastDirection: 0, motions: 0, rng: seeded(841 + selected.name.length) };\n  mouseLean = null; keys.clear(); toggledBreath = false; screen('play');\n}\nfunction completeActivity() {\n  const activity = state.activity;\n  if (!activity) return;\n  const percent = Math.round(clamp(activity.score / Math.max(1, activity.samples) * 100, 0, 100));\n  const stars = percent >= 90 ? 3 : percent >= 65 ? 2 : percent >= 35 ? 1 : 0;\n  const minutes = Math.max(1, Math.round(activity.seconds / 60 * (1 + stars * .25)));\n  state.result = { percent, stars, minutes, stumbles: activity.stumbles, message: stars >= 2 ? 'You made the wobble look rather elegant.' : 'A little practice is still a lovely thing.' };\n  if (!state.hub.active && !state.classMode) { const member = state.member; member.sessions = (member.sessions || 0) + 1; member.minutes = (member.minutes || 0) + minutes; member.stars[activity.id] = Math.max(member.stars[activity.id] || 0, stars); save(); }\n  tone(523, .3); if (state.hub.active) { state.hub.score += percent * 10; screen('hub'); } else screen('result');\n}\nfunction attemptInput(key) {\n  const activity = state.activity;\n  if (!activity || state.screen !== 'play') return;\n  if (activity.kind === 'step') {\n    const directions = ['arrowleft','arrowup','arrowright','arrowdown'];\n    const aliases = { a:'arrowleft', w:'arrowup', d:'arrowright', s:'arrowdown' };\n    const direction = aliases[key] || key, beat = Math.round(activity.elapsed * 100 / 60), phase = Math.abs(activity.elapsed * 100 / 60 - beat);\n    if (direction === directions[(beat + 4) % 4] && phase < .34 && beat !== activity.lastBeat) { activity.beatHits++; activity.lastBeat = beat; tone(520, .08, .35); }\n  }\n  if (activity.kind === 'jog' && (key === 'j' || key === 'k') && key !== activity.lastJog) { activity.lastJog = key; activity.jogHits++; }\n  if (activity.kind === 'hoop' && (key === 'q' || key === 'e')) { activity.hoopHits++; tone(660, .1, .3); }\n  if ((key === ' ' || key === 'enter') && state.settings.breathToggle) toggledBreath = !toggledBreath;\n}\nconst tuningDefaults = { spring: 11, damping: 6, instability: 1.3, noise: .19 };\nconst tuning = { ...tuningDefaults };\nfunction updateActivity(dt) {\n  const activity = state.activity; if (!activity) return;\n  activity.elapsed += dt;\n  const pad = Array.from(navigator.getGamepads?.() || []).find(Boolean), axisX = pad && Math.abs(pad.axes[0]) > .12 ? pad.axes[0] : 0, axisY = pad && Math.abs(pad.axes[1]) > .12 ? pad.axes[1] : 0;\n  const dx = (keys.has('arrowright') || keys.has('d') ? 1 : 0) - (keys.has('arrowleft') || keys.has('a') ? 1 : 0);\n  const dy = (keys.has('arrowdown') || keys.has('s') ? 1 : 0) - (keys.has('arrowup') || keys.has('w') ? 1 : 0);\n  if (activity.stun <= 0) {\n    if (mouseLean) { activity.ux = mouseLean.x; activity.uy = mouseLean.y; }\n    else if (axisX || axisY) { activity.ux = axisX; activity.uy = axisY; }\n    else { activity.ux = clamp(activity.ux + dx * 2.2 * dt, -1, 1); activity.uy = clamp(activity.uy + dy * 2.2 * dt, -1, 1); if (!dx) activity.ux *= Math.max(0, 1 - .5 * dt); if (!dy) activity.uy *= Math.max(0, 1 - .5 * dt); }\n  } else activity.stun -= dt;\n  const gentle = state.settings.gentle ? .7 : 1, time = activity.elapsed, disturbance = tuning.noise * gentle;\n  const ax = tuning.spring * (activity.ux - activity.px) - tuning.damping * activity.vx + tuning.instability * gentle * activity.px + disturbance * (Math.sin(time * 1.7) + .5 * Math.sin(time * 3.23));\n  const ay = tuning.spring * (activity.uy - activity.py) - tuning.damping * activity.vy + tuning.instability * gentle * activity.py + disturbance * (Math.sin(time * 1.19 + 1) + .5 * Math.sin(time * 2.71));\n  activity.vx += ax * dt; activity.vy += ay * dt; activity.px += activity.vx * dt; activity.py += activity.vy * dt;\n  if (Math.hypot(activity.px, activity.py) >= 1 && activity.stun <= 0) { activity.stumbles++; activity.stun = 1; activity.px *= .5; activity.py *= .5; activity.vx *= -.2; activity.vy *= -.2; tone(196, .18); }\n  const phase = Math.floor(time / 12), rng = seeded(phase * 667 + 43);\n  activity.ringX = activity.id === 'stork' ? (rng() - .5) * .65 : activity.kind === 'slalom' ? Math.sin(time * .55) * .46 : 0;\n  activity.ringY = activity.id === 'stork' ? (rng() - .5) * .35 : 0;\n  const distance = Math.hypot(activity.px - activity.ringX, activity.py - activity.ringY), ringSize = state.settings.gentle ? .48 : .38;\n  const steadiness = clamp(1 - distance * 1.4, 0, 1);\n  let quality = steadiness;\n  const held = state.settings.breathToggle ? toggledBreath : keys.has(' ') || !!pad?.buttons[7]?.pressed;\n  activity.effort = clamp(activity.effort + (held ? 1 : -1) * dt / 4, 0, 1);\n  if (activity.kind === 'rep') { const goal = (Math.sin(time * Math.PI / 2 - Math.PI / 2) + 1) / 2; quality = clamp(1 - Math.abs(activity.effort - goal), 0, 1) * steadiness; activity.reps = Math.floor(time / 4); }\n  if (activity.kind === 'breath') { const inhale = Math.sin(time * Math.PI / 4) > 0; quality = steadiness * (held === inhale ? 1 : .5); }\n  if (activity.kind === 'step') quality = clamp(activity.beatHits / Math.max(1, time * 100 / 60) * 1.5, 0, 1);\n  if (activity.kind === 'hoop') { activity.motions += (Math.abs(activity.vx) + Math.abs(activity.vy)) * dt; quality = clamp(activity.motions / Math.max(1, time) * 3 + activity.hoopHits / Math.max(1, time / 10), 0, 1); }\n  if (activity.kind === 'jog') quality = clamp(activity.jogHits / Math.max(1, time * 2) * 1.5, 0, 1) * steadiness;\n  if (activity.kind === 'slalom') quality = clamp(1 - Math.abs(activity.px - activity.ringX) * 1.5, 0, 1);\n  if (activity.kind === 'tray') { activity.tray += (activity.px - activity.tray) * dt * 1.5; quality = clamp(1 - Math.abs(activity.tray) * 2, 0, 1); }\n  if (activity.kind === 'rope') quality = clamp(1 - Math.abs(activity.px) * 2, 0, 1) * (activity.uy < -.1 ? 1 : .65);\n  if (activity.kind === 'candle') { activity.flame = clamp(activity.flame + (distance < ringSize ? .13 : -.3) * dt, 0, 1); quality = activity.flame; }\n  activity.score += quality; activity.samples++;\n  if (state.hub.active) {\n    const now = window.AIHub.time();\n    if (now - state.hub.lastSend >= 100) { state.hub.lastSend = now; window.AIHub.send({ x: activity.px, y: activity.py, exercise: activity.id }); }\n    if (now - state.hub.lastProgress >= 1000) { state.hub.lastProgress = now; window.AIHub.progress({ score: Math.round(state.hub.score + activity.score / Math.max(1, activity.samples) * 1000), label: activity.name }); }\n  }\n  if (activity.elapsed >= activity.seconds) completeActivity();\n}\nfunction updateHUD() {\n  const activity = state.activity; if (!activity) return;\n  const timer = document.getElementById('play-timer'), status = document.getElementById('play-status'), instruction = document.getElementById('play-instruction'), progress = document.getElementById('play-progress'), dot = document.getElementById('plate-dot'), ring = document.getElementById('plate-ring'), score = document.getElementById('play-score');\n  if (!timer) return;\n  timer.textContent = Math.max(0, Math.ceil(activity.seconds - activity.elapsed));\n  if (activity.kind === 'step') { const arrows = ['←','↑','→','↓']; const beat = Math.round(activity.elapsed * 100 / 60); status.textContent = `NEXT STEP  ${arrows[(beat + 4) % 4]}   ·   ${activity.beatHits} on beat`; instruction.textContent = `Press ${arrows[(beat + 4) % 4]} on the beat · ${activity.instruction}`; }\n  else if (activity.kind === 'rep') status.textContent = `Rep ${activity.reps + 1} · ${Math.sin(activity.elapsed * Math.PI / 2 - Math.PI / 2) > 0 ? 'Rise gently' : 'Lower gently'}`;\n  else if (activity.kind === 'breath') status.textContent = Math.sin(activity.elapsed * Math.PI / 4) > 0 ? 'Breathe in · hold' : 'Breathe out · release';\n  else if (activity.kind === 'candle') status.textContent = `Flame ${Math.round(activity.flame * 100)}% · ${activity.flame < .15 ? 'settle to relight' : 'let it glow'}`;\n  else if (activity.kind === 'jog') status.textContent = `${activity.jogHits} steps · alternate J and K`;\n  else if (activity.kind === 'hoop') status.textContent = `${activity.hoopHits} catches · circle your lean`;\n  else status.textContent = activity.stun > 0 ? 'A wobble! Take a moment.' : 'Find the ring. Breathe naturally.';\n  progress.style.width = `${clamp(activity.elapsed / activity.seconds * 100, 0, 100)}%`;\n  dot.style.transform = `translate(${activity.px * 70}px, ${activity.py * 70}px)`;\n  ring.style.transform = `translate(${activity.ringX * 70}px, ${activity.ringY * 70}px)`;\n  score.textContent = `${Math.round(activity.score / Math.max(1, activity.samples) * 100)}% STEADY`;\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_139","type":"reasoning","text":"**Inspecting focused file chunks**"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_140","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '452,487p' PLAN.md; sed -n '1,240p' 'Wee Bit of Zen-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221356/vendor/mocap.js' | head -100; rg -n 'function (render|startActivity|completeActivity|updateActivity|pollGamepad|action|drawPerson)|case .(class|hub|outfit|instructor|create-member)|AIHub|__ZEN' 'Wee Bit of Zen-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221356/src/'{game,art}.js\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_140","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '452,487p' PLAN.md; sed -n '1,240p' 'Wee Bit of Zen-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221356/vendor/mocap.js' | head -100; rg -n 'function (render|startActivity|completeActivity|updateActivity|pollGamepad|action|drawPerson)|case .(class|hub|outfit|instructor|create-member)|AIHub|__ZEN' 'Wee Bit of Zen-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221356/src/'{game,art}.js\"","aggregated_output":"## 14. Multiplayer\n\n**Class (local, on its own, 2 to 4).** From the title: join with Start on a free pad or 2 on the keyboard (`game.allowJoin({ max: 4, onJoin })`; `game.players[i]` has the same input API; keyboard players get `E.Input.halfKeys`). ✔ Half a keyboard runs out of keys with the full `INPUT` (the step and pace actions get none), so the Class scene sets its own `input`: the moves and menu actions plus `breath`, `catchL`, `catchR` only (left half F G H, right half `. / ,`), and its Step Class reads `lanes: ['left', 'down', 'up', 'right']`. Everyone gets a mat, a colour (`E.PLAYER_COLORS`) and a pre-made rig, on one fixed screen at size 1.5 with a small Plate under each. Activities: Stork Stand, Quiet Candle, Squat Rail, Step Class (two lanes), Hoop Hips, 35 s each, or \"Surprise me\" (3 rounds). So every class-capable activity takes a list of **contestants** from the start, not one player. Scores are 0 to 1000 (`round(pct × 1000)`). Results: podium with polite titles (Most Still, Best Wobble, Participated). Tare reads them. Empty mats hold Regulars driven by bots, for life, not for score.\n\n**AI Hub session (`ghost` mode, 1 to 4).** Follow the protocol README (`https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/README.md`); it is short, read it. Outside a session the game is unaffected and `connect()` answers `null`. ✔ This exact shape passed the harness at 1, 2, 3 and 4 players, on the bad network, and with the host leaving.\n\n**The round: \"Morning Class\".** Everyone plays the same 3 events on their own copy, in lockstep, seeing others as translucent seat-coloured ghosts on neighbouring mats (or in the world for Slalom and Jog). About 150 s: each event is 5 s intro + 40 s play + 5 s scores. Deal with `AIHub.rng('deal')`: one from Stork/Candle/Squat/Push-Up, one from Step/Hoop, one from Slalom/Jog.\n\n```js\nconst inSession = !!(window.AIHub && AIHub.active);\nconst game = new E.Game({ canvas: 'screen', id: 'GAMEID', res: 'ps1', expand: true, touch: 'never', input: INPUT,\n  autoPause: !inSession, live: inSession, fullscreen: inSession ? false : 'button',\n  menu: { quit: inSession ? false : 'title', items: inSession ? [] : [/* Restart, Dev Mode */], settings: [/* section 11 */] } });\ngame.start({ scenes, scene: inSession ? 'round' : 'title', boot: {/* steps */} });\nif (inSession) (async () => {\n  const info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'ghost', seats: [1, 4], card: true });\n  if (!info) return game.go('title');\n  AIHub.on('card', c => { card = c; });\n  AIHub.on('start', () => {});\n  AIHub.on('message', (d, from) => { /* ghost state */ });\n  AIHub.on('leave', ({ id }) => { /* remove that ghost */ });\n  AIHub.on('time-up', () => report());                  // result() at once if not reported\n  AIHub.on('end', () => { over = true; game.audio.stopMusic(); game.audio.mute(true); game.input.clear(); });\n  await game.booted; AIHub.ready();                     // no key press\n})();\n```\n\n- **Card (yours, `card: true`):** the studio with the players lined up on mats, Tare hopping, the title, each player's name and colour with a ready tick, how to win, this player's controls, seconds left. While `AIHub.time() === -Infinity`: `confirm` or `start` → `AIHub.answer('ready')`, `more` (△) → `AIHub.answer('more')`, clicks on Ready/More too. No menus or choices on the card. Show \"More time\" state from the `card` event (`asked`, `paused`).\n- **Clock:** all event timing comes from `AIHub.time()`, not `game.time`. A frame over 50 ms gives up its time, so a slow machine's game clock lags and would desync. Countdown while negative. Play at ≥ 0. If `info.limitMs` is shorter than the round, shrink the events.\n- **Randomness:** every activity takes its disturbances from `AIHub.rng('e' + eventIndex)` (and a seeded `E.rng` offline). `Math.random` is only for cosmetics like particles and blinks, because copies draw it at different rates.\n- **Ghost data:** `AIHub.send({ t: 'g', a: eventIndex, l: [x, y], p: phase, w: [wx, wy], s: score }, { reliable: false })` about 10 times a second. Draw only if `a` matches your current event. `r.actor(..., { alpha: .5 })`, name tag in seat colour. Names come from `info.players`, drawn with `E.font` only (never HTML). Limit: 20 messages/s.\n- **Reporting:** `AIHub.progress({ score: total, label: total + ' pts' })` about once a second; at the end `AIHub.result({ score: total, stats: { Steadiness: '84%' }, awards: [{ title: 'Most Still', detail: '...' }] })` once.\n- **In a session:** no title, attract, dev, quit, restart or saved progress. Options opens the settings over the running round (`live`). No chat, emotes or custom names. No other network. Engine already ignores Options while Create is held ✔.\n\n**Head tags (`build.mjs` writes them), in this order ✔:**\n\n/* =============================================================================\n * MOCAP  plays animation sets in the readable format (src/mocap/readable.js; written by tools/anim-import.mjs) on\n * my-3D2dge rigs.\n *   const lib = Mocap.load(window.MOCAP.QUATERNIUS);   // a set: its clips, and the bodies they were measured on\n *   const clip = lib.clip('Dance_Loop');               // { name, dur, loop, tags, desc, keys }\n *   const pose = lib.sample(clip, t);                  // Float32Array: every body point's f r z (mm), in-betweened\n *   const man = new Mocap.Mannequin(lib, { height: 34 });  man.draw(g, ox, oy, view, pose, facing)\n *   Mocap.drive(humanoid, lib)  then each step  humanoid.mocap = pose: the rig plays it at its own build. (Mocap is also\n *     window.Mocap.)\n *     humanoid.mocapW (0..1) fades it in and out over the rig's own animation; humanoid.mocapMask = 'upper' plays\n *     only the chest, head and arms over the rig's own legs (an interaction while walking); humanoid.mocapBlade = true\n *     while the clip holds a sword (the blade follows the fist).\n * Points are in the rig's local frame: f = forward, r = right, z = up, centred on the root on the ground.\n * ============================================================================= */\nconst Mocap = (() => {\n'use strict';\nconst E = My3D2dge, { px } = E, MR = MocapReadable;\n\n/* ---- sets ---- */\n/**\n * Every clip is rebuilt on the first library's proportions (the format does not depend on size); each keeps how its own\n * library bends the spine, since the key poses were measured that way.\n */\nfunction load(set) {\n  const P = MR.P, idx = MR.IDX, ids = Object.keys(set.sources), base = set.sources[ids[0]].rest, rests = {};\n  for (const id of ids) rests[id] = Object.assign({}, base, { spineW: set.sources[id].rest.spineW, neckW: set.sources[id].rest.neckW });\n  const meta = c => ({ name: c.clip, fps: set.fps, n: Math.round(c.dur * set.fps) + 1 }), clips = {};\n  for (const [name, c] of Object.entries(set.clips)) clips[name] = Object.assign(meta(Object.assign({ clip: name }, c)), c);\n  const restOf = c => rests[c.src] || base;\n  const lib = { set, P, idx, clips, names: Object.keys(clips), fps: set.fps, body: set.body, rest: base, points: MR.POINTS };\n  lib.clip = name => clips[name] || null;\n  /** the pose at time t (seconds): key poses in-betweened, loops wrap, one-shots hold their last pose */\n  lib.sample = (clip, t, out = new Float32Array(P * 3)) => { MR.pose(restOf(clip), clip, t, out); out.src = clip.src; return out; };   // (src: whose rest it is measured against)\n  /** a clip that travels: how far it has carried the body at time t ([forward, right] mm), or null */\n  lib.moveAt = (clip, t) => MR.moveAt(restOf(clip), clip, t);\n  /** swap in an edited clip (readable text a person or a model changed); the original is kept for restore() */\n  const originals = {};\n  lib.replace = (name, edited) => { if (!originals[name]) originals[name] = clips[name]; clips[name] = Object.assign({}, originals[name], edited, { name, keys: edited.keys }); return clips[name]; };\n  lib.restore = name => { if (originals[name]) { clips[name] = originals[name]; delete originals[name]; } return clips[name]; };\n  lib.edited = name => !!originals[name];\n  /** the clip as the text a model reads (its header and its key poses) */\n  lib.text = clip => { const o = { clip: clip.clip || clip.name }; for (const k of ['src', 'take', 'orig', 'dur', 'loop', 'tags', 'desc']) if (clip[k] !== undefined) o[k] = clip[k]; o.keys = clip.keys; return MR.text(o); };\n  /** where a clip came from: its library's label, origin and license (from the set's sources), the clip it was made from,\n   *  and (a capture database's) the take and the stretch of it: '13_29 2.30-3.42' */\n  lib.origin = clip => { const s = set.sources[clip.src] || {}; return { src: clip.src, label: s.label || clip.src, origin: s.origin || '', license: s.license || '', url: s.url || '', orig: clip.orig || null, take: clip.take || null }; };\n  /** a pose blended from a to b (crossfades between clips) */\n  lib.blend = (a, b, k, out = new Float32Array(P * 3)) => { for (let i = 0; i < P * 3; i++) out[i] = a[i] + (b[i] - a[i]) * k; out.src = (k < .5 ? a : b).src; return out; };\n  lib.pt = (pose, name) => { const i = idx[name] * 3; return [pose[i], pose[i + 1], pose[i + 2]]; };\n  lib.error = MR.error;\n  return lib;\n}\n\n/* ---- the look-alike mannequin: shaded capsules in the source model's proportions, with its joint bands ---- */\nconst lerp3 = (a, b, t) => [a[0] + (b[0] - a[0]) * t, a[1] + (b[1] - a[1]) * t, a[2] + (b[2] - a[2]) * t];\nconst add3 = (a, b, k = 1) => [a[0] + b[0] * k, a[1] + b[1] * k, a[2] + b[2] * k];\nconst sub3 = (a, b) => [a[0] - b[0], a[1] - b[1], a[2] - b[2]];\nconst norm3 = a => { const l = Math.hypot(a[0], a[1], a[2]) || 1; return [a[0] / l, a[1] / l, a[2] / l]; };\nclass Mannequin {\n  /** o: { height: world units tall (34), main: '#e8aa3a', joint: '#aa66db' } (the colors of the source model's two materials) */\n  constructor(lib, o = {}) {\n    this.lib = lib; this.o = Object.assign({ height: 34, main: '#e8aa3a', joint: '#aa66db' }, o);\n    this.k = this.o.height / ((lib.body && lib.body.height) || 1829);   // world units per mm\n    this._ops = [];\n  }\n  /**\n   * draw the pose into g with (ox, oy) = the projected root. Every part is a capsule between two body points,\n   * sorted by true camera depth, drawn dark-then-lit like the engine's HD rigs.\n   */\n  draw(g, ox, oy, view, pose, facing = 0) {\n    const L = this.lib, o = this.o, k = this.k, ca = Math.cos(facing), sa = Math.sin(facing), sc = view.scale;\n    const pt = name => L.pt(pose, name);\n    const S = p => { const wx = (p[0] * ca - p[1] * sa) * k, wy = (p[0] * sa + p[1] * ca) * k, wz = p[2] * k; return [ox + view.ax * wx + view.ay * wy, oy + view.bx * wx + view.by * wy + view.bz * wz, view.dx * wx + view.dy * wy + view.dz * wz]; };\n    const R = mm => mm * k * sc;   // a radius in mm -> screen pixels\n    const ops = this._ops; ops.length = 0;\n    const main = E.tones(o.main), joint = E.tones(o.joint);\n    // centre depth of the body: parts behind it are drawn a touch darker (the far arm and leg)\n    const mid = S(pt('spine1'))[2];\n    const capsule = (A, B, ra, rb, col, dx = 0, dy = 0) => {\n      const ax = A[0] + dx, ay = A[1] + dy, bx = B[0] + dx, by = B[1] + dy, vx = bx - ax, vy = by - ay, l = Math.hypot(vx, vy);\n      if (l > .01) { const nx = -vy / l, ny = vx / l; px.poly(g, [[ax + nx * ra, ay + ny * ra], [bx + nx * rb, by + ny * rb], [bx - nx * rb, by - ny * rb], [ax - nx * ra, ay - ny * ra]], col); }\n      px.disc(g, ax, ay, Math.max(.5, ra - .3), col); px.disc(g, bx, by, Math.max(.5, rb - .3), col);\n    };\n    // a shaded part: dark silhouette, the base color shifted toward the light (upper left), a soft highlight\n    const part = (a, b, ra, rb, T, bias = 0) => {\n      const A = S(a), B = S(b), pa = R(ra), pb = R(rb), far = (A[2] + B[2]) * .5 < mid - 2 * k * 60;\n      ops.push({ d: (A[2] + B[2]) * .5 + bias, f: () => {\n        capsule(A, B, pa, pb, far ? T.deep : T.sh);\n        capsule(A, B, Math.max(.5, pa - .9), Math.max(.5, pb - .9), far ? T.sh : T.base, -.5, -.6);\n        if (pa > 2.2 && !far) capsule(A, B, pa * .32, pb * .32, T.lt, -pa * .38, -pa * .42);\n      } });\n    };\n    // a ring painted round a limb (the second material): a straight-edged stripe across the capsule, no round ends,\n    // so a thin band reads as a band from every side. Seen end-on (the limb points at the camera) it is hidden.\n    const band = (a, b, t0, t1, ra, rb, T) => {\n      const A = S(lerp3(a, b, t0)), B = S(lerp3(a, b, t1)), axis = S(a), end = S(b), vx = end[0] - axis[0], vy = end[1] - axis[1], l = Math.hypot(vx, vy);\n      if (l < R(Math.max(ra, rb)) * .5) return;\n      const nx = -vy / l, ny = vx / l, wa = R(ra + (rb - ra) * t0) + .2, wb = R(ra + (rb - ra) * t1) + .2;\n      ops.push({ d: (axis[2] + end[2]) * .5 + .02, f: () => {\n        const q = (w0, w1, dx, dy) => [[A[0] + nx * w0 + dx, A[1] + ny * w0 + dy], [B[0] + nx * w1 + dx, B[1] + ny * w1 + dy], [B[0] - nx * w1 + dx, B[1] - ny * w1 + dy], [A[0] - nx * w0 + dx, A[1] - ny * w0 + dy]];\n        px.poly(g, q(wa, wb, 0, 0), T.sh); px.poly(g, q(Math.max(.5, wa - .9), Math.max(.5, wb - .9), -.5, -.6), T.base);\nWee Bit of Zen-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221356/src/art.js:61:function drawPerson(x, ground, size, options = {}) {\nWee Bit of Zen-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221356/src/game.js:12:  festival: false, festivalIndex: 0, hub: { active: !!window.AIHub?.active, started: false, finished: false, score: 0, lastSend: 0, lastProgress: 0, ghosts: {} }\nWee Bit of Zen-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221356/src/game.js:68:function render() {\nWee Bit of Zen-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221356/src/game.js:153:function startActivity(activity, options = {}) {\nWee Bit of Zen-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221356/src/game.js:159:function completeActivity() {\nWee Bit of Zen-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221356/src/game.js:184:function updateActivity(dt) {\nWee Bit of Zen-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221356/src/game.js:219:    const now = window.AIHub.time();\nWee Bit of Zen-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221356/src/game.js:220:    if (now - state.hub.lastSend >= 100) { state.hub.lastSend = now; window.AIHub.send({ x: activity.px, y: activity.py, exercise: activity.id }); }\nWee Bit of Zen-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221356/src/game.js:221:    if (now - state.hub.lastProgress >= 1000) { state.hub.lastProgress = now; window.AIHub.progress({ score: Math.round(state.hub.score + activity.score / Math.max(1, activity.samples) * 1000), label: activity.name }); }\nWee Bit of Zen-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221356/src/game.js:256:function action(name, id) {\nWee Bit of Zen-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221356/src/game.js:262:    case 'outfit': state.member.outfit = Number(id); render(); break;\nWee Bit of Zen-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221356/src/game.js:263:    case 'instructor': state.member.instructor = id; render(); break;\nWee Bit of Zen-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221356/src/game.js:264:    case 'create-member': { const value = document.getElementById('nickname')?.value.trim(); state.member.name = (value || 'Guest').slice(0, 16); save(); screen('intro'); break; }\nWee Bit of Zen-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221356/src/game.js:278:    case 'class': state.classMode = true; if (!state.classPlayers.length) state.classPlayers = [{ name: state.member?.name || 'Player 1', type: 'Keyboard / pad' }, { name: 'Gertrude', type: 'Bot' }]; state.selection = state.selection || ACTIVITIES[0]; screen('class'); break;\nWee Bit of Zen-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221356/src/game.js:279:    case 'class-toggle': { const index = Number(id); if (index === 0) break; state.classPlayers[index] = state.classPlayers[index] ? null : { name: ['Player 1','Gertrude','Dennis','Marisol'][index], type: 'Bot' }; render(); break; }\nWee Bit of Zen-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221356/src/game.js:280:    case 'class-activity': state.selection = ACTIVITIES.find(activity => activity.id === id); render(); break;\nWee Bit of Zen-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221356/src/game.js:317:function pollGamepad() {\nWee Bit of Zen-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221356/src/game.js:345:window.__ZEN = {\nWee Bit of Zen-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221356/src/game.js:354:  window.AIHub.on('start', () => { state.hub.started = true; state.hub.startedAt = window.AIHub.time(); startActivity(ACTIVITIES.find(activity => activity.id === 'stork'), { seconds: 60 }); });\nWee Bit of Zen-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221356/src/game.js:355:  window.AIHub.on('message', (data, from) => { state.hub.ghosts[from] = data; });\nWee Bit of Zen-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221356/src/game.js:356:  window.AIHub.on('time-up', () => { if (!state.hub.finished) { state.hub.finished = true; if (state.activity && state.screen === 'play') state.hub.score += state.activity.score / Math.max(1, state.activity.samples) * 1000; window.AIHub.result({ score: Math.round(state.hub.score) }); screen('hub'); } });\nWee Bit of Zen-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221356/src/game.js:357:  window.AIHub.on('end', () => { state.hub.finished = true; screen('hub'); });\nWee Bit of Zen-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221356/src/game.js:358:  window.AIHub.connect({ mode: 'ghost', seats: [1, 4], card: true }).then(() => window.AIHub.ready()).catch(() => notify('Unable to connect to the Hub.'));\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
