{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_165","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"D='Wee Bit of Zen-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221356'; sed -n '450,495p' PLAN.md; rg -n 'rng|answer|connect:|ready:|time:|progress:|probe|card:|on:' \\\"\"'$D/vendor/session.js\"; sed -n '\"'1,145p' \\\"\"'$D/tests/hub/harness.html\" | head -85; sed -n '\"'1,125p' \\\"\"'$D/tests/hub/round.js\"'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_165","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"D='Wee Bit of Zen-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221356'; sed -n '450,495p' PLAN.md; rg -n 'rng|answer|connect:|ready:|time:|progress:|probe|card:|on:' \\\"\"'$D/vendor/session.js\"; sed -n '\"'1,145p' \\\"\"'$D/tests/hub/harness.html\" | head -85; sed -n '\"'1,125p' \\\"\"'$D/tests/hub/round.js\"'","aggregated_output":"---\n\n## 14. Multiplayer\n\n**Class (local, on its own, 2 to 4).** From the title: join with Start on a free pad or 2 on the keyboard (`game.allowJoin({ max: 4, onJoin })`; `game.players[i]` has the same input API; keyboard players get `E.Input.halfKeys`). ✔ Half a keyboard runs out of keys with the full `INPUT` (the step and pace actions get none), so the Class scene sets its own `input`: the moves and menu actions plus `breath`, `catchL`, `catchR` only (left half F G H, right half `. / ,`), and its Step Class reads `lanes: ['left', 'down', 'up', 'right']`. Everyone gets a mat, a colour (`E.PLAYER_COLORS`) and a pre-made rig, on one fixed screen at size 1.5 with a small Plate under each. Activities: Stork Stand, Quiet Candle, Squat Rail, Step Class (two lanes), Hoop Hips, 35 s each, or \"Surprise me\" (3 rounds). So every class-capable activity takes a list of **contestants** from the start, not one player. Scores are 0 to 1000 (`round(pct × 1000)`). Results: podium with polite titles (Most Still, Best Wobble, Participated). Tare reads them. Empty mats hold Regulars driven by bots, for life, not for score.\n\n**AI Hub session (`ghost` mode, 1 to 4).** Follow the protocol README (`https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/README.md`); it is short, read it. Outside a session the game is unaffected and `connect()` answers `null`. ✔ This exact shape passed the harness at 1, 2, 3 and 4 players, on the bad network, and with the host leaving.\n\n**The round: \"Morning Class\".** Everyone plays the same 3 events on their own copy, in lockstep, seeing others as translucent seat-coloured ghosts on neighbouring mats (or in the world for Slalom and Jog). About 150 s: each event is 5 s intro + 40 s play + 5 s scores. Deal with `AIHub.rng('deal')`: one from Stork/Candle/Squat/Push-Up, one from Step/Hoop, one from Slalom/Jog.\n\n```js\nconst inSession = !!(window.AIHub && AIHub.active);\nconst game = new E.Game({ canvas: 'screen', id: 'GAMEID', res: 'ps1', expand: true, touch: 'never', input: INPUT,\n  autoPause: !inSession, live: inSession, fullscreen: inSession ? false : 'button',\n  menu: { quit: inSession ? false : 'title', items: inSession ? [] : [/* Restart, Dev Mode */], settings: [/* section 11 */] } });\ngame.start({ scenes, scene: inSession ? 'round' : 'title', boot: {/* steps */} });\nif (inSession) (async () => {\n  const info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'ghost', seats: [1, 4], card: true });\n  if (!info) return game.go('title');\n  AIHub.on('card', c => { card = c; });\n  AIHub.on('start', () => {});\n  AIHub.on('message', (d, from) => { /* ghost state */ });\n  AIHub.on('leave', ({ id }) => { /* remove that ghost */ });\n  AIHub.on('time-up', () => report());                  // result() at once if not reported\n  AIHub.on('end', () => { over = true; game.audio.stopMusic(); game.audio.mute(true); game.input.clear(); });\n  await game.booted; AIHub.ready();                     // no key press\n})();\n```\n\n- **Card (yours, `card: true`):** the studio with the players lined up on mats, Tare hopping, the title, each player's name and colour with a ready tick, how to win, this player's controls, seconds left. While `AIHub.time() === -Infinity`: `confirm` or `start` → `AIHub.answer('ready')`, `more` (△) → `AIHub.answer('more')`, clicks on Ready/More too. No menus or choices on the card. Show \"More time\" state from the `card` event (`asked`, `paused`).\n- **Clock:** all event timing comes from `AIHub.time()`, not `game.time`. A frame over 50 ms gives up its time, so a slow machine's game clock lags and would desync. Countdown while negative. Play at ≥ 0. If `info.limitMs` is shorter than the round, shrink the events.\n- **Randomness:** every activity takes its disturbances from `AIHub.rng('e' + eventIndex)` (and a seeded `E.rng` offline). `Math.random` is only for cosmetics like particles and blinks, because copies draw it at different rates.\n- **Ghost data:** `AIHub.send({ t: 'g', a: eventIndex, l: [x, y], p: phase, w: [wx, wy], s: score }, { reliable: false })` about 10 times a second. Draw only if `a` matches your current event. `r.actor(..., { alpha: .5 })`, name tag in seat colour. Names come from `info.players`, drawn with `E.font` only (never HTML). Limit: 20 messages/s.\n- **Reporting:** `AIHub.progress({ score: total, label: total + ' pts' })` about once a second; at the end `AIHub.result({ score: total, stats: { Steadiness: '84%' }, awards: [{ title: 'Most Still', detail: '...' }] })` once.\n- **In a session:** no title, attract, dev, quit, restart or saved progress. Options opens the settings over the running round (`live`). No chat, emotes or custom names. No other network. Engine already ignores Options while Create is held ✔.\n\n**Head tags (`build.mjs` writes them), in this order ✔:**\n\n```html\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<script>/* vendor/session.js, unmodified, first script in head */</script>\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover\">\n<title>THE TITLE — a tagline</title>\n<meta name=\"description\" content=\"one or two sentences\">\n<meta name=\"theme-color\" content=\"#2cc6e6\">\n<meta name=\"hub:type\" content=\"Game\"><meta name=\"hub:players\" content=\"1–4\"><meta name=\"hub:source\" content=\"Wii Fit\">\n24:    version: VERSION,\n36:    /** True when the hub shows the round's splash and collects every player's ready: call ready() once loaded, with no prompt. */\n132:        post('fullscreen', { on: on });\n170:  var probeFn = null;\n188:  var KEEP = { aihub: 1, type: 1, version: 1, protocol: 1, active: 1, seeded: 1 };\n268:      emit('leave', [{ id: m.id, reason: m.reason }]);\n274:      emit('end', [{ reason: m.reason, standings: m.standings || null }]);\n309:        warn('no hub answered; playing normally');\n313:      post('hello', { v: 1, client: VERSION, mode: opts.mode || null, seats: opts.seats || null, card: opts.card === true });\n327:  /** On the game's own card (connect({ card: true })): this player is 'ready', or asks for 'more' time (again takes it back). */\n328:  hub.answer = function (what) {\n330:    if (what !== 'ready' && what !== 'more') return warn('answer is ready or more');\n331:    post('answer', { answer: what });\n387:  hub.rng = function (label) {\n422:  /** Race and side by side: report your own outcome once, {time: ms} (lower wins) or {score: n} (higher wins), with optional stats and awards. */\n467:  /** For the harness, in or out of a session: fn() → { scene, menu, world, input }, read with inspect(). */\n468:  hub.probe = function (fn) {\n469:    probeFn = typeof fn === 'function' ? fn : null;\n473:    if (!probeFn) return null;\n475:      return JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(probeFn()));\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n<title>AI Hub Session Harness</title>\n<meta name=\"description\" content=\"Test a game against the AI Hub Session Protocol: 1–4 copies next to each other on a simulated network.\">\n<style>\n  :root { color-scheme: dark; --bg: #0e0c14; --panel: #191623; --line: #2c2838; --ink: #ece8f4; --dim: #9a93ab; --ok: #4ade80; --bad: #f87171; --warn: #fbbf24; }\n  * { box-sizing: border-box; }\n  html, body { margin: 0; height: 100%; background: var(--bg); color: var(--ink); font: 14px/1.4 system-ui, sans-serif; }\n  body { display: grid; grid-template-rows: auto 1fr; }\n  header { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px 14px; align-items: center; padding: 8px 12px; background: var(--panel); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }\n  header h1 { font-size: 15px; margin: 0 8px 0 0; }\n  header label { color: var(--dim); display: inline-flex; gap: 6px; align-items: center; }\n  input, select, button { font: inherit; color: var(--ink); background: #241f31; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 6px; padding: 4px 8px; }\n  input[type=number] { width: 70px; }\n  input.game { width: 300px; }\n  button { cursor: pointer; }\n  button:hover { border-color: var(--dim); }\n  main { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 340px; min-height: 0; }\n  #grid { display: grid; gap: 6px; padding: 6px; min-height: 0; }\n  .cell { position: relative; display: grid; grid-template-rows: auto 1fr; min-height: 0; border: 2px solid var(--line); border-radius: 8px; overflow: hidden; background: #000; }\n  .cell__bar { display: flex; gap: 8px; align-items: center; padding: 3px 8px; background: var(--panel); font-size: 12px; }\n  .cell__dot { width: 10px; height: 10px; border-radius: 50%; }\n  .cell__state { margin-left: auto; color: var(--dim); }\n  .cell iframe { width: 100%; height: 100%; border: 0; background: #000; }\n  .cell.is-out { opacity: .35; }\n  aside { display: grid; grid-template-rows: auto auto 1fr; min-height: 0; border-left: 1px solid var(--line); background: var(--panel); }\n  aside section { padding: 8px 12px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }\n  aside h2 { font-size: 12px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .06em; color: var(--dim); margin: 0 0 6px; }\n  #checks li { list-style: none; }\n  #checks ul { margin: 0; padding: 0; }\n  .ok::before { content: '✓ '; color: var(--ok); }\n  .bad::before { content: '✗ '; color: var(--bad); }\n  .wait::before { content: '… '; color: var(--warn); }\n  #log { overflow: auto; font: 12px/1.35 ui-monospace, monospace; padding: 8px 12px; margin: 0; white-space: pre-wrap; }\n  #round { white-space: pre-wrap; font-size: 13px; }\n  .hint { color: var(--dim); }\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<header>\n  <h1>AI Hub session harness</h1>\n  <label>Game <input class=\"game\" id=\"game\" placeholder=\"mygame.html or /games/mygame/index.html\"></label>\n  <label>Players <select id=\"players\"><option>1</option><option selected>2</option><option>3</option><option>4</option></select></label>\n  <label>Latency <input type=\"number\" id=\"latency\" min=\"0\" value=\"60\"> ms</label>\n  <label>Jitter <input type=\"number\" id=\"jitter\" min=\"0\" value=\"20\"> ms</label>\n  <label>Loss <input type=\"number\" id=\"loss\" min=\"0\" max=\"50\" value=\"0\"> %</label>\n  <button id=\"restart\" type=\"button\">New round</button>\n  <button id=\"release\" type=\"button\" title=\"End the splash now: the round starts once every game has loaded\">Start now</button>\n  <button id=\"timeup\" type=\"button\">Time up</button>\n  <label>Remove <select id=\"who\"></select></label>\n  <button id=\"remove\" type=\"button\">Remove player</button>\n  <button id=\"hide\" type=\"button\" aria-pressed=\"false\">Hide host tab</button>\n</header>\n<main>\n  <div id=\"grid\"><p class=\"hint\" style=\"padding:16px\">Name a game above (a path or URL served alongside this page), then press New round. Click a player's frame to control that player.</p></div>\n  <aside>\n    <section><h2>Round</h2><div id=\"round\" class=\"hint\">No round yet.</div></section>\n    <section id=\"checks\"><h2>Conformance</h2><ul id=\"checklist\"><li class=\"hint\">Run with <code>?auto=1</code> for the automatic checks.</li></ul></section>\n    <pre id=\"log\" aria-live=\"off\"></pre>\n  </aside>\n</main>\n<script type=\"module\">\nimport { createBridge, attachFrame, postTo, createLocalNetwork } from './bridge.js';\nimport { createRound, limitFor, modeOf, seedsRandom, SELF_REPORTED, TIMINGS } from './round.js';\n\nconst NAMES = ['Red Fox', 'Blue Otter', 'Green Heron', 'Gold Lynx'];\nconst params = new URLSearchParams(location.search);\nconst $ = (id) => document.getElementById(id);\nconst auto = params.get('auto') === '1';\nconst scenario = params.get('scenario') || 'standard';\n/** ?scenario=server: the shared world runs on one more copy with no player of its own, as a dedicated server would run it. */\nconst serverMode = scenario === 'server';\nconst playMs = Number(params.get('play')) || 6000;\nconst SPLASH_MS = 10_000;\n\nfor (const [id, key] of [['game', 'game'], ['players', 'players'], ['latency', 'latency'], ['jitter', 'jitter'], ['loss', 'loss']]) {\n  if (params.has(key)) $(id).value = params.get(key);\n}\n\nconst net = createLocalNetwork({});\nlet current = null;\nlet roundNo = 0;\n/**\n * round.js — one round of an AI Hub session, run by the hub that coordinates\n * it (the harness page, or the session host's tab).\n *\n * It never touches the network or a frame itself: every message for a game\n * goes out through `deliver(key, msg)`, and everything the games report comes\n * in through `receive(key, msg)` and `leave(key, reason)`. The clock is\n * injected, so `scripts/hub.test.mjs` can walk a round through every timeout\n * without waiting for one.\n *\n * Players are known by `key` (whatever the session calls them); games see\n * contiguous ids 0..N-1 in slot order.\n */\n\nexport const TIMINGS = Object.freeze({\n  helloMs: 10_000,\n  readyMs: 45_000,\n  /** Gated rounds: a game still loading when the hub releases the round gets this long more. */\n  loadGraceMs: 20_000,\n  countdownMs: 3_000,\n  graceMs: 5_000,\n  hiddenMs: 20_000,\n  maxRoundMs: 15 * 60_000,\n});\n\n/** P1 red, P2 blue, P3 green, P4 yellow: the colour follows the seat. */\nexport const SLOT_COLORS = Object.freeze(['#e8443a', '#3b82f6', '#22c55e', '#f5b700']);\n\nexport const MODES = Object.freeze(['parallel', 'ghost', 'shared-world']);\n\n/** Each mode's name on screen. */\nexport const MODE_NAMES = Object.freeze({ parallel: 'Parallel', ghost: 'Ghost', 'shared-world': 'Shared world' });\n\n/** Older tags, still played: race as ghost, co-op and versus as a shared world. */\nconst MODE_ALIASES = Object.freeze({ race: 'ghost', 'co-op': 'shared-world', versus: 'shared-world' });\n\n/** The mode a tag or a hello names, older tags included; null for anything else. */\nexport function modeOf(word) {\n  const w = String(word ?? '').trim().toLowerCase();\n  return MODES.includes(w) ? w : (MODE_ALIASES[w] ?? null);\n}\n\n/** Modes where every copy runs its own world: each reports its own result, and nothing depends on a host. */\nexport const SELF_REPORTED = Object.freeze(['parallel', 'ghost']);\n\n/**\n * Whether a game's round carries the seed in its address, so the client seeds\n * Math.random and every copy starts the same: read from the game's own tag,\n * parallel or ghost. A game still tagged race was built for an unseeded start\n * (ids it makes from Math.random must differ between its copies), so it keeps one.\n */\nexport const seedsRandom = (tag) => ['parallel', 'ghost'].includes(String(tag ?? '').trim().toLowerCase());\n\nconst REAL_CLOCK = {\n  now: () => Date.now(),\n  setTimeout: (fn, ms) => setTimeout(fn, ms),\n  clearTimeout: (handle) => clearTimeout(handle),\n};\n\n/** A round's hard cap: half again its declared length, never past 15 minutes; the longest when it declares none. */\nexport function limitFor(minutes, { maxRoundMs = TIMINGS.maxRoundMs } = {}) {\n  const typical = Number(minutes);\n  if (!(typical > 0)) return maxRoundMs;\n  return Math.min(maxRoundMs, Math.round(typical * 1.5 * 60_000));\n}\n\n/**\n * Parallel and ghost order: finishers by time, then the rest by score,\n * then anyone who reported nothing, tied last. Equal times or scores share a\n * place.\n */\nexport function rankResults(results, ids) {\n  const timed = [];\n  const scored = [];\n  const silent = [];\n  for (const id of ids) {\n    const r = results.get(id);\n    if (r && Number.isFinite(r.time)) timed.push([id, r.time]);\n    else if (r && Number.isFinite(r.score)) scored.push([id, r.score]);\n    else silent.push(id);\n  }\n  const groups = (list, order) => {\n    list.sort((a, b) => order * (a[1] - b[1]) || a[0] - b[0]);\n    const out = [];\n    for (const [id, value] of list) {\n      const last = out[out.length - 1];\n      if (last && last.value === value) last.ids.push(id);\n      else out.push({ value, ids: [id] });\n    }\n    return out.map((g) => g.ids);\n  };\n  return [...groups(timed, 1), ...groups(scored, -1), ...(silent.length ? [silent] : [])];\n}\n\n/** A time or score as a number: finite, given as a number or as text; NaN for null, '' or true, which Number() would make 0. */\nconst asNumber = (v) => (typeof v === 'number' || (typeof v === 'string' && v.trim() !== '') ? Number(v) : NaN);\n\n/** The protocol's limits on a round's highlights (README §10). */\nexport const HIGHLIGHTS = Object.freeze({ stats: 6, statName: 16, statText: 16, awards: 3, title: 24, detail: 40 });\n\n/** One player's stats, trimmed: up to six names, each a finite number or a short text. Null when none survive. */\nexport function cleanStats(stats) {\n  if (!stats || typeof stats !== 'object' || Array.isArray(stats)) return null;\n  const out = {};\n  for (const [name, value] of Object.entries(stats).slice(0, HIGHLIGHTS.stats)) {\n    const label = String(name).trim().slice(0, HIGHLIGHTS.statName);\n    if (!label) continue;\n    if (typeof value === 'number' && Number.isFinite(value)) out[label] = value;\n    else if (typeof value === 'string' && value.trim()) out[label] = value.trim().slice(0, HIGHLIGHTS.statText);\n  }\n  return Object.keys(out).length ? out : null;\n}\n\n/**\n * Awards, trimmed: `{ id, title, detail? }`, at most three a player, for\n * players of this round. A result's awards are about its own player: `self` is its id.\n */\nexport function cleanAwards(awards, ids, self = null) {\n  if (!Array.isArray(awards)) return [];\n  const given = new Map();\n  const out = [];\n  for (const a of awards) {\n    const id = self ?? a?.id;\n    const title = String(a?.title ?? '').trim().slice(0, HIGHLIGHTS.title);\n    if (!title || !ids.includes(id) || (given.get(id) || 0) >= HIGHLIGHTS.awards) continue;\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
