{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_232","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n '\"'^#{1,4} |[Mm]ultiplayer|AI Hub|AIHub|duration|35 seconds|class|[Aa]nimation|keyboards|150'\"' PLAN.md TASK.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_232","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n '\"'^#{1,4} |[Mm]ultiplayer|AI Hub|AIHub|duration|35 seconds|class|[Aa]nimation|keyboards|150'\"' PLAN.md TASK.md\"","aggregated_output":"TASK.md:13:Tech Stack: Build on https://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge/tree/main/dist/handoff. You may change anything in it, the engine included, and add whatever systems, art assets and animations the game needs. The rest of the tech stack is your choice.\nTASK.md:17:Animation: Use the engine’s native animation system as the base. Make new animations for whatever makes the game feel like the source.\nTASK.md:24:Create a subfolder called [GameTitle-SOURCE-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221356] to keep all your dev files in. You can develop separate modules, then bundle into a single file [GameTitle-SOURCE-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221356].html in root when you’re done. You may use external CDN dependencies. Do not read files outside what you need: other agents work in the folders beside this one. They share this machine’s ports and processes too. Prefer file:// and the engine’s headless tools. If you need a server (the AI Hub harness does), bind 127.0.0.1 on a port the OS picks (`python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1` prints it) and confirm the page is your game before trusting a result. Stop only processes you started, by their PID: never pkill, killall, fuser -k, or kill whatever holds a port.\nTASK.md:32:## This computer\nTASK.md:48:### What this computer doesn't have\nTASK.md:55:- **No second player.** Play multiplayer with two browser pages (or contexts) on this computer.\nTASK.md:59:### Sharing this computer\nTASK.md:66:## Goal\nTASK.md:78:Multiplayer: Follow https://github.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/tree/main/lib/hub for multiplayer integration into ai-hub as well as for the game on its own.\nTASK.md:82:## UI & UX: 10-Foot Controller-First Philosophy\nTASK.md:89:## Done\nTASK.md:92:## Source Information\nTASK.md:100:- Animation: system used\nTASK.md:107:- Usage: write \"added on import\". You can't see your own cost, so don't estimate it: the runner records the real cost, tokens and time, and the agent that imports the game into AI Hub puts them on your About/Credits screen.\nTASK.md:109:Exit interview: before you finish, also save these answers as exit-interview.json in this folder's root, beside the game's .html: one JSON object in exactly the shape below, every value filled in (\"unknown\" for anything you can't confirm). Tools read it (the game's run record and the AI Hub catalogue), so write plain text, and check that the file parses as JSON.\nTASK.md:111:  \"sourceInformation\": {\"date\": \"\", \"source\": \"\", \"plan\": \"\", \"genre\": \"\", \"perspective\": \"\", \"tech\": \"\", \"artDirection\": \"\", \"animation\": \"\", \"audio\": \"\", \"online\": \"\", \"testing\": \"\", \"research\": \"\", \"environment\": \"\", \"model\": \"\", \"usage\": \"added on import\"},\nPLAN.md:1:# Build plan: a wellness-retreat balance game inspired by Wii Fit\nPLAN.md:13:## 1. The game\nPLAN.md:37:2. **Your thumb is the body.** Squat depth *is* the stick. No canned animation that ignores your input.\nPLAN.md:44:## 2. What the player does\nPLAN.md:54:In an AI Hub session: straight to the round, no title or menus (section 14).\nPLAN.md:61:## 3. The core mechanic: the Lean\nPLAN.md:70:if (Math.hypot(px, py) >= 1) stumble();   // 1 s: input ignored, p eases home, stumble animation, score penalty\nPLAN.md:126:## 4. The activities\nPLAN.md:130:### Stillness\nPLAN.md:138:### Strength (all three are `rep`: one code path, three data rows)\nPLAN.md:148:### Cardio\nPLAN.md:156:### Balance games\nPLAN.md:164:### The Gentle Games (Day 5)\nPLAN.md:169:## 5. Progress\nPLAN.md:207:## 6. The island (hub)\nPLAN.md:234:## 7. Cast and voice\nPLAN.md:236:**Tone rules.** Short sentences. Sincere, polite, a little too personal. Translated-instruction-manual cadence. No sarcasm, no meanness, no profanity, no pop-culture jokes, no references to being a game. Praise that wobbles. Facts nobody asked for. Tare is needy but never says so outright. Every text box: at most 2 lines of about 60 characters; a line is one thought. Use these lines verbatim and write as many more in the same voice as the game needs (aim for 150+ total, so a second playthrough still surprises). All text lives in `game/data/lines.js`.\nPLAN.md:283:## 8. Art direction\nPLAN.md:303:## 9. Animation recipes (all ✔)\nPLAN.md:382:## 10. Audio (all from code, no files)\nPLAN.md:394:## 11. UI and UX: 10 feet, controller first\nPLAN.md:398:**Canvas UI, bright and round.** `E.Menu`'s default is a dark JRPG window: wrong here. Write one **`Pills`** widget (about 70 lines) and use it on every game screen: white rounded pills, cyan focus that grows slightly, soft tick on move. Up/down (or left/right) with `input.repeat`, ✕ or Enter picks, ○ backs out. **Mouse: hover moves focus, a click picks** (`input.pointer()`, `input.clicked()`). `E.Dialog` takes `{ bg: ['#ffffff', '#eaf6f8'], border: '#2cc6e6', color: '#20404c', nameColor: '#14a8c8' }`, but it hard-codes a near-black text shadow that smears on white. **Make this one engine change ✔:** in `class Dialog` in `engine/my-3d2dge.js`, replace each `shadow: '#05040a'` used for the name, the text and the choices (3 places, around lines 9153 to 9176) with `shadow: this.shadow === undefined ? '#05040a' : this.shadow`, then set `talk.shadow = null`.\nPLAN.md:427:## 12. Attract Mode\nPLAN.md:437:## 13. Dev Mode\nPLAN.md:452:## 14. Multiplayer\nPLAN.md:454:**Class (local, on its own, 2 to 4).** From the title: join with Start on a free pad or 2 on the keyboard (`game.allowJoin({ max: 4, onJoin })`; `game.players[i]` has the same input API; keyboard players get `E.Input.halfKeys`). ✔ Half a keyboard runs out of keys with the full `INPUT` (the step and pace actions get none), so the Class scene sets its own `input`: the moves and menu actions plus `breath`, `catchL`, `catchR` only (left half F G H, right half `. / ,`), and its Step Class reads `lanes: ['left', 'down', 'up', 'right']`. Everyone gets a mat, a colour (`E.PLAYER_COLORS`) and a pre-made rig, on one fixed screen at size 1.5 with a small Plate under each. Activities: Stork Stand, Quiet Candle, Squat Rail, Step Class (two lanes), Hoop Hips, 35 s each, or \"Surprise me\" (3 rounds). So every class-capable activity takes a list of **contestants** from the start, not one player. Scores are 0 to 1000 (`round(pct × 1000)`). Results: podium with polite titles (Most Still, Best Wobble, Participated). Tare reads them. Empty mats hold Regulars driven by bots, for life, not for score.\nPLAN.md:456:**AI Hub session (`ghost` mode, 1 to 4).** Follow the protocol README (`https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/README.md`); it is short, read it. Outside a session the game is unaffected and `connect()` answers `null`. ✔ This exact shape passed the harness at 1, 2, 3 and 4 players, on the bad network, and with the host leaving.\nPLAN.md:458:**The round: \"Morning Class\".** Everyone plays the same 3 events on their own copy, in lockstep, seeing others as translucent seat-coloured ghosts on neighbouring mats (or in the world for Slalom and Jog). About 150 s: each event is 5 s intro + 40 s play + 5 s scores. Deal with `AIHub.rng('deal')`: one from Stork/Candle/Squat/Push-Up, one from Step/Hoop, one from Slalom/Jog.\nPLAN.md:461:const inSession = !!(window.AIHub && AIHub.active);\nPLAN.md:467:  const info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'ghost', seats: [1, 4], card: true });\nPLAN.md:469:  AIHub.on('card', c => { card = c; });\nPLAN.md:470:  AIHub.on('start', () => {});\nPLAN.md:471:  AIHub.on('message', (d, from) => { /* ghost state */ });\nPLAN.md:472:  AIHub.on('leave', ({ id }) => { /* remove that ghost */ });\nPLAN.md:473:  AIHub.on('time-up', () => report());                  // result() at once if not reported\nPLAN.md:474:  AIHub.on('end', () => { over = true; game.audio.stopMusic(); game.audio.mute(true); game.input.clear(); });\nPLAN.md:475:  await game.booted; AIHub.ready();                     // no key press\nPLAN.md:479:- **Card (yours, `card: true`):** the studio with the players lined up on mats, Tare hopping, the title, each player's name and colour with a ready tick, how to win, this player's controls, seconds left. While `AIHub.time() === -Infinity`: `confirm` or `start` → `AIHub.answer('ready')`, `more` (△) → `AIHub.answer('more')`, clicks on Ready/More too. No menus or choices on the card. Show \"More time\" state from the `card` event (`asked`, `paused`).\nPLAN.md:480:- **Clock:** all event timing comes from `AIHub.time()`, not `game.time`. A frame over 50 ms gives up its time, so a slow machine's game clock lags and would desync. Countdown while negative. Play at ≥ 0. If `info.limitMs` is shorter than the round, shrink the events.\nPLAN.md:481:- **Randomness:** every activity takes its disturbances from `AIHub.rng('e' + eventIndex)` (and a seeded `E.rng` offline). `Math.random` is only for cosmetics like particles and blinks, because copies draw it at different rates.\nPLAN.md:482:- **Ghost data:** `AIHub.send({ t: 'g', a: eventIndex, l: [x, y], p: phase, w: [wx, wy], s: score }, { reliable: false })` about 10 times a second. Draw only if `a` matches your current event. `r.actor(..., { alpha: .5 })`, name tag in seat colour. Names come from `info.players`, drawn with `E.font` only (never HTML). Limit: 20 messages/s.\nPLAN.md:483:- **Reporting:** `AIHub.progress({ score: total, label: total + ' pts' })` about once a second; at the end `AIHub.result({ score: total, stats: { Steadiness: '84%' }, awards: [{ title: 'Most Still', detail: '...' }] })` once.\nPLAN.md:504:## 15. Tech and setup\nPLAN.md:530:# prints 23 clips, about 173 KB. vendor/clipsrc can then go; it is not bundled\nPLAN.md:541:  index.html   dev page: canvas (#screen with CSS width and height 100%, or it draws at 300×150 ✔) and the scripts in order\nPLAN.md:549:  scenes/      title, attract, member, arrival, island, bodycheck, session, evening, games, ending, about, class, round\nPLAN.md:560:  class: true, hub: true, tiers: [ {/* numbers */}, {/* numbers */} ], stars: [.35, .65, .90], lines: {/* ... */},\nPLAN.md:588:## 16. Testing\nPLAN.md:600:- Class: 4 inputs, scores, podium. Hub logic with a fake `AIHub` object: same seed, same deal; time-up reports once; end stops input.\nPLAN.md:611:**`hub`:** copy the bundle to `tests/hub/game.html`, serve `tests/hub` with `python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1`, read the port it prints, confirm the page is yours, then open `harness.html?game=game.html&` + each of: `players=1&auto=1`; `players=2&auto=1`; `players=3&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`; `players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`; `players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&scenario=host-leave`. Wait for `document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'`, require `window.__hubCheck.pass`, and print failing `checks`. Then open the game on its own and see it reach the title. Stop only your server, by its PID, never with `pkill`, `killall` or `fuser -k`.\nPLAN.md:617:## 17. Build order\nPLAN.md:638:## 18. Finish line: your brief, line by line\nPLAN.md:643:- [ ] Art and animation: engine-native base, new assets and motion (sections 8, 9)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
