{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_401","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"D='Wee Bit of Zen-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221356'; rg -n 'rng:|time:|answer:|probe:|function rng|function answer|function probe|function now' \\\"\"'$D/vendor/session.js\"; sed -n '\"'490,640p' \\\"\"'$D/vendor/session.js\"; rg -n '\"'Hub|hub|Mocap' PLAN.md | tail -20\"","aggregated_output":"175:  function now() {\n331:    post('answer', { answer: what });\n422:  /** Race and side by side: report your own outcome once, {time: ms} (lower wins) or {score: n} (higher wins), with optional stats and awards. */\n499:<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Lean: left stick, WASD or mouse. Breathe: R2, Space or click\">\n506:**Stack:** the my-3D2dge full engine (2D views), its `mode7`, `road`, `physics`, `rhythm` modules (all inside `my-3d2dge.js`), `Mocap` and a cut clip set, the hub client. No World3D, no other libraries. **Start from no single kit:** this game mixes genres, so use the full engine with your own page, and read `engine/kits/road.js`, `kart.js`, `rhythm.js`, `pinball.js` (physics) and `sports.js` (joining players) when you build those parts.\n511:git clone --depth 1 --filter=blob:none --sparse https://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge.git _src\n516:mkdir -p vendor/clipsrc/tools vendor/clipsrc/src/mocap tests/hub\n517:B=https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge/main\n518:H=https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub\n526:for f in harness.html bridge.js round.js; do curl -fsSLo tests/hub/$f $H/$f; done\n533:More clips, if you want them: search `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge/main/src/mocap/catalogs/cmu-takes.tsv` (take `NN_xx` lives in `examples/cmu-lib/CMU_NN.js`) and `.../catalogs/mesh2motion.json`.\n542:  core.js      G namespace, game, INPUT, DEV defaults, state, saves, deep links (#hub, #act/stork/1, #day/3, #ending)\n550:tests/run.mjs  the one test command; tests/hub/ the harness\n560:  class: true, hub: true, tiers: [ {/* numbers */}, {/* numbers */} ], stars: [.35, .65, .90], lines: {/* ... */},\n568:**`build.mjs`:** concatenates engine, `vendor/readable.js`, `vendor/mocap.js`, `vendor/fitclips.js`, game files; replaces every `</script` with `<\\/script` in everything it inlines ✔; writes head tags, CSS, the boot markup at the start of `<body>` (copy the `e3-boot` div from `engine/game/index.html`); injects the exit-interview JSON as `G.ABOUT`; writes the single file to the place your brief names (pass it as an argument) and copies it to `tests/hub/game.html`. External CDN is allowed but not needed: inline everything. About 1.5 MB.\n590:**One command: `node tests/run.mjs [rules|browser|hub|all]`.** It prints only failures and one final line (`213 passed, 0 failed`). Rerun only the group whose code you changed. Use scripted checks first and screenshots only for what a script can't judge. Do not use subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit.\n592:**`rules` (Node, no browser, seconds).** Load engine, vendor and game files in a `vm` context with `window`, `addEventListener` and `location` stand-ins (✔ `Mocap` and clips load this way; see `engine/kits/test.mjs`). Drive with `game.advance` and `input.tap/hold`; read `game.debug.snapshot()`.\n600:- Class: 4 inputs, scores, podium. Hub logic with a fake `AIHub` object: same seed, same deal; time-up reports once; end stops input.\n611:**`hub`:** copy the bundle to `tests/hub/game.html`, serve `tests/hub` with `python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1`, read the port it prints, confirm the page is yours, then open `harness.html?game=game.html&` + each of: `players=1&auto=1`; `players=2&auto=1`; `players=3&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`; `players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`; `players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&scenario=host-leave`. Wait for `document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'`, require `window.__hubCheck.pass`, and print failing `checks`. Then open the game on its own and see it reach the title. Stop only your server, by its PID, never with `pkill`, `killall` or `fuser -k`.\n630:| M7 | Class mode; the hub round with ghosts and card | Harness at all five settings; two-page play shows ghosts |\n634:**If you truly run out of room, cut in this order and remove every trace (no stubs):** tier 2s except Eyes Closed → Tare's Day scene → Laundry Line → Coastal Jog → wardrobe items beyond three. Never cut: the Lean, Stork, Rail, Step, Candle, Slalom, Tray, the day loop, the ending, attract, dev mode, Class, the hub round, About.\n645:- [ ] Hub session passes the harness; the game also runs on its own, with local Class (section 14)\n655:- [ ] Exit-interview JSON beside the HTML, in the brief's exact shape, parses. Suggested `aiHub`: type `Game`, genre `Sports`, source `Wii Fit`, series empty, players `1–4`, controls in one line, tags from: `pixel art`, `comedy`, `versus`, `arcade`, `story`, `2d`\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
