{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_636","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"D='Wee Bit of Zen-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221356'; sed -n '100,122p' \\\"\"'$D/tests/run.py\"; sed -n '\"'245,300p' \\\"\"'$D/src/game.js\"; sed -n '\"'1,75p' \\\"\"'$D/src/style.css\" | sed '\"'s/}/}\\\\n/g'; sed -n '115,128p' \\\"\"'$D/src/game.js\" | fold -w 200; sed -n '\"'1,160p' TASK.md | tail -n 80\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_636","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"D='Wee Bit of Zen-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221356'; sed -n '100,122p' \\\"\"'$D/tests/run.py\"; sed -n '\"'245,300p' \\\"\"'$D/src/game.js\"; sed -n '\"'1,75p' \\\"\"'$D/src/style.css\" | sed '\"'s/}/}\\\\n/g'; sed -n '115,128p' \\\"\"'$D/src/game.js\" | fold -w 200; sed -n '\"'1,160p' TASK.md | tail -n 80\"","aggregated_output":"      z.startActivity(ACTIVITIES[0], { seconds: 5 }); z.step(.5); z.action('pause');\n      const paused = z.state.activity.elapsed; z.step(2);\n      verify('pause freezes the workout', z.state.activity.elapsed === paused);\n      z.action('dev'); tuning.spring = 3; z.action('reset-tuning');\n      verify('developer tuning resets', tuning.spring === tuningDefaults.spring);\n      z.action('resume'); verify('pause resumes', z.state.screen === 'play');\n      z.action('leave-play');\n      for (const count of [2, 3, 4]) {\n        z.state.classPlayers = [];\n        z.action('class');\n        if (count >= 3) z.action('class-toggle', '2');\n        if (count >= 4) z.action('class-toggle', '3');\n        z.action('start-class');\n        verify(`${count}-person class starts`, z.state.classActors.length === count - 1);\n        z.step(36);\n        verify(`${count}-person class finishes`, z.state.screen === 'class-result' && z.state.classScores.length === count);\n        verify(`${count}-person class has independent scores`, new Set(z.state.classScores.map(item => item.score)).size > 1);\n      }\n      z.state.classPlayers = []; z.action('class'); z.action('class-toggle', '1');\n      verify('second keyboard player joins', z.state.classPlayers[1].source === 'keyboard');\n      z.action('start-class'); keys.add('l'); z.step(1); keys.delete('l');\n      verify('second keyboard controls their own player', z.state.classActors[0].px > 0);\n      z.action('leave-play'); z.action('island');\n  progress.style.width = `${clamp(activity.elapsed / activity.seconds * 100, 0, 100)}%`;\n  dot.style.transform = `translate(${activity.px * 70}px, ${activity.py * 70}px)`;\n  ring.style.transform = `translate(${activity.ringX * 70}px, ${activity.ringY * 70}px)`;\n  score.textContent = `${Math.round(activity.score / Math.max(1, activity.samples) * 100)}% STEADY`;\n}\nfunction updateCheckHUD() {\n  if (!state.check) return;\n  const timer = document.getElementById('check-timer'), text = document.getElementById('check-text'), progress = document.getElementById('check-progress');\n  if (!timer) return;\n  timer.textContent = state.check.phase === 'still' ? String(Math.max(0, Math.ceil(5 - state.check.elapsed))).padStart(2, '0') : `${state.check.directions.size}/4`;\n  text.textContent = state.check.phase === 'still' ? 'Find a comfortable center.' : 'Lean left, up, right and down.';\n  progress.style.width = `${state.check.phase === 'still' ? clamp(state.check.elapsed / 5 * 50, 0, 50) : 50 + state.check.directions.size * 12.5}%`;\n}\nfunction update(dt) {\n  state.clock += dt;\n  if (state.screen === 'title') { state.idle += dt; if (state.idle >= 10 && !state.hub.active) screen('attract'); }\n  if (state.screen === 'check') { state.check.elapsed += dt; if (state.check.phase === 'still' && state.check.elapsed >= 5) { state.check.phase = 'lean'; state.check.elapsed = 0; } if (state.check.phase === 'lean' && (state.check.directions.size === 4 || state.check.elapsed >= 14)) screen('question'); }\n  if (state.screen === 'play') updateActivity(dt);\n}\nfunction action(name, id) {\n  unlockAudio(); state.idle = 0; tone(440, .07, .2);\n  switch (name) {\n    case 'home': if (!state.hub.active) { state.classMode = false; screen('title'); } break;\n    case 'slots': screen('slots'); break;\n    case 'slot': state.slot = Number(id); state.member = state.slots[state.slot] || memberDefault(); state.classMode = false; screen(state.slots[state.slot] ? 'island' : 'setup'); break;\n    case 'outfit': state.member.name = document.getElementById('nickname')?.value || state.member.name; state.member.outfit = Number(id); render(); break;\n    case 'instructor': state.member.name = document.getElementById('nickname')?.value || state.member.name; state.member.instructor = id; render(); break;\n    case 'create-member': { const value = document.getElementById('nickname')?.value.trim(); state.member.name = (value || 'Guest').slice(0, 16); save(); screen('intro'); break; }\n    case 'check': beginCheck(); break;\n    case 'question-answer': state.check.answer = id; screen('check-result'); break;\n    case 'island': state.classMode = false; screen('island'); break;\n    case 'select-activity': state.selection = ACTIVITIES.find(activity => activity.id === id); state.classMode = false; screen('activity'); break;\n    case 'locked': notify('A new mat opens on a later day.'); break;\n    case 'start-activity': startActivity(state.selection); break;\n    case 'retry': startActivity(state.selection, { seconds: state.classMode ? 35 : state.festival ? 30 : undefined }); break;\n    case 'result-continue': if (state.festival) { state.festivalIndex++; if (state.festivalIndex >= 3) { state.festival = false; state.member.finished = true; save(); screen('ending'); } else screen('festival'); } else if (state.classMode) screen('class-result'); else screen('island'); break;\n    case 'sleep': if (memberDefault && state.member.sessions < 3) notify('Try three sessions before calling it a day.'); else if (state.member.day === 5) { state.festival = true; state.festivalIndex = 0; screen('festival'); } else screen('recap'); break;\n    case 'next-day': state.member.day = Math.min(5, state.member.day + 1); state.member.sessions = 0; save(); screen('intro'); break;\n    case 'festival-start': startActivity(ACTIVITIES.find(activity => activity.id === ['stork','slalom','candle'][state.festivalIndex]), { seconds: 30 }); break;\n    case 'ending': screen('ending'); break;\n    case 'free-play': state.member.finished = true; save(); screen('island'); break;\n    case 'class': state.classMode = true; if (!state.classPlayers.length) state.classPlayers = [{ name: state.member?.name || 'Player 1', type: 'Keyboard / pad', source: 'primary' }, { name: 'Gertrude', type: 'Bot', source: 'bot' }]; if (!CLASS_IDS.includes(state.selection?.id)) state.selection = ACTIVITIES[0]; screen('class'); break;\n    case 'class-toggle': { const index = Number(id); if (index === 0) break; const current = state.classPlayers[index]; state.classPlayers[index] = !current ? { name: ['Player 1','Gertrude','Dennis','Marisol'][index], type: 'Bot', source: 'bot' } : index === 1 && current.source === 'bot' ? { name: 'Player 2', type: 'Keyboard 2', source: 'keyboard' } : null; render(); break; }\n    case 'class-activity': state.selection = ACTIVITIES.find(activity => activity.id === id); render(); break;\n    case 'start-class': state.classPlayers = state.classPlayers.filter(Boolean); if (state.classPlayers.length < 2) { notify('Add at least one friend or bot.'); break; } startActivity(state.selection, { seconds: 35 }); break;\n    case 'hub-ready': window.AIHub.answer('ready'); notify('Ready to go!'); break;\n    case 'hub-more': window.AIHub.answer('more'); notify('Waiting for more players.'); break;\n    case 'settings': state.returnScreen = state.screen; screen('settings'); break;\n    case 'settings-back': save(); screen(state.returnScreen || 'title'); break;\n    case 'toggle': state.settings[id] = !state.settings[id]; save(); render(); break;\n    case 'volume': state.settings[id] = state.settings[id] >= 100 ? 0 : state.settings[id] + 10; save(); render(); break;\n    case 'glyphs': state.settings.glyphs = state.settings.glyphs === 'Xbox' ? 'PlayStation' : 'Xbox'; save(); render(); break;\n    case 'pause': if (!state.hub.active) { pausedFrom = state.screen === 'play' ? 'play' : pausedFrom; screen('pause'); } break;\n    case 'resume': screen(pausedFrom || 'play'); break;\n    case 'restart': startActivity(state.selection, { seconds: state.classMode ? 35 : state.festival ? 30 : undefined }); break;\n    case 'leave-play': state.festival = false; state.classMode ? screen('class') : screen('island'); break;\n:root{color-scheme:light;--ink:#263d42;--muted:#708485;--teal:#248e8b;--line:#d9e9e2;--paper:#fffefa;--sun:#f8cc76;--shadow:0 18px 50px rgba(41,78,72,.12)}\n\n*{box-sizing:border-box}\nhtml,body{width:100%;height:100%;margin:0;overflow:hidden}\nbody{font-family:ui-rounded,\"Avenir Next\",Avenir,\"Trebuchet MS\",sans-serif;background:#e9f4ed;color:var(--ink);-webkit-font-smoothing:antialiased}\nbutton,input,select{font:inherit}\nbutton{color:inherit;cursor:pointer}\nbutton:focus-visible,input:focus-visible,select:focus-visible{outline:4px solid #f3bb5d;outline-offset:3px}\n#world{position:fixed;inset:0;width:100%;height:100%;display:block}\n#app{position:fixed;inset:0;overflow:auto;scrollbar-width:thin}\n#app:empty{pointer-events:none}\n.page{min-height:100%;padding:clamp(20px,4vw,64px);display:flex;flex-direction:column;position:relative}\n.topbar{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:15px;z-index:2}\n.brand{font-weight:900;letter-spacing:.15em;text-transform:uppercase;font-size:clamp(10px,.9vw,13px);display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px}\n.brand-mark{display:grid;place-items:center;background:var(--teal);color:white;border-radius:50%;width:30px;height:30px;font-size:17px;letter-spacing:0}\n.top-actions{display:flex;gap:8px}\n.icon-btn,.small-btn{border:1px solid rgba(72,116,105,.18);background:rgba(255,255,250,.83);border-radius:999px;box-shadow:0 4px 12px rgba(42,72,64,.05);font-weight:800;padding:11px 17px}\n.icon-btn:hover,.small-btn:hover{background:#fff;transform:translateY(-2px)}\n.hero{flex:1;display:flex;align-items:center;min-height:0}\n.hero-copy{width:min(50%,620px);padding:28px 0 54px}\n.eyebrow{font-size:12px;font-weight:900;letter-spacing:.19em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#5b9186}\n.eyebrow:before{content:'';display:inline-block;width:25px;height:2px;background:#8fb9a5;vertical-align:middle;margin-right:10px}\n.logo{font-size:clamp(50px,7.5vw,108px);letter-spacing:-.075em;line-height:.88;margin:20px 0 22px;font-weight:900;color:#244944}\n.logo span{color:#49a99d}\n.lede{font-size:clamp(17px,1.6vw,23px);line-height:1.45;max-width:470px;color:#58716e;margin:0 0 28px}\n.menu-stack{display:grid;gap:10px;width:min(100%,370px)}\n.action{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;text-align:left;border:1px solid rgba(61,119,103,.11);background:rgba(255,255,250,.92);border-radius:18px;padding:16px 19px;box-shadow:0 6px 20px rgba(50,95,80,.06);font-weight:850;font-size:17px;transition:transform .15s,box-shadow .15s,background .15s}\n.action:hover,.action.is-focused{transform:translateX(6px);box-shadow:0 8px 24px rgba(46,112,98,.15);background:#fff}\n.action.primary{background:#2b9991;color:white;border-color:#2b9991}\n.action .arrow{font-size:19px;opacity:.75}\n.footer{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:15px;align-items:center;font-size:11px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.11em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#76918a;z-index:2}\n.footer strong{color:#44655e}\n.footer .hint{letter-spacing:.02em;text-transform:none}\n.main-wrap{flex:1;width:100%;max-width:1160px;margin:0 auto;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;padding:28px 0}\n.card{width:min(100%,760px);background:rgba(255,255,251,.96);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.9);box-shadow:var(--shadow);border-radius:30px;padding:clamp(24px,4vw,50px);position:relative}\n.card.wide{width:min(100%,1060px)}\n.card.narrow{width:min(100%,560px)}\n.card h1,.card h2{letter-spacing:-.045em;line-height:1.05;margin:10px 0 12px}\n.card h1{font-size:clamp(32px,4.3vw,53px)}\n.card h2{font-size:clamp(25px,3vw,36px)}\n.card p{line-height:1.5;color:#667c79;font-size:17px}\n.card .action{background:#f4f8f4;box-shadow:none}\n.card .action.primary{background:#2b9991;color:white}\n.card .action:hover,.card .action.is-focused{background:#e7f3ed}\n.card .action.primary:hover,.card .action.primary.is-focused{background:#218b83}\n.card-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:12px}\n.activity-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:12px}\n.activity{border:1px solid #e4eee7;background:#f8fbf7;border-radius:19px;padding:15px;text-align:left;min-height:114px;position:relative}\n.activity:hover,.activity.is-focused{background:#edf8f1;border-color:#8ec9b3;transform:translateY(-2px)}\n.activity:disabled{opacity:.5;cursor:not-allowed}\n.activity-icon{display:grid;place-items:center;float:left;width:42px;height:42px;border-radius:13px;background:var(--tint,#e2f2e9);font-size:23px;margin-right:12px}\n.activity strong{display:block;font-size:16px}\n.activity small{display:block;color:#83948e;margin-top:5px}\n.activity .stars{color:#e4ad4f;font-size:13px;margin-top:8px}\n.chip{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:7px;border-radius:99px;background:#edf6ef;color:#56836f;font-size:11px;font-weight:900;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.12em;padding:9px 12px}\n.chip.orange{background:#fff1d5;color:#ae7e31}\n.chip.pink{background:#fce9df;color:#b77e6e}\n.split{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:25px;align-items:center}\n.row{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:16px}\n.divider{height:1px;background:#e7efe9;margin:19px 0}\n.field{display:grid;gap:8px;margin:16px 0;color:#748c83;font-weight:800;font-size:12px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.12em}\n.field input,.field select{width:100%;border:2px solid #e3eee6;border-radius:14px;padding:13px 15px;color:var(--ink);background:#fbfdf9;font-size:17px;letter-spacing:0;text-transform:none}\n.options{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px}\n.option{border:2px solid #e6eee6;border-radius:13px;padding:10px 14px;background:#f8fbf8;font-weight:800}\n.option.selected{border-color:#63b2a0;background:#e7f7ec}\n.dialogue{background:#eef8f2;border-radius:20px;padding:18px 20px;color:#42665c;font-size:18px;line-height:1.45}\n.dialogue strong{color:#278f82}\n.actions{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:10px;margin-top:22px}\n.actions .action{min-width:160px}\n.play-hud{position:absolute;inset:0;pointer-events:none;padding:clamp(18px,3vw,40px);display:flex;flex-direction:column;justify-content:space-between}\n.play-hud button{pointer-events:auto}\n.hud-top,.hud-bottom{display:flex;align-items:flex-start;justify-content:space-between;gap:12px}\n.hud-box{background:rgba(255,255,250,.92);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.8);border-radius:20px;padding:14px 20px;box-shadow:0 9px 28px rgba(44,83,75,.09)}\n.hud-box strong{font-size:20px;letter-spacing:-.03em}\n.hud-box small{display:block;font-size:11px;color:#79938a;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.12em;font-weight:900;margin-bottom:3px}\n.meter{height:9px;width:180px;border-radius:20px;background:#e5efe6;overflow:hidden;margin-top:8px}\n.meter>i{display:block;height:100%;background:#efba68;border-radius:20px}\n.play-instruction{text-align:center;align-self:center;background:rgba(255,255,250,.91);border-radius:999px;padding:12px 20px;font-weight:800;color:#57776c;box-shadow:var(--shadow)}\n.progress-dots{display:flex;gap:6px}\n.progress-dots i{width:9px;height:9px;border-radius:50%;background:#dcebe2}\n.progress-dots i.on{background:#4cae9c}\n.score-big{font-size:clamp(48px,7vw,76px);font-weight:900;letter-spacing:-.07em;color:#2b9991;line-height:1}\n.stars-big{font-size:30px;color:#efb956;letter-spacing:5px}\n.note{font-size:13px!important;color:#91a39b!important}\n.scroll{max-height:min(57vh,570px);overflow:auto;padding-right:8px}\n.about-group{border-top:1px solid #e7efe9;padding:12px 0}\n.about-group h3{font-size:18px}\n.about-group p{font-size:14px;margin:5px 0;overflow-wrap:anywhere}\n.touch-notice{position:fixed;inset:0;z-index:20;display:grid;place-items:center;padding:20px;background:rgba(230,244,236,.92);text-align:center}\n.touch-notice .card{width:min(100%,460px)}\n.hidden{display:none!important}\n.toast{position:fixed;bottom:25px;left:50%;transform:translateX(-50%);background:#284e49;color:#fff;border-radius:99px;padding:12px 22px;z-index:10;font-weight:800}\n.class-players{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:10px}\n.player-tile{padding:18px;background:#f2f8f1;border-radius:18px;text-align:center}\n.player-tile .face{font-size:35px}\n.slider{width:100%;accent-color:#38a597}\n.island-message{position:absolute;top:12%;left:50%;transform:translateX(-50%);text-align:center;white-space:nowrap;pointer-events:none}\n.island-message h1{font-size:clamp(24px,3.2vw,40px);margin:6px;letter-spacing:-.04em}\n.island-message p{margin:0;color:#708e82;font-weight:700}\n.map-actions{position:absolute;bottom:clamp(20px,4vh,45px);left:50%;transform:translateX(-50%);width:min(92%,760px);display:flex;justify-content:center;gap:10px}\n.map-actions .action{min-width:180px}\n.map-actions button{pointer-events:auto}\n.center-copy{text-align:center}\n.center-copy p{max-width:580px;margin-left:auto;margin-right:auto}\n\n@media(max-width:850px){.hero-copy{width:58%}\n.logo{font-size:clamp(48px,8vw,72px)}\n.activity-grid{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr))}\n.footer .weather{display:none}\n.card{padding:26px}\n.main-wrap{align-items:flex-start;padding:25px 0}\n.page{min-height:100%;padding:22px}\n.play-hud{padding:16px}\n.island-message{top:12%}\n}\n\n@media(max-width:540px){.page{padding:18px}\n.hero{align-items:flex-end}\n.hero-copy{width:100%;padding:30px 0 20px}\n.logo{font-size:58px;max-width:320px;margin:12px 0}\n.lede{font-size:16px;max-width:315px;margin-bottom:18px}\n.menu-stack{width:100%;max-width:340px}\n.action{padding:13px 16px;font-size:15px;border-radius:15px}\n.brand{font-size:10px}\n.footer{font-size:9px}\n.card-grid,.split{grid-template-columns:1fr}\n.activity-grid{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:7px}\n.activity{padding:10px;min-height:92px}\n.activity-icon{width:34px;height:34px;font-size:18px}\n.activity strong{font-size:13px}\n.activity small{font-size:11px}\n.card h1{font-size:34px}\n.card p{font-size:15px}\n.hud-box{padding:10px 12px}\n.hud-box strong{font-size:16px}\n.meter{width:110px}\n.play-instruction{font-size:12px;max-width:90%;padding:10px 14px}\n.class-players{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr)}\n.map-actions .action{min-width:0;flex:1}\n.map-actions{width:90%}\n.scroll{max-height:55vh}\n}\n\n    heading = 'DAY 5 &nbsp; / &nbsp; GENTLE GAMES';\n    content = `<main class=\"main-wrap narrow\"><div class=\"card dialogue\"><div class=\"eyebrow\">✳ &nbsp; THE GENTLE GAMES</div><h1>Ready, steady,<br><em>be yourself.</em></h1><p>Three friendly challenge\ns, ending in the Grand Stillness with Gertrude. The prize is a very nice feeling.</p><p class=\"note\">Challenge ${state.festivalIndex + 1} of 3 &nbsp; · &nbsp; ${['Stork Stand', 'Slalom', 'Quiet Candle\n'][state.festivalIndex]}</p><div class=\"actions\">${button('Begin challenge', 'festival-start', true)}</div></div></main>`;\n  } else if (state.screen === 'ending') {\n    heading = 'THANK YOU FOR STAYING';\n    content = `<main class=\"main-wrap narrow\"><div class=\"card dialogue\"><div class=\"eyebrow\">✳ &nbsp; YOUR ISLAND IS ALWAYS HERE</div><div class=\"stars-big\">✳</div><h1>A little steadier.<br><em>A lot\n more you.</em></h1><p>Gertrude awards you the Golden Composure. Dennis is emotional. Tare insists the award is calibrated.</p><p class=\"note\">Thank you for five days of moving, breathing, and making \nroom. The mats are yours whenever you wish.</p><div class=\"actions\">${button('Explore freely', 'free-play', true)}${button('About & credits', 'about')}</div></div></main>`;\n  } else if (state.screen === 'class') {\n    heading = 'LOCAL CLASS';\n    const players = state.classPlayers;\n    content = `<main class=\"main-wrap\"><div class=\"section-head\"><div><div class=\"eyebrow\">✳ &nbsp; BETTER TOGETHER</div><h1>Make room for friends.</h1><p>Up to four share the same screen. One keyboar\nd player; connect controllers for more.</p></div></div><div class=\"class-players\">${[0, 1, 2, 3].map((index) => `<div class=\"card player-tile\"><span class=\"slot-avatar\">${players[index] ? '☺' : '+'}</\nspan><strong>${players[index] ? escapeHTML(players[index].name) : 'Open spot'}</strong><small>${players[index] ? escapeHTML(players[index].type) : 'Join or add a bot'}</small><button class=\"chip\" data\n-action=\"class-toggle\" data-id=\"${index}\">${players[index] ? 'REMOVE' : 'ADD BOT'}</button></div>`).join('')}</div><div class=\"card class-select\"><p>CHOOSE A CLASS</p><div class=\"options\">${['stork','\ncandle','step','slalom','tray'].map(id => `<button class=\"option ${state.selection?.id === id ? 'selected' : ''}\" data-action=\"class-activity\" data-id=\"${id}\">${ACTIVITIES.find(a => a.id === id).name}\n</button>`).join('')}</div></div><div class=\"actions\">${button('Back', member.name === 'Guest' ? 'home' : 'island')}${button('Start class', 'start-class', true)}</div></main>`;\n  } else if (state.screen === 'class-result') {\n    heading = 'LOCAL CLASS';\n    content = `<main class=\"main-wrap narrow\"><div class=\"card dialogue\"><div class=\"eyebrow\">✳ &nbsp; EVERYONE SHOWED UP</div><h1>A class act.</h1><p>Everyone gets their own kind of gold star.</p>${s\ntate.classPlayers.map((player, index) => `<div class=\"row\"><span>${escapeHTML(player.name)} ${player.type === 'Bot' ? '· BOT' : ''}</span><b>${Math.max(30, state.result.percent - index * 5)} points &n\nbsp; ★</b></div>`).join('')}<div class=\"actions\">${button('Back to class', 'class', true)}</div></div></main>`;\n  } else if (state.screen === 'settings') {\n    heading = 'SETTINGS';\nCreate a feature-complete demo. Capture what makes the source distinctive (its world, characters, themes and tone) and turn it into the mechanics, pacing and UX of a great game. The demo must be long enough to show ALL features and gameplay mechanics so a player can clearly understand how the game plays and feels, and what they can and cannot do. Treat the demo as a complete, polished vertical slice. It should contain all the infrastructure, systems, and polish needed so the remainder of the game could later be built out with normal designer tools.\n\nInclude a dev mode, reachable from the pause menu, with the standard tools for testing the game quickly. Balance is key, so expose the most important gameplay variables as live sliders, with a reset to defaults.\n\nAttract Mode: After 10 seconds without input on the title/menu screen, start a looping AI-played demo or scripted replay (arcade/kiosk style); any input exits it. The AI (or replay) can be simple and may cheat freely (infinite health, ammo, abilities, no clip, etc). Its only job is to show as much of the demo as possible, the attract mode is not meant to balance the game.\n\nMultiplayer: Follow https://github.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/tree/main/lib/hub for multiplayer integration into ai-hub as well as for the game on its own.\n\nNarrative tone: Use a writing style similar to the source’s.\n\n## UI & UX: 10-Foot Controller-First Philosophy\nDesign the game around a PS5 DualSense (or any pad the browser reports in its standard mapping) played on a TV at 10 feet. With keyboard and mouse it's the same game on the same screens, not a separate desktop layout, but they should feel native, not like stand-ins for controller buttons. The keyboard uses the keys PC players expect for the genre. The mouse aims, looks, and clicks menu items and things in the world (hover moves the focus) wherever the genre uses it. On-screen prompts follow the input used last: PlayStation glyphs for the controller (with a Settings option to show Xbox glyphs, A B X Y, instead), keys and mouse buttons for keyboard and mouse.\n\nDo not use overly dense, web-style data screens.\n\nTouch-only devices: no touch controls; show \"Controller or keyboard required\" and the settings button. Let the attract mode run.\n\n## Done\nNo TODOs, placeholders, or stubbed features. The demo is complete.\n\n## Source Information\nCRITICAL: Put Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback in your chat reply and an in-game About/Credits screen. Write \"unknown\" for anything you can't confirm.\n- Date: 2026-11-04 22:13:56\n- Source: the work it's based on\n- Plan: the file name of the plan you were given to build from, or none\n- Genre and Perspective: genre and camera perspective used\n- Tech: stack, libraries/engines, with versions if applicable\n- Art Direction: style used\n- Animation: system used\n- Audio: music, sound effects and voice used\n- Online: network features used, or none\n- Testing: testing parameters allowed\n- Research: research done, or none\n- Environment: Codex CLI (headless); Linux\n- Model: OpenAI, gpt-6.1-terra, reasoning effort max\n- Usage: write \"added on import\". You can't see your own cost, so don't estimate it: the runner records the real cost, tokens and time, and the agent that imports the game into AI Hub puts them on your About/Credits screen.\n\nExit interview: before you finish, also save these answers as exit-interview.json in this folder's root, beside the game's .html: one JSON object in exactly the shape below, every value filled in (\"unknown\" for anything you can't confirm). Tools read it (the game's run record and the AI Hub catalogue), so write plain text, and check that the file parses as JSON.\n{\n  \"sourceInformation\": {\"date\": \"\", \"source\": \"\", \"plan\": \"\", \"genre\": \"\", \"perspective\": \"\", \"tech\": \"\", \"artDirection\": \"\", \"animation\": \"\", \"audio\": \"\", \"online\": \"\", \"testing\": \"\", \"research\": \"\", \"environment\": \"\", \"model\": \"\", \"usage\": \"added on import\"},\n  \"testingFeedback\": [\"your answer to each Testing Feedback question, in order\"],\n  \"engineFeedback\": [\"your answer to each Engine Feedback question, in order\"],\n  \"promptFeedback\": [\"your answer to each Prompt Feedback question, in order\"],\n  \"aiHub\": {\n    \"name\": \"the game's title, as on its title screen\",\n    \"tagline\": \"a few words to go under the title\",\n    \"description\": \"one or two sentences for the catalogue\",\n    \"type\": \"Game, Tech demo or Tool\",\n    \"genre\": \"one of Action, Adventure, Fighting, Flight, Horror, Kids & Learning, Life Sim, Platformer, Puzzle, Racing, RPG, Shooter, Simulation, Sports, Stealth, Strategy\",\n    \"source\": \"the work it's based on, e.g. Moby-Dick\",\n    \"series\": \"its franchise, e.g. Star Fox, or empty\",\n    \"players\": \"how many can play: 1, 1–2 or 1–4\",\n    \"controls\": \"the controls, in one line\",\n    \"tags\": [\"3 to 6 lowercase tags, e.g. 2d, 3d, arcade, story, co-op, versus, first-person, third-person, top-down, side-scrolling, pixel art, low-poly, retro, sci-fi, fantasy, comedy, vehicles, boss fights, exploration\"]\n  }\n}\nThe catalogue's model, effort, CLI, date and usage come from the run's record after you finish, so they aren't asked here.\n\nTesting Feedback\n\n- How many issues did testing catch?\n- How many would be considered critical issues / game breaking?\n- What was the most helpful test you ran?\n- What was the least helpful test you ran?\n\nEngine Feedback\n\n- What did you like most about the engine?\n- Did you get stuck or guess wrong?\n- What was the most important thing you had to build yourself?\n- What was the hardest part about using the engine?\n- What did you change in the engine, and why? (none if nothing)\n- If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be?\n\nPrompt Feedback\n\n- What did you like most about this prompt?\n- What was confusing?\n- What was the hardest thing to do?\n- What would you change in this prompt?\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
