{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_670","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"D='Wee Bit of Zen-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221356'; apply_patch <<'PATCH'\n*** Begin Patch\n*** Update File: Wee Bit of Zen-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221356/src/game.js\n@@\n-function screen(name) { state.screen = name; state.idle = 0; render(); }\n+function screen(name) { if (state.screen \"'!== name) app.scrollTop = 0; state.screen = name; state.idle = 0; render(); }\n*** Update File: Wee Bit of Zen-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221356/tests/run.py\n@@\n-    page.evaluate(\"__ZEN.action('\"'slots'); __ZEN.action('slot', '0')\\\")\n+    page.evaluate(\\\"__ZEN.action('slots')\\\")\n+    check('profile sections stack vertically', page.eval_on_selector('.page--slots .main-wrap', \\\"element => getComputedStyle(element).flexDirection === 'column'\\\"))\n+    page.evaluate(\\\"__ZEN.action('slot', '0')\\\")\n+    check('outfit swatches have distinct colors', page.evaluate(\\\"new Set([...document.querySelectorAll('.swatch')].map(element => getComputedStyle(element).backgroundColor)).size > 1\\\"))\n@@\n def smoke(browser, label, context_options=None):\n@@\n         context.close()\n \n \n+def compact_navigation(browser):\n+    context = browser.new_context(viewport={'width': 375, 'height': 667})\n+    page = context.new_page()\n+    try:\n+        page.goto(URL, wait_until='load')\n+        page.evaluate(\\\"__ZEN.action('slots')\\\")\n+        page.eval_on_selector('#app', 'element => element.scrollTop = element.scrollHeight')\n+        check('compact profile list scrolls', page.eval_on_selector('#app', 'element => element.scrollTop > 0'))\n+        page.evaluate(\\\"__ZEN.action('slot', '0')\\\")\n+        check('new screen starts at top', page.eval_on_selector('#app', 'element => element.scrollTop === 0'))\n+        page.eval_on_selector('#app', 'element => element.scrollTop = element.scrollHeight')\n+        old_scroll = page.eval_on_selector('#app', 'element => element.scrollTop')\n+        page.evaluate(\\\"__ZEN.action('outfit', '1')\\\")\n+        check('editing a screen keeps its scroll position', old_scroll > 0 and page.eval_on_selector('#app', 'element => element.scrollTop') == old_scroll)\n+    except Exception as error:\n+        check('compact navigation ran', False, str(error).splitlines()[0])\n+    finally:\n+        context.close()\n+\n+\n def main():\n@@\n         for engine in ['firefox', 'webkit']:\n             browser = getattr(playwright, engine).launch(headless=True)\n             smoke(browser, engine)\n             if engine == 'webkit':\n+                compact_navigation(browser)\n                 smoke(browser, 'iPhone WebKit', playwright.devices['iPhone 13'])\n*** Update File: exit-interview.json\n@@\n-    \\\"tech\\\": \\\"HTML5 Canvas, JavaScript, my-3D2dge handoff, Mocap, AI Hub client\\\",\n+    \\\"tech\\\": \\\"HTML5 Canvas, JavaScript, my-3D2dge 0.89.0, Mocap clips, AI Hub client\\\",\n@@\n-    \\\"testing\\\": \\\"Headless scripted playthrough and browser/device testing\\\",\n+    \\\"testing\\\": \\\"Scripted full-story and activity playthrough, 1–4 player and host-leave Hub conformance, synthetic gamepads, and Chromium, Firefox, WebKit and viewport checks\\\",\n@@\n-  \\\"testingFeedback\\\": [\\\"unknown\\\", \\\"unknown\\\", \\\"unknown\\\", \\\"unknown\\\"],\n-  \\\"engineFeedback\\\": [\\\"The complete engine handoff provides a useful fixed-step game loop.\\\", \\\"unknown\\\", \\\"The game-specific activities, UI and island presentation.\\\", \\\"Combining the engine loop with the game's varied activities and session protocol.\\\", \\\"None.\\\", \\\"More small end-to-end examples combining fixed-step play, animation and the Hub.\\\"],\n-  \\\"promptFeedback\\\": [\\\"The distinctive source, complete plan and clear handoff requirements.\\\", \\\"unknown\\\", \\\"Building and validating the varied activity and multiplayer flows.\\\", \\\"Include an explicit priority order for scope when a detailed plan exceeds one development session.\\\"],\n+  \\\"testingFeedback\\\": [\\\"Eight issues across Hub input, responsive layouts, indicators, colors and navigation; inspection also found one misleading class-score fallback.\\\", \\\"One mode-blocking issue: the Hub harness could not submit Ready with Enter before the keyboard fix.\\\", \\\"The Hub conformance test across one to four clients and host departure; the scripted full-story playthrough was also valuable.\\\", \\\"The isolated title-screen smoke check: it confirmed startup but could not exercise the gameplay and multiplayer flows.\\\"],\n+  \\\"engineFeedback\\\": [\\\"The complete handoff and fixed-step loop made the game logic straightforward to advance and test.\\\", \\\"Yes. I initially missed how the Hub harness sends Enter to answer the Ready prompt.\\\", \\\"The twelve activity rules, island presentation, progression and local class scoring.\\\", \\\"Combining fixed-step activity simulation, motion clips and the multiplayer session lifecycle.\\\", \\\"None; I built the game and integration around the supplied engine.\\\", \\\"Include a small end-to-end example combining fixed-step play, animation and the Hub.\\\"],\n+  \\\"promptFeedback\\\": [\\\"The distinctive source, detailed plan and clear handoff requirements.\\\", \\\"The plan's breadth made the intended priority order unclear if implementation time was limited.\\\", \\\"Building and validating the varied activity, story and multiplayer flows together.\\\", \\\"Include an explicit priority order for a detailed plan that may exceed one development session.\\\"],\n*** Update File: PROGRESS.md\n@@\n-- [ ] Exercise the game and inspect responsive, cross-browser screenshots; finalize the interview.\n+- [x] Run the scripted game, multiplayer, and browser checks; fix issues found.\n+- [ ] Complete final cross-browser and viewport checks and handoff.\n@@\n-- The first full test run exposed one Hub integration issue: pressing Enter without button focus failed to answer Ready. The keyboard handler now answers explicitly; rerun the suite and inspect responsive screenshots.\n+- The full suite previously passed 181 checks after fixing Enter-to-Ready. Visual checks caught overlapping layout, swatch and scrolling defects; final verification remains after those changes.\n*** End Patch\nPATCH\nnode \\\"\"'$D/build.mjs\"\n'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
