\n  \"engineFeedback\": [\"The complete handoff and fixed-step loop made the game logic straightforward to advance and test.\", \"Yes. I initially missed how the Hub harness sends Enter to answer the Ready prompt.\", \"The twelve activity rules, island presentation, progression and local class scoring.\", \"Combining fixed-step activity simulation, motion clips and the multiplayer session lifecycle.\", \"None; I built the game and integration around the supplied engine.\", \"Include a small end-to-end example combining fixed-step play, animation and the Hub.\"],\n  \"promptFeedback\": [\"The distinctive source, detailed plan and clear handoff requirements.\", \"The plan's breadth made the intended priority order unclear if implementation time was limited.\", \"Building and validating the varied activity, story and multiplayer flows together.\", \"Include an explicit priority order for a detailed plan that may exceed one development session.\"],\n  \"aiHub\": {\n    \"name\": \"Wee Bit of Zen\",\n    \"tagline\": \"Find your balance. Lose it cheerfully.\",\n    \"description\": \"Visit a friendly island retreat and find your balance across gentle, playful exercises. Bring friends for a local or online class.\",\n    \"type\": \"Game\",\n    \"genre\": \"Sports\",\n    \"source\": \"Wii Fit\",\n    \"series\": \"Wii Fit\",\n    \"players\": \"1–4\",\n    \"controls\": \"Left stick/WASD to lean; R2/Space to breathe; Enter or Cross to select; Escape or Options to pause.\",\n    \"tags\": [\"2d\", \"sports\", \"simulation\", \"comedy\", \"story\", \"versus\"]\n  }\n}\n\n--- Progress ---\n# Progress\n\n## Handoff\n- Game title: Wee Bit of Zen\n- Deliverable basename: `Wee Bit of Zen-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221356`\n- Build a complete, single-file game from `PLAN.md` and follow `TASK.md` for the handoff.\n\n## Status\n- [x] Read the task and begin extracting the game design.\n- [x] Fetch the required engine, mocap clips, and AI Hub client and harness.\n- [x] Integrate the fixed-step engine and load the AI Hub client.\n- [x] Implement the island, 12 activities, story, saves, settings, and initial class mode.\n- [x] Produce the first self-contained HTML and a provisional structured exit interview.\n- [x] Finish multiplayer scoring, the three-event AI Hub session, and motion integration.\n- [x] Run the scripted game, multiplayer, and browser checks; fix issues found.\n- [ ] Complete final cross-browser and viewport checks and handoff.\n\n## Notes\n- Keep all project work inside this run's workspace; do not inspect sibling runs.\n- Use Playwright's WebKit as the available approximation of iOS Safari.\n- The original handoff, motion sources, and hub client are in the development folder; `vendor/fitclips.js` is the generated local clip set.\n- Build with `node 'Wee Bit of Zen-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221356/build.mjs'`; this also copies the standalone build into the Hub harness.\n- A local preview is running at `http://127.0.0.1:32893/` in exec session `68330`; stop only that session when finished.\n- The full suite previously passed 181 checks after fixing Enter-to-Ready. Visual checks caught overlapping layout, swatch and scrolling defects; final verification remains after those changes.\n- `tests/run.py` starts its own localhost server and exercises a scripted story, all activities, multiplayer, Hub conformance, audio, accessibility settings, and browser smoke tests.\n\n--- Task handoff requirements ---\n92:## Source Information\n93:CRITICAL: Put Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback in your chat reply and an in-game About/Credits screen. Write \"unknown\" for anything you can't confirm.\n94-- Date: 2026-11-04 22:13:56\n95-- Source: the work it's based on\n96-- Plan: the file name of the plan you were given to build from, or none\n97-- Genre and Perspective: genre and camera perspective used\n98-- Tech: stack, libraries/engines, with versions if applicable\n99-- Art Direction: style used\n100-- Animation: system used\n101-- Audio: music, sound effects and voice used\n102-- Online: network features used, or none\n103-- Testing: testing parameters allowed\n104-- Research: research done, or none\n105-- Environment: Codex CLI (headless); Linux\n106-- Model: OpenAI, gpt-6.1-terra, reasoning effort max\n107-- Usage: write \"added on import\". You can't see your own cost, so don't estimate it: the runner records the real cost, tokens and time, and the agent that imports the game into AI Hub puts them on your About/Credits screen.\n108-\n109:Exit interview: before you finish, also save these answers as exit-interview.json in this folder's root, beside the game's .html: one JSON object in exactly the shape below, every value filled in (\"unknown\" for anything you can't confirm). Tools read it (the game's run record and the AI Hub catalogue), so write plain text, and check that the file parses as JSON.\n110-{\n111-  \"sourceInformation\": {\"date\": \"\", \"source\": \"\", \"plan\": \"\", \"genre\": \"\", \"perspective\": \"\", \"tech\": \"\", \"artDirection\": \"\", \"animation\": \"\", \"audio\": \"\", \"online\": \"\", \"testing\": \"\", \"research\": \"\", \"environment\": \"\", \"model\": \"\", \"usage\": \"added on import\"},\n112:  \"testingFeedback\": [\"your answer to each Testing Feedback question, in order\"],\n113-  \"engineFeedback\": [\"your answer to each Engine Feedback question, in order\"],\n114-  \"promptFeedback\": [\"your answer to each Prompt Feedback question, in order\"],\n115-  \"aiHub\": {\n116-    \"name\": \"the game's title, as on its title screen\",\n117-    \"tagline\": \"a few words to go under the title\",\n118-    \"description\": \"one or two sentences for the catalogue\",\n119-    \"type\": \"Game, Tech demo or Tool\",\n120-    \"genre\": \"one of Action, Adventure, Fighting, Flight, Horror, Kids & Learning, Life Sim, Platformer, Puzzle, Racing, RPG, Shooter, Simulation, Sports, Stealth, Strategy\",\n121-    \"source\": \"the work it's based on, e.g. Moby-Dick\",\n122-    \"series\": \"its franchise, e.g. Star Fox, or empty\",\n123-    \"players\": \"how many can play: 1, 1–2 or 1–4\",\n124-    \"controls\": \"the controls, in one line\",\n125-    \"tags\": [\"3 to 6 lowercase tags, e.g. 2d, 3d, arcade, story, co-op, versus, first-person, third-person, top-down, side-scrolling, pixel art, low-poly, retro, sci-fi, fantasy, comedy, vehicles, boss fights, exploration\"]\n126-  }\n127-}\n128-The catalogue's model, effort, CLI, date and usage come from the run's record after you finish, so they aren't asked here.\n129-\n130:Testing Feedback\n131-\n132-- How many issues did testing catch?\n133-- How many would be considered critical issues / game breaking?\n134-- What was the most helpful test you ran?\n135-- What was the least helpful test you ran?\n136-\n137-Engine Feedback\n138-\n139-- What did you like most about the engine?\n140-- Did you get stuck or guess wrong?\n141-- What was the most important thing you had to build yourself?\n142-- What was the hardest part about using the engine?\n143-- What did you change in the engine, and why? (none if nothing)\n144-- If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be?\n145-\n146-Prompt Feedback\n147-\n148-- What did you like most about this prompt?\n149-- What was confusing?\n150-- What was the hardest thing to do?\n151-- What would you change in this prompt?\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
