{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_701","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '92,107p;130,160p' TASK.md && printf '\\\\n--- exit interview ---\\\\n' && cat exit-interview.json && printf '\\\\n--- file anchors ---\\\\n' && rg -n '\\\"testingFeedback\\\"|\\\"engineFeedback\\\"|\\\"promptFeedback\\\"|\\\"sourceInformation\\\"' exit-interview.json && rg -n '\"'^## (Status|Notes)'\"' PROGRESS.md\"","aggregated_output":"## Source Information\nCRITICAL: Put Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback in your chat reply and an in-game About/Credits screen. Write \"unknown\" for anything you can't confirm.\n- Date: 2026-11-04 22:13:56\n- Source: the work it's based on\n- Plan: the file name of the plan you were given to build from, or none\n- Genre and Perspective: genre and camera perspective used\n- Tech: stack, libraries/engines, with versions if applicable\n- Art Direction: style used\n- Animation: system used\n- Audio: music, sound effects and voice used\n- Online: network features used, or none\n- Testing: testing parameters allowed\n- Research: research done, or none\n- Environment: Codex CLI (headless); Linux\n- Model: OpenAI, gpt-6.1-terra, reasoning effort max\n- Usage: write \"added on import\". You can't see your own cost, so don't estimate it: the runner records the real cost, tokens and time, and the agent that imports the game into AI Hub puts them on your About/Credits screen.\nTesting Feedback\n\n- How many issues did testing catch?\n- How many would be considered critical issues / game breaking?\n- What was the most helpful test you ran?\n- What was the least helpful test you ran?\n\nEngine Feedback\n\n- What did you like most about the engine?\n- Did you get stuck or guess wrong?\n- What was the most important thing you had to build yourself?\n- What was the hardest part about using the engine?\n- What did you change in the engine, and why? (none if nothing)\n- If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be?\n\nPrompt Feedback\n\n- What did you like most about this prompt?\n- What was confusing?\n- What was the hardest thing to do?\n- What would you change in this prompt?\n\n--- exit interview ---\n{\n  \"sourceInformation\": {\n    \"date\": \"2026-11-04 22:13:56\",\n    \"source\": \"Wii Fit\",\n    \"plan\": \"PLAN.md\",\n    \"genre\": \"Fitness party and life simulation\",\n    \"perspective\": \"2D, third-person island and exercise views\",\n    \"tech\": \"HTML5 Canvas, JavaScript, my-3D2dge 0.89.0, Mocap clips, AI Hub client\",\n    \"artDirection\": \"Original soft, cheerful vector island, studio and characters\",\n    \"animation\": \"Procedural character animation and my-3D2dge Mocap clip set\",\n    \"audio\": \"Web Audio procedural music, effects and character voices; default music 10%\",\n    \"online\": \"AI Hub ghost sessions, 1–4 players\",\n    \"testing\": \"Scripted full-story and activity playthrough, 1–4 player and host-leave Hub conformance, synthetic gamepads, and Chromium, Firefox, WebKit and viewport checks\",\n    \"research\": \"Read the supplied plan, engine handoff and AI Hub protocol\",\n    \"environment\": \"Codex CLI (headless); Linux\",\n    \"model\": \"OpenAI, gpt-6.1-terra, reasoning effort max\",\n    \"usage\": \"added on import\"\n  },\n  \"testingFeedback\": [\"Eight issues across Hub input, responsive layouts, indicators, colors and navigation; inspection also found one misleading class-score fallback.\", \"One mode-blocking issue: the Hub harness could not submit Ready with Enter before the keyboard fix.\", \"The Hub conformance test across one to four clients and host departure; the scripted full-story playthrough was also valuable.\", \"The isolated title-screen smoke check: it confirmed startup but could not exercise the gameplay and multiplayer flows.\"],\n  \"engineFeedback\": [\"The complete handoff and fixed-step loop made the game logic straightforward to advance and test.\", \"Yes. I initially missed how the Hub harness sends Enter to answer the Ready prompt.\", \"The twelve activity rules, island presentation, progression and local class scoring.\", \"Combining fixed-step activity simulation, motion clips and the multiplayer session lifecycle.\", \"None; I built the game and integration around the supplied engine.\", \"Include a small end-to-end example combining fixed-step play, animation and the Hub.\"],\n  \"promptFeedback\": [\"The distinctive source, detailed plan and clear handoff requirements.\", \"The plan's breadth made the intended priority order unclear if implementation time was limited.\", \"Building and validating the varied activity, story and multiplayer flows together.\", \"Include an explicit priority order for a detailed plan that may exceed one development session.\"],\n  \"aiHub\": {\n    \"name\": \"Wee Bit of Zen\",\n    \"tagline\": \"Find your balance. Lose it cheerfully.\",\n    \"description\": \"Visit a friendly island retreat and find your balance across gentle, playful exercises. Bring friends for a local or online class.\",\n    \"type\": \"Game\",\n    \"genre\": \"Sports\",\n    \"source\": \"Wii Fit\",\n    \"series\": \"Wii Fit\",\n    \"players\": \"1–4\",\n    \"controls\": \"Left stick/WASD to lean; R2/Space to breathe; Enter or Cross to select; Escape or Options to pause.\",\n    \"tags\": [\"2d\", \"sports\", \"simulation\", \"comedy\", \"story\", \"versus\"]\n  }\n}\n\n--- file anchors ---\n2:  \"sourceInformation\": {\n19:  \"testingFeedback\": [\"Eight issues across Hub input, responsive layouts, indicators, colors and navigation; inspection also found one misleading class-score fallback.\", \"One mode-blocking issue: the Hub harness could not submit Ready with Enter before the keyboard fix.\", \"The Hub conformance test across one to four clients and host departure; the scripted full-story playthrough was also valuable.\", \"The isolated title-screen smoke check: it confirmed startup but could not exercise the gameplay and multiplayer flows.\"],\n20:  \"engineFeedback\": [\"The complete handoff and fixed-step loop made the game logic straightforward to advance and test.\", \"Yes. I initially missed how the Hub harness sends Enter to answer the Ready prompt.\", \"The twelve activity rules, island presentation, progression and local class scoring.\", \"Combining fixed-step activity simulation, motion clips and the multiplayer session lifecycle.\", \"None; I built the game and integration around the supplied engine.\", \"Include a small end-to-end example combining fixed-step play, animation and the Hub.\"],\n21:  \"promptFeedback\": [\"The distinctive source, detailed plan and clear handoff requirements.\", \"The plan's breadth made the intended priority order unclear if implementation time was limited.\", \"Building and validating the varied activity, story and multiplayer flows together.\", \"Include an explicit priority order for a detailed plan that may exceed one development session.\"],\n8:## Status\n18:## Notes\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_702","type":"agent_message","text":"Built **Wee Bit of Zen**, with 12 activities, a five-day story, local classes, and AI Hub ghost sessions.\n\n- Open `Wee Bit of Zen-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221356.html:1` to play with a keyboard or controller.\n- The matching development folder contains the source, build script, and tests. Progress is recorded in `PROGRESS.md:1`; the structured interview is in `exit-interview.json:1`.\n- Verification: **189 checks passed** and 24 viewport/browser captures were clean. WebKit approximates iOS Safari; real iOS and physical controllers were not tested.\n\n**Source Information**\n- Source: Wii Fit; plan: `PLAN.md:1`; date: 2026-11-04 22:13:56. Genre: fitness party/life simulation; perspective: 2D third-person.\n- Stack: HTML5 Canvas, JavaScript, `my-3D2dge` 0.89.0, Mocap clips, and AI Hub. Art is original vector illustration; animation combines procedural motion and Mocap clips.\n- Audio uses procedural Web Audio music, effects, and character voices; music defaults to 10%. Online play uses AI Hub ghost sessions for 1–4 players.\n- Testing covered scripted story and activities, multiplayer and host departure, synthetic gamepads, Chromium, Firefox, WebKit, and viewport checks. Research used the supplied plan, engine handoff, and AI Hub protocol.\n- Environment: Codex CLI (headless), Linux. Model: OpenAI `gpt-6.1-terra`, reasoning effort max. Usage: added on import.\n\n**Testing Feedback**\n- Testing caught eight issues, including one mode-blocking Hub keyboard issue; inspection also found an incorrect class-score fallback.\n- Most helpful: Hub conformance across 1–4 clients and host departure. Least helpful: the title-only smoke test, which could not exercise gameplay.\n\n**Engine Feedback**\n- The handoff and fixed-step loop made gameplay straightforward to test. I initially missed how the Hub harness submits Ready with Enter.\n- I built the activity rules, island presentation, progression, and class scoring; combining simulation, motion clips, and the multiplayer lifecycle was hardest.\n- Engine changes: none. An end-to-end example combining fixed-step play, animation, and Hub integration would help.\n\n**Prompt Feedback**\n- The source, detailed plan, and handoff requirements were useful; the plan’s breadth made priorities unclear under time constraints.\n- The hardest part was building and validating the activity, story, and multiplayer flows together. An explicit priority order would improve the prompt."}}
